{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EfxvwWqA49g2HbcizhV9Fi","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * VariablesTab - Define intermediate entity selections\n     3→ */\n     4→\n     5→import React, { useState } from \"react\";\n     6→import PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\n     7→import VariableSelectionEditor from \"../../shared/VariableSelectionEditor\";\n     8→import \"./VariablesTab.css\";\n     9→\n    10→/**\n    11→ * Safely display a value that should be a string.\n    12→ * If it's an object, log a warning and return a fallback.\n    13→ */\n    14→function safeDisplay(value, fallback = \"?\", label = \"value\") {\n    15→  if (value === null || value === undefined) return fallback;\n    16→  if (typeof value === \"object\") {\n    17→    console.warn(`[VariablesTab] Expected string for ${label} but got object:`, value);\n    18→    return `[object]`;\n    19→  }\n    20→  return String(value);\n    21→}\n    22→\n    23→// ============================================================================\n    24→// VariableCard - Individual variable editor card\n    25→// ============================================================================\n    26→\n    27→function VariableCard({ name, config, onChange, onRemove, schema, availableRefs = [] }) {\n    28→  const [expanded, setExpanded] = useState(false);\n    29→  const [hovering, setHovering] = useState(false);\n    30→\n    31→  // Handle the nested select structure: { select: { from, kind, pickStrategy, ... }, required }\n    32→  const selectConfig = config.select || {};\n    33→  const isRequired = config.required || false;\n    34→\n    35→  const updateRequired = (value) => {\n    36→    onChange({ ...config, required: value });\n    37→  };\n    38→\n    39→  // Display info\n    40→  const displayMode =\n    41→    selectConfig.from && typeof selectConfig.from === \"object\"\n    42→      ? \"Related entities\"\n    43→      : selectConfig.kind || \"Not configured\";\n    44→  const displayStrategy = safeDisplay(selectConfig.pickStrategy, \"Not set\", \"pickStrategy\");\n    45→  const filterCount = (selectConfig.filters || []).length;\n    46→\n    47→  return (\n    48→    <div className=\"item-card\">\n    49→      <div\n    50→        className={`item-card-header ${hovering ? \"item-card-header-hover\" : \"\"}`}\n    51→        onClick={() => setExpanded(!expanded)}\n    52→        onMouseEnter={() => setHovering(true)}\n    53→        onMouseLeave={() => setHovering(false)}\n    54→        role=\"button\"\n    55→        tabIndex={0}\n    56→        onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }}\n    57→      >\n    58→        <div className=\"item-card-icon item-card-icon-variable\">📦</div>\n    59→        <div className=\"item-card-info\">\n    60→          <div className=\"item-card-title\">\n    61→            <span className=\"variable-ref\">{name}</span>\n    62→            {isRequired && (\n    63→              <span className=\"badge badge-warning ml-md text-xs\">\n    64→                Required\n    65→              </span>\n    66→            )}\n    67→          </div>\n    68→          <div className=\"item-card-subtitle\">\n    69→            {displayMode} • {displayStrategy}\n    70→            {filterCount > 0 && (\n    71→              <span className=\"ml-xs\">\n    72→                • {filterCount} filter{filterCount > 1 ? \"s\" : \"\"}\n    73→              </span>\n    74→            )}\n    75→          </div>\n    76→        </div>\n    77→        <div className=\"item-card-actions\">\n    78→          <button className=\"btn-icon\">{expanded ? \"▲\" : \"▼\"}</button>\n    79→          <button\n    80→            className=\"btn-icon btn-icon-danger\"\n    81→            onClick={(e) => {\n    82→              e.stopPropagation();\n    83→              onRemove();\n    84→            }}\n    85→          >\n    86→            ×\n    87→          </button>\n    88→        </div>\n    89→      </div>\n    90→\n    91→      {expanded && (\n    92→        <div className=\"item-card-body\">\n    93→          {/* Required checkbox */}\n    94→          <div className=\"mb-xl\">\n    95→            <label className=\"vt-required-checkbox\">\n    96→              <input\n    97→                type=\"checkbox\"\n    98→                checked={isRequired}\n    99→                onChange={(e) => updateRequired(e.target.checked)}\n   100→              />\n   101→              <span className=\"label mb-0\">\n   102→                Required\n   103→              </span>\n   104→              <span className=\"text-muted text-xs\">\n   105→                (Template won&apos;t run unless this variable resolves)\n   106→              </span>\n   107→            </label>\n   108→          </div>\n   109→\n   110→\n   111→          <VariableSelectionEditor\n   112→            value={selectConfig}\n   113→            onChange={(updated) => onChange({ ...config, select: updated })}\n   114→            schema={schema}\n   115→            availableRefs={availableRefs}\n   116→          />\n   117→        </div>\n   118→      )}\n   119→    </div>\n   120→  );\n   121→}\n   122→\n   123→VariableCard.propTypes = {\n   124→  name: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\n   125→  config: PropTypes.object.isRequired,\n   126→  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   127→  onRemove: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   128→  schema: PropTypes.object,\n   129→  availableRefs: PropTypes.array,\n   130→};\n   131→\n   132→// ============================================================================\n   133→// VariablesTab - Main tab component\n   134→// ============================================================================\n   135→\n   136→/**\n   137→ * @param {Object} props\n   138→ * @param {Object} props.generator - The generator being edited\n   139→ * @param {Function} props.onChange - Callback when generator changes\n   140→ * @param {Object} props.schema - Domain schema\n   141→ */\n   142→export function VariablesTab({ generator, onChange, schema }) {\n   143→  const variables = generator.variables || {};\n   144→  const [newVarName, setNewVarName] = useState(\"\");\n   145→  const [showAddForm, setShowAddForm] = useState(false);\n   146→\n   147→  // Build available refs for relationship queries (target + other vars + creation refs)\n   148→  const buildAvailableRefs = (excludeVar) => {\n   149→    const refs = [\"$target\"];\n   150→    Object.keys(variables).forEach((v) => {\n   151→      if (v !== excludeVar) refs.push(v);\n   152→    });\n   153→    (generator.creation || []).forEach((c) => {\n   154→      if (c.entityRef && !refs.includes(c.entityRef)) refs.push(c.entityRef);\n   155→    });\n   156→    return refs;\n   157→  };\n   158→\n   159→  const handleAddVariable = () => {\n   160→    if (!newVarName.trim()) return;\n   161→    // Ensure the name starts with $\n   162→    const name = newVarName.startsWith(\"$\") ? newVarName : `$${newVarName}`;\n   163→    // Create with empty required fields - validation will flag them\n   164→    onChange({\n   165→      ...generator,\n   166→      variables: {\n   167→        ...variables,\n   168→        [name]: { select: { from: \"graph\", kind: \"\", pickStrategy: \"\" } },\n   169→      },\n   170→    });\n   171→    setNewVarName(\"\");\n   172→    setShowAddForm(false);\n   173→  };\n   174→\n   175→  const varEntries = Object.entries(variables);\n   176→\n   177→  return (\n   178→    <div>\n   179→      <div className=\"section\">\n   180→        <div className=\"section-title\">Variables</div>\n   181→\n   182→        <div className=\"info-box\">\n   183→          <div className=\"info-box-title\">What are variables?</div>\n   184→          <div className=\"info-box-text\">\n   185→            Variables let you select additional entities from the graph to use in creation and\n   186→            relationships. For example, you might select a{\" \"}\n   187→            <code className=\"inline-code\">$faction</code> to make a new NPC a member of, or an{\" \"}\n   188→            <code className=\"inline-code\">$ability</code> for them to practice. Variables are\n   189→            selected after <code className=\"inline-code\">$target</code> is chosen.\n   190→          </div>\n   191→        </div>\n   192→\n   193→        {varEntries.length === 0 && !showAddForm ? (\n   194→          <div className=\"empty-state\">\n   195→            <div className=\"empty-state-icon\">📦</div>\n   196→            <div className=\"empty-state-title\">No variables defined</div>\n   197→            <div className=\"empty-state-desc\">\n   198→              Add variables to select additional entities for use in creation and relationships.\n   199→            </div>\n   200→          </div>\n   201→        ) : (\n   202→          varEntries.map(([name, config]) => (\n   203→            <VariableCard\n   204→              key={name}\n   205→              name={name}\n   206→              config={config}\n   207→              onChange={(updated) =>\n   208→                onChange({ ...generator, variables: { ...variables, [name]: updated } })\n   209→              }\n   210→              onRemove={() => {\n   211→                const newVars = { ...variables };\n   212→                delete newVars[name];\n   213→                onChange({ ...generator, variables: newVars });\n   214→              }}\n   215→              schema={schema}\n   216→              availableRefs={buildAvailableRefs(name)}\n   217→            />\n   218→          ))\n   219→        )}\n   220→\n   221→        {showAddForm ? (\n   222→          <div className=\"item-card add-form\">\n   223→            <div className=\"add-form-fields\">\n   224→              <div className=\"flex-1\">\n   225→                <label htmlFor=\"variable-name\" className=\"label\">Variable Name</label>\n   226→                <input id=\"variable-name\"\n   227→                  type=\"text\"\n   228→                  value={newVarName}\n   229→                  onChange={(e) => setNewVarName(e.target.value.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9_$]/g, \"\"))}\n   230→                  className=\"input\"\n   231→                  placeholder=\"$myVariable\"\n   232→                  // eslint-disable-next-line jsx-a11y/no-autofocus\n   233→                  autoFocus\n   234→                />\n   235→              </div>\n   236→              <button\n   237→                className=\"btn btn-primary\"\n   238→                onClick={handleAddVariable}\n   239→                disabled={!newVarName.trim()}\n   240→              >\n   241→                Add\n   242→              </button>\n   243→              <button\n   244→                className=\"btn btn-secondary\"\n   245→                onClick={() => {\n   246→                  setShowAddForm(false);\n   247→                  setNewVarName(\"\");\n   248→                }}\n   249→              >\n   250→                Cancel\n   251→              </button>\n   252→            </div>\n   253→          </div>\n   254→        ) : (\n   255→          <button className=\"btn-add\" onClick={() => setShowAddForm(true)}>\n   256→            + Add Variable\n   257→          </button>\n   258→        )}\n   259→      </div>\n   260→    </div>\n   261→  );\n   262→}\n   263→\n   264→VariablesTab.propTypes = {\n   265→  generator: PropTypes.object.isRequired,\n   266→  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   267→  schema: PropTypes.object,\n   268→};\n   269→\n   270→export default VariablesTab;\n   271→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20d8db96-9940-458a-8101-1376b9d882e0","uuid":"f91a76bf-913d-40bb-b32c-cf45b2bf9754","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/apps/coherence-engine/webui/src/components/generators/tabs/VariablesTab.jsx","content":"/**\n * VariablesTab - Define intermediate entity selections\n */\n\nimport React, { useState } from \"react\";\nimport PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\nimport VariableSelectionEditor from \"../../shared/VariableSelectionEditor\";\nimport \"./VariablesTab.css\";\n\n/**\n * Safely display a value that should be a string.\n * If it's an object, log a warning and return a fallback.\n */\nfunction safeDisplay(value, fallback = \"?\", label = \"value\") {\n  if (value === null || value === undefined) return fallback;\n  if (typeof value === \"object\") {\n    console.warn(`[VariablesTab] Expected string for ${label} but got object:`, value);\n    return `[object]`;\n  }\n  return String(value);\n}\n\n// ============================================================================\n// VariableCard - Individual variable editor card\n// ============================================================================\n\nfunction VariableCard({ name, config, onChange, onRemove, schema, availableRefs = [] }) {\n  const [expanded, setExpanded] = useState(false);\n  const [hovering, setHovering] = useState(false);\n\n  // Handle the nested select structure: { select: { from, kind, pickStrategy, ... }, required }\n  const selectConfig = config.select || {};\n  const isRequired = config.required || false;\n\n  const updateRequired = (value) => {\n    onChange({ ...config, required: value });\n  };\n\n  // Display info\n  const displayMode =\n    selectConfig.from && typeof selectConfig.from === \"object\"\n      ? \"Related entities\"\n      : selectConfig.kind || \"Not configured\";\n  const displayStrategy = safeDisplay(selectConfig.pickStrategy, \"Not set\", \"pickStrategy\");\n  const filterCount = (selectConfig.filters || []).length;\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"item-card\">\n      <div\n        className={`item-card-header ${hovering ? \"item-card-header-hover\" : \"\"}`}\n        onClick={() => setExpanded(!expanded)}\n        onMouseEnter={() => setHovering(true)}\n        onMouseLeave={() => setHovering(false)}\n        role=\"button\"\n        tabIndex={0}\n        onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }}\n      >\n        <div className=\"item-card-icon item-card-icon-variable\">📦</div>\n        <div className=\"item-card-info\">\n          <div className=\"item-card-title\">\n            <span className=\"variable-ref\">{name}</span>\n            {isRequired && (\n              <span className=\"badge badge-warning ml-md text-xs\">\n                Required\n              </span>\n            )}\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"item-card-subtitle\">\n            {displayMode} • {displayStrategy}\n            {filterCount > 0 && (\n              <span className=\"ml-xs\">\n                • {filterCount} filter{filterCount > 1 ? \"s\" : \"\"}\n              </span>\n            )}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\"item-card-actions\">\n          <button className=\"btn-icon\">{expanded ? \"▲\" : \"▼\"}</button>\n          <button\n            className=\"btn-icon btn-icon-danger\"\n            onClick={(e) => {\n              e.stopPropagation();\n              onRemove();\n            }}\n          >\n            ×\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      {expanded && (\n        <div className=\"item-card-body\">\n          {/* Required checkbox */}\n          <div className=\"mb-xl\">\n            <label className=\"vt-required-checkbox\">\n              <input\n                type=\"checkbox\"\n                checked={isRequired}\n                onChange={(e) => updateRequired(e.target.checked)}\n              />\n              <span className=\"label mb-0\">\n                Required\n              </span>\n              <span className=\"text-muted text-xs\">\n                (Template won&apos;t run unless this variable resolves)\n              </span>\n            </label>\n          </div>\n\n\n          <VariableSelectionEditor\n            value={selectConfig}\n            onChange={(updated) => onChange({ ...config, select: updated })}\n            schema={schema}\n            availableRefs={availableRefs}\n          />\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nVariableCard.propTypes = {\n  name: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\n  config: PropTypes.object.isRequired,\n  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n  onRemove: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n  schema: PropTypes.object,\n  availableRefs: PropTypes.array,\n};\n\n// ============================================================================\n// VariablesTab - Main tab component\n// ============================================================================\n\n/**\n * @param {Object} props\n * @param {Object} props.generator - The generator being edited\n * @param {Function} props.onChange - Callback when generator changes\n * @param {Object} props.schema - Domain schema\n */\nexport function VariablesTab({ generator, onChange, schema }) {\n  const variables = generator.variables || {};\n  const [newVarName, setNewVarName] = useState(\"\");\n  const [showAddForm, setShowAddForm] = useState(false);\n\n  // Build available refs for relationship queries (target + other vars + creation refs)\n  const buildAvailableRefs = (excludeVar) => {\n    const refs = [\"$target\"];\n    Object.keys(variables).forEach((v) => {\n      if (v !== excludeVar) refs.push(v);\n    });\n    (generator.creation || []).forEach((c) => {\n      if (c.entityRef && !refs.includes(c.entityRef)) refs.push(c.entityRef);\n    });\n    return refs;\n  };\n\n  const handleAddVariable = () => {\n    if (!newVarName.trim()) return;\n    // Ensure the name starts with $\n    const name = newVarName.startsWith(\"$\") ? newVarName : `$${newVarName}`;\n    // Create with empty required fields - validation will flag them\n    onChange({\n      ...generator,\n      variables: {\n        ...variables,\n        [name]: { select: { from: \"graph\", kind: \"\", pickStrategy: \"\" } },\n      },\n    });\n    setNewVarName(\"\");\n    setShowAddForm(false);\n  };\n\n  const varEntries = Object.entries(variables);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <div className=\"section\">\n        <div className=\"section-title\">Variables</div>\n\n        <div className=\"info-box\">\n          <div className=\"info-box-title\">What are variables?</div>\n          <div className=\"info-box-text\">\n            Variables let you select additional entities from the graph to use in creation and\n            relationships. For example, you might select a{\" \"}\n            <code className=\"inline-code\">$faction</code> to make a new NPC a member of, or an{\" \"}\n            <code className=\"inline-code\">$ability</code> for them to practice. Variables are\n            selected after <code className=\"inline-code\">$target</code> is chosen.\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        {varEntries.length === 0 && !showAddForm ? (\n          <div className=\"empty-state\">\n            <div className=\"empty-state-icon\">📦</div>\n            <div className=\"empty-state-title\">No variables defined</div>\n            <div className=\"empty-state-desc\">\n              Add variables to select additional entities for use in creation and relationships.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        ) : (\n          varEntries.map(([name, config]) => (\n            <VariableCard\n              key={name}\n              name={name}\n              config={config}\n              onChange={(updated) =>\n                onChange({ ...generator, variables: { ...variables, [name]: updated } })\n              }\n              onRemove={() => {\n                const newVars = { ...variables };\n                delete newVars[name];\n                onChange({ ...generator, variables: newVars });\n              }}\n              schema={schema}\n              availableRefs={buildAvailableRefs(name)}\n            />\n          ))\n        )}\n\n        {showAddForm ? (\n          <div className=\"item-card add-form\">\n            <div className=\"add-form-fields\">\n              <div className=\"flex-1\">\n                <label htmlFor=\"variable-name\" className=\"label\">Variable Name</label>\n                <input id=\"variable-name\"\n                  type=\"text\"\n                  value={newVarName}\n                  onChange={(e) => setNewVarName(e.target.value.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9_$]/g, \"\"))}\n                  className=\"input\"\n                  placeholder=\"$myVariable\"\n                  // eslint-disable-next-line jsx-a11y/no-autofocus\n                  autoFocus\n                />\n              </div>\n              <button\n                className=\"btn btn-primary\"\n                onClick={handleAddVariable}\n                disabled={!newVarName.trim()}\n              >\n                Add\n              </button>\n              <button\n                className=\"btn btn-secondary\"\n                onClick={() => {\n                  setShowAddForm(false);\n                  setNewVarName(\"\");\n                }}\n              >\n                Cancel\n              </button>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        ) : (\n          <button className=\"btn-add\" onClick={() => setShowAddForm(true)}>\n            + Add Variable\n          </button>\n        )}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nVariablesTab.propTypes = {\n  generator: PropTypes.object.isRequired,\n  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n  schema: PropTypes.object,\n};\n\nexport default VariablesTab;\n","numLines":271,"startLine":1,"totalLines":271}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Nm9MiL1M6ktLj7BmM8wYrv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me analyze the situation:\n\n**Three CSS files with duplicated tab companion styles:**\n\n1. **`actions/tabs/VariablesTab.css`** — canonical, prefix `avt-`, 3 rules: required-badge, checkbox-label, required-hint\n2. **`systems/tabs/ThresholdTriggerTab.css`** — `ttt-` prefix, identical 3 rules\n3. **`generators/tabs/VariablesTab.css`** — `vt-` prefix, only 1 rule (checkbox equivalent named `vt-required-checkbox`)\n \nLooking at how these styles are actually used in the components, I see the pattern clearly: the actions and systems tabs both use their prefixed CSS classes consistently, but the generators tab takes a different approach—it relies on utility classes for the badge and hint styling while only defining a custom class for the checkbox element.\n\nMy plan is to consolidate these into a single shared CSS file with standardized class names, then update all three components to reference those unified styles and remove the redundant individual CSS files. First, I need to figure out where the project keeps its shared styles.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12864,"cache_read_input_tokens":50979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12864},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20d8db96-9940-458a-8101-1376b9d882e0","uuid":"ec03e051-076c-41dd-9376-d9d9b95c7624"}
