"Update actions/VariablesTab to use shared styles","status":"completed","activeForm":"Updating actions/VariablesTab to use shared styles"},{"content":"Update generators/VariablesTab to use shared styles","status":"completed","activeForm":"Updating generators/VariablesTab to use shared styles"},{"content":"Delete redundant CSS files","status":"completed","activeForm":"Deleting redundant CSS files"},{"content":"Append entry to UNIFICATION_LOG.md","status":"completed","activeForm":"Appending entry to UNIFICATION_LOG.md"},{"content":"Create ESLint guard rule","status":"completed","activeForm":"Creating ESLint guard rule"},{"content":"Create ADR document","status":"in_progress","activeForm":"Creating ADR document"},{"content":"Create pattern doc","status":"pending","activeForm":"Creating pattern doc"},{"content":"Wire ESLint rule into config","status":"completed","activeForm":"Wiring ESLint rule into config"}]}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019mu5EpWwdzwiWCwEUQvLfB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018MRj4dUDeffXJedFPNwJNq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/adr/024-tab-form-css-consolidation.md","content":"<!-- drift-generated -->\n# ADR-024: Tab Form CSS Consolidation\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\nThe coherence-engine has multiple tab components (VariablesTab in actions, VariablesTab in generators, ThresholdTriggerTab in systems) that each maintained their own companion CSS file with per-component prefixed class names (`avt-required-badge`, `ttt-checkbox-label`, `vt-required-checkbox`, etc.). These files were 95% identical — they all defined the same three concerns: a required badge with left margin, a flexbox checkbox label, and a small-text required hint.\n\nEach time a new tab component was added, the pattern was copy-paste-rename from an existing tab's CSS, changing only the prefix. This created three independent files that would drift independently on any styling change.\n\n## Decision\nConsolidate all tab form companion styles into a single shared file at `styles/components/tab-form.css`, imported centrally via `styles/index.css`. Use generic `tab-` prefixed class names (`tab-required-badge`, `tab-checkbox-label`, `tab-required-hint`) instead of per-component prefixes.\n\nTab components in coherence-engine must not import their own local CSS files for form-level styles. All such styles belong in the centralized `styles/components/` directory.\n\n## Consequences\n- **Positive:** Single source of truth for tab form styling. Changes propagate to all tabs automatically.\n- **Positive:** New tab components get form styles for free via the central import — no CSS file needed.\n- **Negative:** If a tab genuinely needs unique form styling, it must either extend `tab-form.css` or add overrides in `compact-overrides.css` rather than creating a local CSS file.\n\n## Enforcement\n- ESLint rule `local/no-tab-companion-css` bans local CSS imports from coherence-engine `tabs/` directories.\n- Pattern doc: `docs/patterns/tab-form-styles.md`\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":464,"cache_read_input_tokens":79187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":464},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20d8db96-9940-458a-8101-1376b9d882e0","uuid":"4c069eae-10b0-4d6b-9099-b473df31c27b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018MRj4dUDeffXJedFPNwJNq","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/adr/024-tab-form-css-consolidation.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20d8db96-9940-458a-8101-1376b9d882e0","uuid":"508c31be-181a-49b7-a99b-8d372063d60d","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/adr/024-tab-form-css-consolidation.md","content":"<!-- drift-generated -->\n# ADR-024: Tab Form CSS Consolidation\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\nThe coherence-engine has multiple tab components (VariablesTab in actions, VariablesTab in generators, ThresholdTriggerTab in systems) that each maintained their own companion CSS file with per-component prefixed class names (`avt-required-badge`, `ttt-checkbox-label`, `vt-required-checkbox`, etc.). These files were 95% identical — they all defined the same three concerns: a required badge with left margin, a flexbox checkbox label, and a small-text required hint.\n\nEach time a new tab component was added, the pattern was copy-paste-rename from an existing tab's CSS, changing only the prefix. This created three independent files that would drift independently on any styling change.\n\n## Decision\nConsolidate all tab form companion styles into a single shared file at `styles/components/tab-form.css`, imported centrally via `styles/index.css`. Use generic `tab-` prefixed class names (`tab-required-badge`, `tab-checkbox-label`, `tab-required-hint`) instead of per-component prefixes.\n\nTab components in coherence-engine must not import their own local CSS files for form-level styles. All such styles belong in the centralized `styles/components/` directory.\n\n## Consequences\n- **Positive:** Single source of truth for tab form styling. Changes propagate to all tabs automatically.\n- **Positive:** New tab components get form styles for free via the central import — no CSS file needed.\n- **Negative:** If a tab genuinely needs unique form styling, it must either extend `tab-form.css` or add overrides in `compact-overrides.css` rather than creating a local CSS file.\n\n## Enforcement\n- ESLint rule `local/no-tab-companion-css` bans local CSS imports from coherence-engine `tabs/` directories.\n- Pattern doc: `docs/patterns/tab-form-styles.md`\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019mu5EpWwdzwiWCwEUQvLfB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DWtiLxM11okUtpeu9JRCcq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/patterns/tab-form-styles.md","content":"<!-- drift-generated -->\n# Tab Form Styles\n\nShared CSS classes for form elements inside coherence-engine tab components (required badges, checkbox labels, hints).\n\n## Location\n\n`apps/coherence-engine/webui/src/styles/components/tab-form.css`\n\nImported centrally via `styles/index.css` — no per-component import needed.\n\n## Available Classes\n\n| Class | Purpose |\n|-------|---------|\n| `tab-required-badge` | Small badge next to a title indicating a required field. Adds left margin and 10px font. |\n| `tab-checkbox-label` | Flexbox label wrapping a checkbox, label text, and hint. Uses `var(--spacing-md)` gap. |\n| `tab-required-hint` | Small 11px hint text explaining what \"required\" means in context. |\n\n## Usage\n\n```jsx\n// In any coherence-engine tab component — NO local CSS import needed\n\n<span className=\"badge badge-warning tab-required-badge\">Required</span>\n\n<label className=\"tab-checkbox-label\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" checked={isRequired} onChange={...} />\n  <span className=\"label mb-0\">Required</span>\n  <span className=\"text-muted tab-required-hint\">\n    (Action won't execute unless this variable resolves)\n  </span>\n</label>\n```\n\n## Adding New Tab Form Styles\n\nIf you need a new shared style for tab forms:\n\n1. Add the class to `styles/components/tab-form.css`\n2. Use the `tab-` prefix for the class name\n3. It's available immediately in all tab components via the central import\n\n**Do not** create a per-component CSS file in the `tabs/` directory. The ESLint rule `local/no-tab-companion-css` will flag this.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":464,"cache_read_input_tokens":79187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":464},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20d8db96-9940-458a-8101-1376b9d882e0","uuid":"953474c3-f12b-471a-9e83-10d895ff2a45"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DWtiLxM11okUtpeu9JRCcq","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/patterns/tab-form-styles.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20d8db96-9940-458a-8101-1376b9d882e0","uuid":"c94d03a8-caac-4d9e-a034-bf8da64c0459","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/patterns/tab-form-styles.md","content":"<!-- drift-generated -->\n# Tab Form Styles\n\nShared CSS classes for form elements inside coherence-engine tab components (required badges, checkbox labels, hints).\n\n## Location\n\n`apps/coherence-engine/webui/src/styles/components/tab-form.css`\n\nImported centrally via `styles/index.css` — no per-component import needed.\n\n## Available Classes\n\n| Class | Purpose |\n|-------|---------|\n| `tab-required-badge` | Small badge next to a title indicating a required field. Adds left margin and 10px font. |\n| `tab-checkbox-label` | Flexbox label wrapping a checkbox, label text, and hint. Uses `var(--spacing-md)` gap. |\n| `tab-required-hint` | Small 11px hint text explaining what \"required\" means in context. |\n\n## Usage\n\n```jsx\n// In any coherence-engine tab component — NO local CSS import needed\n\n<span className=\"badge badge-warning tab-required-badge\">Required</span>\n\n<label className=\"tab-checkbox-label\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" checked={isRequired} onChange={...} />\n  <span className=\"label mb-0\">Required</span>\n  <span className=\"text-muted tab-required-hint\">\n    (Action won't execute unless this variable resolves)\n  </span>\n</label>\n```\n\n## Adding New Tab Form Styles\n\nIf you need a new shared style for tab forms:\n\n1. Add the class to `styles/components/tab-form.css`\n2. Use the `tab-` prefix for the class name\n3. It's available immediately in all tab components via the central import\n\n**Do not** create a per-component CSS file in the `tabs/` directory. The ESLint rule `local/no-tab-companion-css` will flag this.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
