{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Sp9izB8qhM7wmtbvEiKdsU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## PART 2: GUARD\n\nThe existing `no-duplicate-component-css` ESLint rule already enforces this exact constraint — it detects when an app's `styles/components/` directory contains CSS files whose names match shared-components files. It's already wired into the ESLint config at `warn` severity. ADR-023 documents the decision.\n\nI need to update ADR-023 to reference this additional drift area (css-css-cluster-007), and verify the existing pattern doc covers level-selector."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":267,"cache_read_input_tokens":72230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":267},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a13268b0-3558-4a8f-abab-805b852d788c","uuid":"4b5cd99a-9d72-43f7-9dc4-ccfac77ad13a"}
