{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XJP8CRCRb2f6HdBLjg3J6x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture. Here's the consolidation strategy:\n\n**The drift:** `coherence-engine/dropdown.css` and `shared-components/dropdown.css` are full duplicates with identical class names and structure, just different sizing values. Coherence-engine imports shared-components styles first, then overrides them with its local copy — so the local copy just provides compact sizing.\n\n**The fix:**\n1. Delete `coherence-engine/dropdown.css` (the full redundant copy)\n2. Remove its `@import` from coherence-engine's `index.css`\n3. Add compact dropdown overrides to coherence-engine's `compact-overrides.css` (only the classes actually used: `.dropdown-menu`, `.dropdown-menu-item`, `.dropdown-menu-icon`, `.dropdown-menu-label`)\n4. WikiSearch.module.css is an intentional exception — it's a CSS Module with scoped class names for a different component (search widget vs generic dropdown)\n\nLet me execute. First, delete the coherence-engine dropdown.css and update its index.css."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4004,"cache_read_input_tokens":65968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4004},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b5ce8f0-862b-4723-9467-f6e56df17d06","uuid":"08a97f02-b5f0-4c03-9742-6955d51ff441"}
