{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Au255AvYEGgUVjjE7S9Xq8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the three CSS files:\n\n**GraphView.css** (canonical):\n- `.gv-wrapper` — position absolute, inset 0, overflow hidden\n- `.gv-cytoscape` — full width/height container\n- `.gv-legend` — gradient background (blue theme)\n- `.gv-legend-header` — blue-tinted background\n- `.gv-legend-footer` — lighter blue-tinted background\n- `.gv-legend-swatch` — dynamic color via CSS variable\n- Shape variants (`.gv-shape-*`) — various clip-paths for legend swatches\n\n\n- `.gv-controls` — same gradient as legend\n- `.gv-controls-header` — same as legend-header\n\n**GraphView3D.css** (variant):\n- `.gv3d-no-webgl` — WebGL fallback (unique to 3D views)\n- `.gv3d-no-webgl-inner/icon/title/message` — fallback subcomponents\n- `.gv3d-container` — position absolute, inset 0, overflow hidden (same as gv-wrapper)\n- `.gv3d-legend` — same gradient as gv-legend (blue theme)\n\nComparing the 3D variant to the canonical version, it's using the same layout and color patterns but with 3D-specific prefixes and a WebGL fallback state.\n\nContinuing with TimelineView3D.css, which follows the same structure but swaps in a warmer golden gradient for the legend instead of blue.\n\nLooking at the overlap now, I'm noticing that the container wrapper and WebGL fallback blocks are completely identical across all three stylesheets, and the legend panel structure follows the same pattern too. three have legend, legend-header, legend-footer, legend-swatch, controls, controls-header — same structural pattern but different themes\n\n2. **Structural pattern with theme variation:**\n   - Legend/controls use the same gradient pattern but with different colors (blue vs golden)\n   - This is the same UI PATTERN (floating overlay panels with gradient backgrounds) with different color themes\n\n3. **Unique to specific views:**\n   - GraphView.css: shape variants (`.gv-shape-*`) and `.gv-cytoscape`\n   - TimelineView3D.css: `.tv3d-era-swatch` and `.tv3d-era-link`\n\n**Consolidation approach:**\n\nThe shared CSS patterns are:\n1. **View container** — absolute-positioned full-bleed wrapper\n2. **WebGL fallback** — identical between the two 3D views\n3. **Overlay panel** — the legend/controls floating panel pattern (structural; colors vary by theme)\n\nI should create a shared visualization CSS file with common patterns and use CSS custom properties for theming, keeping component-specific styles separate and updating imports accordingly. Now I need to check which components actually use these CSS files and what's already in the shared-components styles.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2782,"cache_read_input_tokens":49154,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2782},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b63bbfa3-8e9b-4041-b254-e9bba5dedd64","uuid":"42c01bbf-e915-49c0-8645-3606eb5803dc"}
