{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QGP7meodknudJGPrNT2hzN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document for you. Here's the complete structure and organization:\n\n## Shared Components Styles Organization\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\n/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/packages/shared-components/src/styles/\n├── index.css                          # Main entry point (imports all other files)\n├── theme.css                          # Design tokens (CSS variables)\n├── base.css                           # CSS reset and base element styles\n├── utilities.css                      # Utility classes\n└── components/                        # Component-specific styles\n    ├── card.css\n    ├── form.css\n    ├── button.css\n    ├── modal.css\n    ├── badge.css\n    ├── toggle.css\n    ├── section.css\n    ├── empty-state.css\n    ├── error-boundary.css\n    ├── error-message.css\n    ├── item-row.css\n    ├── dropdown.css\n    ├── level-selector.css\n    ├── editor.css\n    └── actions.css\n```\n\n### How Styles Are Imported\n\nThe **`index.css`** file serves as the single entry point and follows this import order:\n\n1. **Design tokens** (`theme.css`) - CSS variables for colors, spacing, typography, shadows, z-index\n2. **Base styles** (`base.css`) - CSS reset, global element styles, focus states, scrollbar styling\n3. **Component styles** (`components/*.css`) - Individual component styles\n4. **Utilities** (`utilities.css`) - Utility classes for common patterns\n\n**Usage:** Import `index.css` once in your app's root component to get all shared styles.\n\n### Key Design Tokens (from theme.css)\n\nAll components use CSS custom properties defined in theme.css:\n\n**Colors:**\n- Background: `--color-bg`, `--color-bg-card`, `--color-bg-dark`\n- Text: `--color-text`, `--color-text-muted`, `--color-text-dim`\n- Semantic: `--color-success`, `--color-danger`, `--color-warning`, `--color-info`\n- Accent: `--color-accent`, `--color-accent-light`, `--gradient-accent`\n- Additional: `--color-purple`, `--color-pink`, `--color-teal`, `--color-gray`\n\n**Spacing:** `--spacing-xs` through `--spacing-4xl` (4px to 48px)\n\n**Border Radius:** `--radius-sm` through `--radius-full` (4px to 50%)\n\n**Typography:** Font sizes (`--font-size-xs` to `--font-size-3xl`), weights, line heights\n\n**Transitions:** `--transition-fast`, `--transition-normal`\n\n**Z-Index:** `--z-dropdown`, `--z-modal`\n\n### Component Style Patterns\n\nEach component CSS file follows these patterns:\n\n1. **Base component class** - Core styling (e.g., `.card`, `.button`, `.section`)\n2. **Variants** - State variations (e.g., `.card-clickable`, `.card-disabled`)\n3. **Sub-elements** - Internal structure (e.g., `.card-header`, `.card-title`, `.card-desc`)\n4. **Utility modifiers** - Small behavior tweaks\n5. **Responsive rules** - Media queries at the bottom\n\n**Example from card.css:**\n- `.card` - Base card container\n- `.card-clickable` - Hover state variant\n- `.card-header`, `.card-title`, `.card-desc` - Internal elements\n- `.item-card`, `.item-card-header`, `.item-card-icon` - Variation for item cards\n- Responsive rules for smaller screens\n\n### Utilities Available (from utilities.css)\n\n**Layout:**\n- Flex utilities: `.flex`, `.flex-col`, `.flex-center`, `.flex-between`, `.flex-1`, `.flex-wrap`\n- Alignment: `.items-center`\n- Gap classes: `.gap-xs` through `.gap-2xl`\n\n**Text:**\n- Colors: `.text-white`, `.text-muted`, `.text-dim`, `.text-accent`, `.text-success`, `.text-danger`, `.text-warning`\n- Sizes: `.text-xs` through `.text-2xl`\n- Weight: `.font-medium`, `.font-semibold`\n- Alignment: `.text-center`, `.text-right`\n- Effects: `.truncate`, `.text-uppercase`\n\n**Spacing:**\n- Padding: `.p-sm` through `.p-2xl`\n- Margin bottom: `.mb-0` through `.mb-2xl`\n- Margin top: `.mt-lg`, `.mt-xl`\n\n**Other:**\n- Sizing: `.w-full`\n- Positioning: `.relative`, `.absolute`\n- Cursor: `.cursor-pointer`\n- Code styling: `.inline-code`\n\n### Where to Place New Shared Visualization CSS\n\n**For new shared visualization CSS, create a new file in `/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/` following these naming conventions:**\n\n1. **Name the file** after the component/feature: `visualization.css`, `graph-view.css`, `timeline.css`, etc.\n\n2. **Structure the file** following the existing pattern:\n   ```css\n   /**\n    * [Component name] styles\n    */\n   \n   /* Base component */\n   .component-name { ... }\n   \n   /* Variants */\n   .component-name-variant { ... }\n   \n   /* Sub-elements */\n   .component-name-element { ... }\n   \n   /* Responsive rules */\n   @media (width <= 900px) { ... }\n   ```\n\n3. **Use existing CSS variables** from `theme.css`:\n   - Colors: `var(--color-bg)`, `var(--color-accent)`, etc.\n   - Spacing: `var(--spacing-lg)`, `var(--spacing-xl)`, etc.\n   - Border radius: `var(--radius-lg)`, etc.\n   - Transitions: `var(--transition-normal)`, etc.\n\n4. **Add an import in `index.css`** in the Components section:\n   ```css\n   @import url('./components/visualization.css');\n   ```\n\n5. **Follow the naming convention:**\n   - Base class: `.visualization` or `.graph-view`\n   - Variants: `.visualization-compact`, `.visualization-expanded`\n   - Elements: `.visualization-title`, `.visualization-node`, `.visualization-edge`\n\n### Best Practices\n\n1. **Always use CSS variables** for colors, spacing, and sizing - never hardcode values\n2. **Keep component-specific styles in their own files** - maintains organization\n3. **Use semantic color names** (`--color-success`, `--color-danger`) rather than specific colors\n4. **Include responsive rules** at the bottom of each file for mobile optimization\n5. **Use transitions** from theme.css for consistent animation timing\n6. **Add comments** to explain complex styles or layout patterns\n7. **Group related classes** together (base, variants, sub-elements)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a9e93d8a9378ce735 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 39403\ntool_uses: 9\nduration_ms: 23903</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b63bbfa3-8e9b-4041-b254-e9bba5dedd64","uuid":"b8a465aa-3169-4f57-a2c6-b747c4de9f46","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/packages/shared-components/src/styles/, list all files and show the structure. Also read the index.css file to understand how shared styles are organized and imported. I need to understand where to place new shared visualization CSS.","agentId":"a9e93d8a9378ce735","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document for you. Here's the complete structure and organization:\n\n## Shared Components Styles Organization\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\n/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/packages/shared-components/src/styles/\n├── index.css                          # Main entry point (imports all other files)\n├── theme.css                          # Design tokens (CSS variables)\n├── base.css                           # CSS reset and base element styles\n├── utilities.css                      # Utility classes\n└── components/                        # Component-specific styles\n    ├── card.css\n    ├── form.css\n    ├── button.css\n    ├── modal.css\n    ├── badge.css\n    ├── toggle.css\n    ├── section.css\n    ├── empty-state.css\n    ├── error-boundary.css\n    ├── error-message.css\n    ├── item-row.css\n    ├── dropdown.css\n    ├── level-selector.css\n    ├── editor.css\n    └── actions.css\n```\n\n### How Styles Are Imported\n\nThe **`index.css`** file serves as the single entry point and follows this import order:\n\n1. **Design tokens** (`theme.css`) - CSS variables for colors, spacing, typography, shadows, z-index\n2. **Base styles** (`base.css`) - CSS reset, global element styles, focus states, scrollbar styling\n3. **Component styles** (`components/*.css`) - Individual component styles\n4. **Utilities** (`utilities.css`) - Utility classes for common patterns\n\n**Usage:** Import `index.css` once in your app's root component to get all shared styles.\n\n### Key Design Tokens (from theme.css)\n\nAll components use CSS custom properties defined in theme.css:\n\n**Colors:**\n- Background: `--color-bg`, `--color-bg-card`, `--color-bg-dark`\n- Text: `--color-text`, `--color-text-muted`, `--color-text-dim`\n- Semantic: `--color-success`, `--color-danger`, `--color-warning`, `--color-info`\n- Accent: `--color-accent`, `--color-accent-light`, `--gradient-accent`\n- Additional: `--color-purple`, `--color-pink`, `--color-teal`, `--color-gray`\n\n**Spacing:** `--spacing-xs` through `--spacing-4xl` (4px to 48px)\n\n**Border Radius:** `--radius-sm` through `--radius-full` (4px to 50%)\n\n**Typography:** Font sizes (`--font-size-xs` to `--font-size-3xl`), weights, line heights\n\n**Transitions:** `--transition-fast`, `--transition-normal`\n\n**Z-Index:** `--z-dropdown`, `--z-modal`\n\n### Component Style Patterns\n\nEach component CSS file follows these patterns:\n\n1. **Base component class** - Core styling (e.g., `.card`, `.button`, `.section`)\n2. **Variants** - State variations (e.g., `.card-clickable`, `.card-disabled`)\n3. **Sub-elements** - Internal structure (e.g., `.card-header`, `.card-title`, `.card-desc`)\n4. **Utility modifiers** - Small behavior tweaks\n5. **Responsive rules** - Media queries at the bottom\n\n**Example from card.css:**\n- `.card` - Base card container\n- `.card-clickable` - Hover state variant\n- `.card-header`, `.card-title`, `.card-desc` - Internal elements\n- `.item-card`, `.item-card-header`, `.item-card-icon` - Variation for item cards\n- Responsive rules for smaller screens\n\n### Utilities Available (from utilities.css)\n\n**Layout:**\n- Flex utilities: `.flex`, `.flex-col`, `.flex-center`, `.flex-between`, `.flex-1`, `.flex-wrap`\n- Alignment: `.items-center`\n- Gap classes: `.gap-xs` through `.gap-2xl`\n\n**Text:**\n- Colors: `.text-white`, `.text-muted`, `.text-dim`, `.text-accent`, `.text-success`, `.text-danger`, `.text-warning`\n- Sizes: `.text-xs` through `.text-2xl`\n- Weight: `.font-medium`, `.font-semibold`\n- Alignment: `.text-center`, `.text-right`\n- Effects: `.truncate`, `.text-uppercase`\n\n**Spacing:**\n- Padding: `.p-sm` through `.p-2xl`\n- Margin bottom: `.mb-0` through `.mb-2xl`\n- Margin top: `.mt-lg`, `.mt-xl`\n\n**Other:**\n- Sizing: `.w-full`\n- Positioning: `.relative`, `.absolute`\n- Cursor: `.cursor-pointer`\n- Code styling: `.inline-code`\n\n### Where to Place New Shared Visualization CSS\n\n**For new shared visualization CSS, create a new file in `/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/` following these naming conventions:**\n\n1. **Name the file** after the component/feature: `visualization.css`, `graph-view.css`, `timeline.css`, etc.\n\n2. **Structure the file** following the existing pattern:\n   ```css\n   /**\n    * [Component name] styles\n    */\n   \n   /* Base component */\n   .component-name { ... }\n   \n   /* Variants */\n   .component-name-variant { ... }\n   \n   /* Sub-elements */\n   .component-name-element { ... }\n   \n   /* Responsive rules */\n   @media (width <= 900px) { ... }\n   ```\n\n3. **Use existing CSS variables** from `theme.css`:\n   - Colors: `var(--color-bg)`, `var(--color-accent)`, etc.\n   - Spacing: `var(--spacing-lg)`, `var(--spacing-xl)`, etc.\n   - Border radius: `var(--radius-lg)`, etc.\n   - Transitions: `var(--transition-normal)`, etc.\n\n4. **Add an import in `index.css`** in the Components section:\n   ```css\n   @import url('./components/visualization.css');\n   ```\n\n5. **Follow the naming convention:**\n   - Base class: `.visualization` or `.graph-view`\n   - Variants: `.visualization-compact`, `.visualization-expanded`\n   - Elements: `.visualization-title`, `.visualization-node`, `.visualization-edge`\n\n### Best Practices\n\n1. **Always use CSS variables** for colors, spacing, and sizing - never hardcode values\n2. **Keep component-specific styles in their own files** - maintains organization\n3. **Use semantic color names** (`--color-success`, `--color-danger`) rather than specific colors\n4. **Include responsive rules** at the bottom of each file for mobile optimization\n5. **Use transitions** from theme.css for consistent animation timing\n6. **Add comments** to explain complex styles or layout patterns\n7. **Group related classes** together (base, variants, sub-elements)"}],"totalDurationMs":23903,"totalTokens":39403,"totalToolUseCount":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6994,"cache_read_input_tokens":30691,"output_tokens":1711,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6994,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016tSdXwQbnsJ6B2jL33yLiM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me analyze the overlap:\n\n**Shared patterns across all 3 CSS files:**\n\n1. **View container** — `position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden;`\n   - `.gv-wrapper` (GraphView)\n   - `.gv3d-container` (GraphView3D)\n   - `.tv3d-container` (TimelineView3D)\n\n2. **Legend panel** — gradient background (different colors per theme)\n   - `.gv-legend`, `.gv3d-legend`, `.tv3d-legend`\n\n3. **Legend header** — tinted background\n   - `.gv-legend-header`, `.gv3d-legend-header`, `.tv3d-legend-header`\n\n4. **Legend footer** — lighter tinted background\n   - `.gv-legend-footer`, `.gv3d-legend-footer`, `.tv3d-legend-footer`\n\n5. **Legend swatch** — dynamic color via CSS variable\n   - `.gv-legend-swatch`, `.gv3d-legend-swatch`, `.tv3d-legend-swatch`\n\n6. **Controls panel** — same gradient as legend\n   - `.gv-controls`, `.gv3d-controls`, `.tv3d-controls`\n\nI can see the pattern now—each component has three parallel implementations with consistent naming conventions. The controls panel mirrors the legend styling, which suggests I could consolidate these shared styles into a base set of rules.\n\nFor the 3D views specifically, I need to handle the WebGL fallback states across both GraphView3D and TimelineView3D with matching class names and styling for the container, inner wrapper, icon, title, and message elements.\n\nBeyond the shared patterns, GraphView has its own Cytoscape container and shape variants, while TimelineView3D introduces era-specific styling for swatches and links. The key visual distinction comes down to color theming—GraphView uses a cool blue palette with blue accents, whereas TimelineView3D shifts to a warmer golden tone throughout its gradient and highlights.\n\nFor consolidation, I'm thinking about creating a shared visualization stylesheet that centralizes the common container patterns, WebGL fallback messaging, and legend/controls components with CSS custom properties for theming flexibility. The tricky part is that these panels currently rely on hardcoded colors rather than pulling from the theme system, so I need to refactor them to use CSS variables instead, allowing the blue and golden themes to be swapped cleanly. Still writing theme variables... Finishing up the WebGL fallback styles with centered messaging and icons, then I'm moving on to think through how to structure the component-specific CSS files after extracting the shared theme variables.\n\nFor GraphView, the Cytoscape container and shape legend swatches need to stay, GraphView3D can be deleted entirely since it has no unique styles, and TimelineView3D keeps its era-specific swatches and link indicators. Now I need to update the component files themselves to import the shared CSS and apply the theme classes properly, though I'm realizing the components are using Tailwind which might complicate things.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4795,"cache_read_input_tokens":51936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4795},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b63bbfa3-8e9b-4041-b254-e9bba5dedd64","uuid":"345d8a57-2d2b-4889-a1a0-64967f654028"}
