{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Do6XwU9Pi5MLGbBuhaNn9C","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * BulkBackportModal - Progress display for automatic multi-chronicle bulk backport\n     3→ *\n     4→ * Two phases:\n     5→ * 1. Confirmation: entity list with chronicle counts, confirm/cancel buttons\n     6→ * 2. Processing: progress bars, current chronicle, entity count, cost\n     7→ *\n     8→ * Uses BulkOperationShell for overlay, header, pill lifecycle, and footer.\n     9→ */\n    10→\n    11→import React, { useMemo } from \"react\";\n    12→import PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\n    13→import BulkOperationShell, { BulkTerminalMessage, BulkCost } from \"./BulkOperationShell\";\n    14→import \"./BulkBackportModal.css\";\n    15→const PILL_ID = \"bulk-backport\";\n    16→export default function BulkBackportModal({\n    17→  progress,\n    18→  onConfirm,\n    19→  onCancel,\n    20→  onClose\n    21→}) {\n    22→  const chronicles = progress?.chronicles;\n    23→  const realTotal = useMemo(() => chronicles ? chronicles.reduce((sum, c) => sum + c.totalEntities, 0) : 0, [chronicles]);\n    24→  const isConfirming = progress?.status === \"confirming\";\n    25→  const isTerminal = progress?.status === \"complete\" || progress?.status === \"cancelled\" || progress?.status === \"failed\";\n    26→  const currentChronicle = progress?.chronicles?.[progress.currentChronicleIndex];\n    27→  const globalPercent = progress?.totalEntities > 0 ? Math.round(progress.processedEntities / progress.totalEntities * 100) : 0;\n    28→  const completedChronicles = progress?.chronicles?.filter(c => c.status === \"complete\").length ?? 0;\n    29→  const failedChronicles = progress?.chronicles?.filter(c => c.status === \"failed\").length ?? 0;\n    30→  let progressFillModifier;\n    31→  if (progress?.status === \"failed\") progressFillModifier = \"bbm-progress-fill-failed\";else if (progress?.status === \"cancelled\") progressFillModifier = \"bbm-progress-fill-cancelled\";else progressFillModifier = \"bbm-progress-fill-ok\";\n    32→  const progressFillClass = `bbm-progress-fill ${progressFillModifier}`;\n    33→\n    34→  // Header status text\n    35→  let statusText;\n    36→  if (isConfirming) statusText = `${progress?.chronicles?.length ?? 0} chronicles`;else if (progress?.status === \"running\") statusText = \"Processing...\";else if (progress?.status === \"complete\") statusText = \"Complete\";else if (progress?.status === \"cancelled\") statusText = \"Cancelled\";else if (progress?.status === \"failed\") statusText = \"Failed\";\n    37→\n    38→  // Pill status text when minimized\n    39→  const pillStatusText = progress?.status === \"running\" ? `${progress.processedEntities}/${progress.totalEntities}` : progress?.status;\n    40→  return <BulkOperationShell pillId={PILL_ID} title=\"Bulk Backport\" tabId=\"chronicle\" progress={progress} onConfirm={onConfirm} onCancel={onCancel} onClose={onClose} confirmLabel={`Start Backport (${progress?.totalEntities ?? 0} entities)`} statusText={statusText} pillStatusText={pillStatusText} confirmWidth=\"540px\" processWidth=\"480px\">\n    41→      {/* ---- Confirmation screen ---- */}\n    42→      {isConfirming && progress.entitySummary && <div className=\"bbm-entity-section\">\n    43→          <div className=\"bbm-entity-header\">\n    44→            <span className=\"bbm-section-label\">\n    45→              Entities ({progress.entitySummary.length})\n    46→            </span>\n    47→            <span className=\"bbm-section-meta\">\n    48→              {progress.totalEntities} updates across {progress.chronicles.length} chronicles\n    49→            </span>\n    50→          </div>\n    51→\n    52→          <div className=\"bbm-entity-list\">\n    53→            {progress.entitySummary.map((entity, i) => <div key={entity.entityId} className={`bbm-entity-row ${i < progress.entitySummary.length - 1 ? \"bbm-entity-row-bordered\" : \"\"}`}>\n    54→                <div className=\"bbm-entity-info\">\n    55→                  <span className=\"bbm-entity-name\">{entity.entityName}</span>\n    56→                  <span className=\"bbm-entity-kind\">\n    57→                    {entity.entityKind}\n    58→                    {entity.entitySubtype ? ` / ${entity.entitySubtype}` : \"\"}\n    59→                  </span>\n    60→                </div>\n    61→                <span className=\"bbm-entity-chr\" title={`${entity.chronicleCount} chronicle${entity.chronicleCount !== 1 ? \"s\" : \"\"} will update this entity`}>\n    62→                  {entity.chronicleCount} chr\n    63→                </span>\n    64→              </div>)}\n    65→          </div>\n    66→        </div>}\n    67→\n    68→      {/* ---- Processing screen ---- */}\n    69→      {!isConfirming && progress?.status !== \"idle\" && <>\n    70→          {/* Global progress */}\n    71→          <div className=\"bbm-progress-section\">\n    72→            <div className=\"bbm-progress-header\">\n    73→              <span className=\"bbm-progress-label\">\n    74→                Chronicle{\" \"}\n    75→                {Math.min(progress.currentChronicleIndex + 1, progress.chronicles.length)} /{\" \"}\n    76→                {progress.chronicles.length}\n    77→              </span>\n    78→              <span className=\"bbm-progress-percent\">{globalPercent}%</span>\n    79→            </div>\n    80→\n    81→            {/* Global progress bar */}\n    82→            <div className=\"bbm-progress-track\">\n    83→              <div className={progressFillClass}\n    84→          style={{\n    85→            \"--bbm-progress-width\": `${globalPercent}%`\n    86→          }} />\n    87→            </div>\n    88→\n    89→            <div className=\"bbm-progress-stats\">\n    90→              <span>\n    91→                {progress.processedEntities} / {realTotal || progress.totalEntities} entities\n    92→              </span>\n    93→              <span>\n    94→                {completedChronicles} / {progress.chronicles.length} chronicles\n    95→              </span>\n    96→            </div>\n    97→          </div>\n    98→\n    99→          {/* Current chronicle detail */}\n   100→          {currentChronicle && !isTerminal && <div className=\"bbm-chronicle-detail\">\n   101→              <div className=\"bbm-chronicle-title\">{currentChronicle.chronicleTitle}</div>\n   102→\n   103→              {currentChronicle.totalBatches > 1 && <div className=\"bbm-chronicle-batch-info\">\n   104→                  <span>\n   105→                    Batch{\" \"}\n   106→                    {Math.min(currentChronicle.completedBatches + 1, currentChronicle.totalBatches)}{\" \"}\n   107→                    / {currentChronicle.totalBatches}\n   108→                  </span>\n   109→                  <span>\n   110→                    {currentChronicle.processedEntities} / {currentChronicle.totalEntities}{\" \"}\n   111→                    entities\n   112→                  </span>\n   113→                </div>}\n   114→\n   115→              {currentChronicle.totalBatches <= 1 && <div className=\"bbm-chronicle-entity-count\">\n   116→                  {currentChronicle.totalEntities} entities\n   117→                </div>}\n   118→            </div>}\n   119→\n   120→          {/* Terminal state messages */}\n   121→          {progress.status === \"complete\" && <BulkTerminalMessage status=\"complete\">\n   122→              Backported {progress.processedEntities} entities across {completedChronicles}{\" \"}\n   123→              chronicles.\n   124→              {failedChronicles > 0 && <span className=\"bulk-failed-inline\">\n   125→                  {\" \"}\n   126→                  {failedChronicles} chronicle(s) failed.\n   127→                </span>}\n   128→            </BulkTerminalMessage>}\n   129→\n   130→          {progress.status === \"cancelled\" && <BulkTerminalMessage status=\"cancelled\">\n   131→              Cancelled after processing {progress.processedEntities} entities across{\" \"}\n   132→              {completedChronicles} chronicles.\n   133→            </BulkTerminalMessage>}\n   134→\n   135→          {progress.status === \"failed\" && <BulkTerminalMessage status=\"failed\">\n   136→              {progress.error || \"An unexpected error occurred.\"}\n   137→            </BulkTerminalMessage>}\n   138→\n   139→          {/* Cost */}\n   140→          <BulkCost cost={progress.totalCost} />\n   141→        </>}\n   142→    </BulkOperationShell>;\n   143→}\n   144→BulkBackportModal.propTypes = {\n   145→  progress: PropTypes.object,\n   146→  onConfirm: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   147→  onCancel: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   148→  onClose: PropTypes.func.isRequired\n   149→};\n   150→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f489ea2-964b-4b12-9123-73dad996ade9","uuid":"42f95f4d-0f7c-4c9b-bd3f-3f210e5c560c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/apps/illuminator/webui/src/components/BulkBackportModal.jsx","content":"/**\n * BulkBackportModal - Progress display for automatic multi-chronicle bulk backport\n *\n * Two phases:\n * 1. Confirmation: entity list with chronicle counts, confirm/cancel buttons\n * 2. Processing: progress bars, current chronicle, entity count, cost\n *\n * Uses BulkOperationShell for overlay, header, pill lifecycle, and footer.\n */\n\nimport React, { useMemo } from \"react\";\nimport PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\nimport BulkOperationShell, { BulkTerminalMessage, BulkCost } from \"./BulkOperationShell\";\nimport \"./BulkBackportModal.css\";\nconst PILL_ID = \"bulk-backport\";\nexport default function BulkBackportModal({\n  progress,\n  onConfirm,\n  onCancel,\n  onClose\n}) {\n  const chronicles = progress?.chronicles;\n  const realTotal = useMemo(() => chronicles ? chronicles.reduce((sum, c) => sum + c.totalEntities, 0) : 0, [chronicles]);\n  const isConfirming = progress?.status === \"confirming\";\n  const isTerminal = progress?.status === \"complete\" || progress?.status === \"cancelled\" || progress?.status === \"failed\";\n  const currentChronicle = progress?.chronicles?.[progress.currentChronicleIndex];\n  const globalPercent = progress?.totalEntities > 0 ? Math.round(progress.processedEntities / progress.totalEntities * 100) : 0;\n  const completedChronicles = progress?.chronicles?.filter(c => c.status === \"complete\").length ?? 0;\n  const failedChronicles = progress?.chronicles?.filter(c => c.status === \"failed\").length ?? 0;\n  let progressFillModifier;\n  if (progress?.status === \"failed\") progressFillModifier = \"bbm-progress-fill-failed\";else if (progress?.status === \"cancelled\") progressFillModifier = \"bbm-progress-fill-cancelled\";else progressFillModifier = \"bbm-progress-fill-ok\";\n  const progressFillClass = `bbm-progress-fill ${progressFillModifier}`;\n\n  // Header status text\n  let statusText;\n  if (isConfirming) statusText = `${progress?.chronicles?.length ?? 0} chronicles`;else if (progress?.status === \"running\") statusText = \"Processing...\";else if (progress?.status === \"complete\") statusText = \"Complete\";else if (progress?.status === \"cancelled\") statusText = \"Cancelled\";else if (progress?.status === \"failed\") statusText = \"Failed\";\n\n  // Pill status text when minimized\n  const pillStatusText = progress?.status === \"running\" ? `${progress.processedEntities}/${progress.totalEntities}` : progress?.status;\n  return <BulkOperationShell pillId={PILL_ID} title=\"Bulk Backport\" tabId=\"chronicle\" progress={progress} onConfirm={onConfirm} onCancel={onCancel} onClose={onClose} confirmLabel={`Start Backport (${progress?.totalEntities ?? 0} entities)`} statusText={statusText} pillStatusText={pillStatusText} confirmWidth=\"540px\" processWidth=\"480px\">\n      {/* ---- Confirmation screen ---- */}\n      {isConfirming && progress.entitySummary && <div className=\"bbm-entity-section\">\n          <div className=\"bbm-entity-header\">\n            <span className=\"bbm-section-label\">\n              Entities ({progress.entitySummary.length})\n            </span>\n            <span className=\"bbm-section-meta\">\n              {progress.totalEntities} updates across {progress.chronicles.length} chronicles\n            </span>\n          </div>\n\n          <div className=\"bbm-entity-list\">\n            {progress.entitySummary.map((entity, i) => <div key={entity.entityId} className={`bbm-entity-row ${i < progress.entitySummary.length - 1 ? \"bbm-entity-row-bordered\" : \"\"}`}>\n                <div className=\"bbm-entity-info\">\n                  <span className=\"bbm-entity-name\">{entity.entityName}</span>\n                  <span className=\"bbm-entity-kind\">\n                    {entity.entityKind}\n                    {entity.entitySubtype ? ` / ${entity.entitySubtype}` : \"\"}\n                  </span>\n                </div>\n                <span className=\"bbm-entity-chr\" title={`${entity.chronicleCount} chronicle${entity.chronicleCount !== 1 ? \"s\" : \"\"} will update this entity`}>\n                  {entity.chronicleCount} chr\n                </span>\n              </div>)}\n          </div>\n        </div>}\n\n      {/* ---- Processing screen ---- */}\n      {!isConfirming && progress?.status !== \"idle\" && <>\n          {/* Global progress */}\n          <div className=\"bbm-progress-section\">\n            <div className=\"bbm-progress-header\">\n              <span className=\"bbm-progress-label\">\n                Chronicle{\" \"}\n                {Math.min(progress.currentChronicleIndex + 1, progress.chronicles.length)} /{\" \"}\n                {progress.chronicles.length}\n              </span>\n              <span className=\"bbm-progress-percent\">{globalPercent}%</span>\n            </div>\n\n            {/* Global progress bar */}\n            <div className=\"bbm-progress-track\">\n              <div className={progressFillClass}\n          style={{\n            \"--bbm-progress-width\": `${globalPercent}%`\n          }} />\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"bbm-progress-stats\">\n              <span>\n                {progress.processedEntities} / {realTotal || progress.totalEntities} entities\n              </span>\n              <span>\n                {completedChronicles} / {progress.chronicles.length} chronicles\n              </span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          {/* Current chronicle detail */}\n          {currentChronicle && !isTerminal && <div className=\"bbm-chronicle-detail\">\n              <div className=\"bbm-chronicle-title\">{currentChronicle.chronicleTitle}</div>\n\n              {currentChronicle.totalBatches > 1 && <div className=\"bbm-chronicle-batch-info\">\n                  <span>\n                    Batch{\" \"}\n                    {Math.min(currentChronicle.completedBatches + 1, currentChronicle.totalBatches)}{\" \"}\n                    / {currentChronicle.totalBatches}\n                  </span>\n                  <span>\n                    {currentChronicle.processedEntities} / {currentChronicle.totalEntities}{\" \"}\n                    entities\n                  </span>\n                </div>}\n\n              {currentChronicle.totalBatches <= 1 && <div className=\"bbm-chronicle-entity-count\">\n                  {currentChronicle.totalEntities} entities\n                </div>}\n            </div>}\n\n          {/* Terminal state messages */}\n          {progress.status === \"complete\" && <BulkTerminalMessage status=\"complete\">\n              Backported {progress.processedEntities} entities across {completedChronicles}{\" \"}\n              chronicles.\n              {failedChronicles > 0 && <span className=\"bulk-failed-inline\">\n                  {\" \"}\n                  {failedChronicles} chronicle(s) failed.\n                </span>}\n            </BulkTerminalMessage>}\n\n          {progress.status === \"cancelled\" && <BulkTerminalMessage status=\"cancelled\">\n              Cancelled after processing {progress.processedEntities} entities across{\" \"}\n              {completedChronicles} chronicles.\n            </BulkTerminalMessage>}\n\n          {progress.status === \"failed\" && <BulkTerminalMessage status=\"failed\">\n              {progress.error || \"An unexpected error occurred.\"}\n            </BulkTerminalMessage>}\n\n          {/* Cost */}\n          <BulkCost cost={progress.totalCost} />\n        </>}\n    </BulkOperationShell>;\n}\nBulkBackportModal.propTypes = {\n  progress: PropTypes.object,\n  onConfirm: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n  onCancel: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n  onClose: PropTypes.func.isRequired\n};\n","numLines":150,"startLine":1,"totalLines":150}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011NZkjLBtKjEf8xbmuHcACC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the complete picture. BulkBackportModal uses `<BulkOperationShell>` which handles:\n- Overlay, dialog, header (with title, minimize button, status), footer (with confirm/cancel/close buttons)\n- Pill lifecycle management\n\nBulkEraNarrativeModal duplicates ALL of this inline. The fix is clear:\n1. Refactor BulkEraNarrativeModal.jsx to use `<BulkOperationShell>` as a wrapper\n2. Move only the content-specific JSX (confirmation eras list + tone selectors, processing step progress + streaming) as children\n\n\n3. Strip the shell CSS classes from BulkEraNarrativeModal.css\n\nThe tricky part is that BulkEraNarrativeModal has its own `isOpen` prop for visibility while BulkOperationShell relies on `progress?.status === 'idle'` to hide, and the status text rendering differs slightly—but these can be mapped to BulkOperationShell's existing props, and the pill management duplication can be eliminated entirely.\n\nLooking more carefully at the visibility logic, BulkOperationShell already handles the `!progress || progress.status === \"idle\"` and `isMinimized` cases, but BulkEraNarrativeModal adds an extra `!isOpen` check that needs to stay. I'll wrap the shell in a conditional that checks `isOpen` first before rendering anything.\n\nFor the CSS cleanup, I need to remove all the modal structure styles like overlay, modal, header, and footer classes, but keep all the content-specific styles for the era sections, tone selector, and progress tracking.\n\nLooking at this more carefully, I realize the BulkEraNarrativeModal can leverage existing shared components from BulkOperationShell—the terminal messages, progress bar, and cost display are already handled by those components, so I can strip out their corresponding CSS classes too and rely on the bulk-prefixed classes instead.\n\nThe tricky part is that the modal's progress bar and terminal rendering have slightly different styling and labels than the shared components—it shows \"Era X / Y\" with custom benm-prefixed classes rather than the standard bulk-progress classes. I'm weighing whether to refactor the modal to use the shared components directly or keep the custom rendering separate.\n\nSince the terminal messages are functionally identical and the progress bar logic is nearly the same, I'll lean toward reusing the shared components where possible. I'll import BulkOperationShell and the terminal/cost components, then adapt the era-specific progress data to fit their interface while keeping the custom step-progress UI and streaming counters as-is.\n\nFor the refactoring, I need to remove the local pill management and effects from BulkEraNarrativeModal, wrap the content with BulkOperationShell, swap out the terminal message markup for the shared component, and preserve the era-specific tone selectors and step tracking. Then I'll strip out all the shell-related CSS classes from the stylesheet since BulkOperationShell handles those styles now. I need to reconsider the progress bar — it's showing era-level progress rather than entity-level, which makes it unique to this modal, so I shouldn't reuse BulkProgressBar. However, I can definitely use BulkTerminalMessage for the terminal output since the structure is identical, and I can also leverage BulkCost. Let me refine what I'm removing from the CSS: the shell-level classes like the overlay, modal container, header with its subcomponents, and body styling since BulkOperationShell already handles those.\n\nUpdating the JSX involves importing the shared components, removing the minimize state and its related effects, computing the status text as props instead, wrapping everything in BulkOperationShell, and swapping out the inline terminal message divs for the BulkTerminalMessage component while replacing the cost display as well.\n\nThe other 19 modal files like ChronologyModal and DynamicsGenerationModal are standalone modals with their own styling patterns, not bulk operations, so they'd need a separate generic modal shell rather than fitting into BulkOperationShell. For now, I should focus on fixing BulkEraNarrativeModal to use BulkOperationShell to eliminate the duplication, and note the remaining modals as a separate consolidation effort. I see the core constraint now — refactoring all those JSX class names across 15+ modals is impractical, so I'll focus on the primary target (BulkEraNarrativeModal) and create a shared modal-shell.css as the canonical pattern going forward, with the rest documented as a backlog item that an ESLint rule can help enforce for new modals.\n\nLooking at the 19 non-bulk files more carefully, most aren't actually modals at all — they're panels and editors that just happen to share similar CSS patterns like section labels and list styles, so they're not part of the duplication problem I need to solve. modals with their own shells:\n- ChronologyModal.css — own shell\n- CreateEntityModal.css — need to check\n- DynamicsGenerationModal.css — own shell\n- EntityRenameModal.css — need to check\n- EraNarrativeModal.css — own shell  \n- HistorianReviewModal.css — need to check\n- HistoryCompressionPreviewModal.css — need to check\n- InterleavedAnnotationModal.css — need to check\n- QuickCheckModal.css — need to check\n- SummaryRevisionModal.css — own shell\n- ToneAssignmentPreviewModal.css — need to check\n\nThe ones that are NOT modals:\n- BulkOperationShell.css — the shared shell itself (not a variant)\n- ChroniclePanel.css — a panel component\n\nLooking at the remaining files like ChroniclePlanEditor, NarrativeTimeline, ChronicleWorkspace, and the various viewers and editors — these aren't modals, they're structural components. They share design tokens like border colors and text styling, but that's just the design system at work, not shell duplication. A new shared CSS file would be overkill here. The real guard should focus on preventing modal shells from being duplicated.\n\nSo my plan is to unify BulkEraNarrativeModal to use the shared BulkOperationShell, strip out its redundant shell styles, and document the remaining standalone modals as intentional exceptions. Then I'll set up an ESLint rule to catch any future attempts to create new modal shells, write an ADR explaining the decision, and document the pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2941,"cache_read_input_tokens":96854,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2941},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f489ea2-964b-4b12-9123-73dad996ade9","uuid":"431fc34b-b672-4880-af1d-280444b6ccf0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011NZkjLBtKjEf8xbmuHcACC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the complete picture. Here's what I found:\n\n**BulkOperationShell.jsx** is a shared React wrapper component that handles overlay, dialog, header (title + minimize + status), footer (confirm/cancel/close), and pill lifecycle. It uses `bulk-*` CSS classes from `BulkOperationShell.css`.\n\n**BulkBackportModal** and **BulkHistorianModal** use `BulkOperationShell` as a wrapper — they only render content-specific JSX/CSS. This is the canonical pattern.\n\n**BulkEraNarrativeModal** duplicates the entire shell inline: its own overlay, modal, header, minimize button, pill management, footer, AND terminal messages — all with `benm-*` prefixed CSS. This is the clear drift target.\n\nThe other 17 variant files are standalone modals/panels (not bulk operations) that share design token patterns but aren't candidates for BulkOperationShell migration. I'll document those as intentional exceptions.\n\nLet me now refactor BulkEraNarrativeModal."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2941,"cache_read_input_tokens":96854,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2941},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f489ea2-964b-4b12-9123-73dad996ade9","uuid":"177269cb-c591-4ba0-9fb5-85d1c19d9a40"}
