{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ARboYL3e56qW6UCVwUosp4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I have the ESLint config and the ADR numbering. The next ADR will be 028. Let me now:\n\n1. Append to UNIFICATION_LOG.md\n2. Create the ESLint rule for preventing bulk modal shell duplication\n3. Wire it into eslint.config.js4. Create ADR 028\n5. Create/update pattern doc\n\nLet me think about what the ESLint rule should enforce. The drift was BulkEraNarrativeModal duplicating the shell (overlay, modal, header, footer, etc.) instead of using BulkOperationShell. The guard should prevent new bulk modals from doing the same thing.\n\n\nI'm considering what's actually enforceable here—I could check for imports from bulk stores paired with BulkOperationShell, but that's too narrow. CSS patterns would be ideal but ESLint doesn't lint CSS files. The most practical approach is a JSX check that flags when a component renders the telltale overlay-modal-header-footer structure together.\n\nActually, I should look at the existing rules I've already written—`no-duplicate-component-css.js`, `no-viz-overlay-drift.js`, and `no-remote-shell-drift.js`—to understand the established pattern before building something new.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4313,"cache_read_input_tokens":130406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4313},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f489ea2-964b-4b12-9123-73dad996ade9","uuid":"8723a50c-127d-4fd0-a6fc-03ef42edd1a5"}
