{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017pfnJnWMTU9ZbnpycHc2wQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The BulkCost is imported but I changed the cost rendering pattern. Let me check. In the original, cost was rendered as inline text:\n```\n{progress.totalCost > 0 && <span>Cost: ${progress.totalCost.toFixed(4)}</span>}\n```\n\nI didn't actually use `BulkCost` because the component wraps cost differently — the BulkEraNarrativeModal shows \"words\" and \"cost\" side by side in a `benm-stats` div. Let me look at BulkCost to understand its rendering.\n\nLooking at the BulkOperationShell code:\n\n\nDefining the BulkCost component...\n\nI see the issue now—the BulkCost component wraps the cost in its own div, which doesn't fit well inside the flex row layout of benm-stats where the cost and word count are displayed together. Since the cost is already being rendered inline with the word count in the modal, I can remove the unused BulkCost import and keep the cost display as a simple span within the existing stats container.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":145566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":468},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f489ea2-964b-4b12-9123-73dad996ade9","uuid":"8ff72084-83c3-4dfb-b672-0a13bb3fa754"}
