abel styles with muted text colors that appear throughout the codebase.\n\nFooter action rows use flexbox with right-aligned content and consistent spacing, while modal dialogs follow a standard structure with overlay, card, header, scrollable body, and footer sections. Now I'm trying to figure out the best approach for consolidating these patterns—the shared-components package already has a styles directory with component-specific files, and ActivityPanel.css demonstrates a prefix-based approach with co-located styles, but there's some tension in how to handle this drift.\n\nThe real issue is that these same CSS micro-patterns keep getting redeclared across every file. I should create shared utility classes in the styles directory that components can import and reuse, or define CSS custom properties and composable utilities instead of having each component reinvent the wheel. Let me check what's already available in shared-components and re-read the task to make sure I'm consolidating in the right place.\n\nSince there's 44% similarity across 20 files but each one has mostly unique component-specific styles, the practical approach is to extract just the commonly duplicated utility-level patterns—empty states, section cards, action buttons, status colors—into a shared file, have each component import it, and then delete the redundant declarations while keeping their unique rules intact.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10684,"cache_read_input_tokens":102417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10684},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05755054-80c6-4cf5-a504-7682615d2e55","uuid":"c10791e2-7b2d-4cbb-860a-b6ebc303758d"}
