{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me chronologically analyze the conversation:\n\n1. The user's initial message is a complex drift unification + guard task for CSS duplication across 17 CSS files in the illuminator app. The area ID is `css-css-cluster-003` with LOW impact and 43% average similarity.\n\n2. The canonical pattern is BackrefImageEditor.css, and there are 16 variant files to migrate.\n\n3. The task has two parts:\n   - PART 1: UNIFY - Refactor variant files to align with canonical pattern\n   - PART 2: GUARD - Generate ESLint rules, ADR, and pattern docs\n\n4. I started by reading the work file and ESLint rule patterns reference, then read all 17 CSS files to understand the patterns.\n\n5. I discovered that BackrefImageEditor.css (the \"canonical\") actually uses hardcoded `rgb()` colors while all other files use CSS custom properties - making it the outlier.\n\n6. I identified the duplicated patterns across files:\n   - Empty states (12+ files)\n   - Selection bars (3 files)\n   - Stats grids (2-3 files)\n   - Image thumbnail covers (3 files)\n   - Section labels (8+ files)\n\n7. I read the existing shared-components CSS infrastructure (panel-utilities.css, empty-state.css, badge.css) and found that `ilu-empty` and `ilu-section-label` already existed.\n\n8. My approach:\n   a. Extend panel-utilities.css with new shared utilities\n   b. Migrate BackrefImageEditor.css to CSS variables\n   c. Trim duplicated rules from all variant CSS files\n   d. Update JSX files to compose shared utility classes\n   e. Write guard artifacts\n\n9. Actions completed:\n   - Extended panel-utilities.css with: ilu-selection-bar, ilu-stats-grid, ilu-stat-card, ilu-stat-value, ilu-stat-label, ilu-thumb-cover, ilu-thumb-placeholder\n   - Migrated BackrefImageEditor.css from hardcoded colors to CSS custom properties\n   - Dispatched 3 parallel agents for selection bars, stats grids, and thumb covers (all completed successfully)\n   - Trimmed empty state CSS rules from all variant files\n   - Updated JSX files for empty states, selection bars, stats grids, and thumb covers\n\n10. Errors encountered:\n    - MCP replace_content tool was denied - switched to Edit tool\n    - Edit tool requires files to be read first - had to re-read files\n    - `rgb(var(--accent-color-rgb, 59 130 246) / 30%)` doesn't work in CSS - reverted to hardcoded `rgb(59 130 246 / 30%)`\n\n11. What's still pending:\n    - Update StoragePanel.jsx and TraitPaletteSection.tsx empty state JSX (storage-panel-empty, tps-loading, tps-empty, tps-kind-empty)\n    - Update remaining CSS files that don't have clear empty state patterns (GenerateStep, RoleAssignmentStep, ImageSettingsDrawer, WorldContextEditor) - need some change per instructions\n    - Append to UNIFICATION_LOG.md\n    - Create ESLint guard rule\n    - Create ADR document\n    - Create pattern documentation\n\n12. The current todo list shows:\n    - [completed] Extend panel-utilities.css\n    - [completed] Migrate BackrefImageEditor.css\n    - [in_progress] Trim duplicated empty-state rules\n    - [pending] Trim duplicated selection-bar, stats-grid, and thumb rules (agents completed this)\n    - [pending] Update JSX files (partially done)\n    - [pending] Append entry to UNIFICATION_LOG.md\n    - [pending] Create ESLint guard rule\n    - [pending] Create ADR and pattern documentation\n\nLet me now list all specific file changes made and pending.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user requested execution of a drift unification AND guard artifact generation for area `css-css-cluster-003` — \"CSS Duplication: BackrefImageEditor.css, ChronicleImagePicker.css, EntryPointStep.css\" in `/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry`. This is a two-part task:\n   \n   **PART 1 (UNIFY):** Refactor 17 CSS files (1 canonical + 16 variants) in the illuminator app to consolidate duplicated CSS patterns into shared utilities in `packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/panel-utilities.css`. Update `@import` paths and JSX class compositions. Append to `UNIFICATION_LOG.md`.\n   \n   **PART 2 (GUARD):** Generate ESLint rules in `eslint-rules/`, an ADR in `docs/adr/`, and a pattern doc in `docs/patterns/` — all with drift markers on line 1. Every area MUST have at least one machine-enforceable ESLint rule.\n\n   The work file is at `.drift-audit/unify-work/unify-work-css-css-cluster-003.json`. Canonical variant: `BackrefImageEditor.css`. Environment: `DRIFT_SEMANTIC=/home/tsonu/.drift-semantic`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - CSS utility class composition pattern: `className=\"ilu-shared component-specific\"` (ADR-029 approach)\n   - Panel utilities CSS (`ilu-*` prefix) as shared structural patterns\n   - Design token usage via CSS custom properties (`var(--text-muted)`, `var(--bg-tertiary)`, etc.)\n   - Drift pipeline: audit → unify → guard\n   - ESLint custom rule writing with `warn` severity for drift prevention\n   - Drift markers: `// drift-generated` for JS, `<!-- drift-generated -->` for MD\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Work File Read:**\n   - `.drift-audit/unify-work/unify-work-css-css-cluster-003.json` — Contains area definition with 17 files total, canonical variant BackrefImageEditor.css, 16 variants to migrate. All in `apps/illuminator/webui/src/components/`.\n\n   **ESLint Reference Read:**\n   - `~/.drift-semantic/skill/drift-guard/references/eslint-rule-patterns.md` — Reference for writing custom ESLint rules (flat config, inline plugins, no-restricted-imports, no-restricted-syntax, custom rule modules).\n\n   **Shared Infrastructure Read:**\n   - `packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/panel-utilities.css` — Already had `ilu-section`, `ilu-container`, `ilu-action-btn`, `ilu-empty`, `ilu-footer`, `ilu-warning-banner`, `ilu-error-banner`, `il