{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0128mCFqjmHPRCEZ91kVLQc6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to create an ESLint guard rule for this CSS cluster. The existing `no-panel-css-duplication` rule is close but covers a different set of patterns (section containers, action buttons, etc.). For this cluster, I need a rule that detects:\n\n1. CSS files that redeclare empty-state patterns (`text-align: center; color: var(--text-muted)`) when `ilu-empty` should be used\n2. CSS files that redeclare selection-bar patterns (`display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 12px 16px; background: var(--bg-secondary)`) when `ilu-selection-bar` should be used\n\n\n3. CSS files that redeclare stats-grid patterns when `ilu-stats-grid` should be used\n4. CSS files that redeclare thumb-cover patterns (`object-fit: cover; position: absolute`) when `ilu-thumb-cover` should be used\n\nI think extending the existing rule makes more sense than creating a new one, since they're both checking for CSS pattern duplication. I'll add these new patterns to the detection logic alongside the structural patterns it already handles. I'm realizing the existing rule's early exit condition would actually skip all the updated files since they now reference `ilu-` in their content, so I need to either create a new rule specifically for detecting new panel CSS duplication or refactor the existing one to handle both the old and new patterns properly. I'm realizing that detecting these patterns from JSX alone is tricky since there's no consistent way to identify what an empty state div or selection bar actually is. The CSS approach makes more sense — I can extend the existing rule to flag when a CSS file in the illuminator components folder redefines patterns that should be imported from panel-utilities instead.\n\nI'll update the `no-panel-css-duplication.js` rule to include the new CSS patterns from cluster 003 in the duplicated patterns list.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4487,"cache_read_input_tokens":74724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4487},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b5b64fd-02b5-4d0c-8463-5e560f74a8b2","uuid":"dcd6fcb5-1f1b-4f01-bbf5-de06478d60ec"}
