{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BJ836Ht8BdnC7AFxSCQYMc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. The card.css and editor.css are imported globally via the styles/index.css. The component CSS files are imported locally in their respective components.\n\nNow let me understand what needs to happen:\n\n1. **card.css**: Eliminate CE local copy. Move compact overrides to compact-overrides.css.\n2. **editor.css**: Eliminate CE local copy. Move compact overrides to compact-overrides.css.\n3. **Component CSS files**: Create a shared viewer utility CSS in shared-components and document the migration path.\n\nFor the card.css consolidation, I need to figure out exactly which properties differ and add those as compact overrides. \n\nNow I'm comparing the CE and shared-components versions rule by rule to identify which specific properties need to be overridden in compact-overrides.css. Still writing styles... Still writing styles... I'm comparing the CSS overrides between versions, looking at how the expandable card content differs in padding and background color, and noting which styles the CE version doesn't include. I need to preserve the `overflow: visible` property on those card elements since it's critical for allowing dropdowns to extend beyond the card boundaries, even though the SP version doesn't include it. Let me verify whether the SP card.css applies `overflow: hidden` to `.item-card` before finalizing the overrides. I need to override the SP's `overflow: hidden` with `overflow: visible` in the compact overrides. Let me add card and editor compact overrides to compact-overrides.css, remove those imports from index.css, and delete the CE local files. For the component CSS files themselves, I'm reconsidering whether to create a shared viewer-patterns.css or handle them differently since they're part of the coherence-engine app with component-prefixed class names and similar structural patterns.\n\nI think the best path is to create a shared viewer utility CSS with generic class names like `.viewer-section` and `.viewer-section-header`, wire it into shared-components/styles/index.css, and document this as a follow-up for JSX migration rather than changing the component files now. This lets new viewer components use the shared classes directly while existing ones migrate gradually, and the guard phase can enforce that new components use the shared utilities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7962,"cache_read_input_tokens":91901,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7962},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f674cf0-9f5a-4696-8008-0664523e53e2","uuid":"73337792-1268-4c2e-ba8b-277d047fca23"}
