{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WgxcTeDxfm5bgzbRDf161M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand the pattern here. The audit identified these 5 CSS files as having similarity (avg 0.42). Looking at them:\n\n1. **BulkChronicleAnnotationModal.css** (canonical) - `bcam-` prefix, list items, processing screen styles\n2. **ConfigPanel.css** - `cfgp-` prefix, hints, checkbox spacing, workers row, about text\n3. **CostsPanel.css** - `cpanel-` prefix, cost rows, section hints, clear button\n4. **IlluminatorTabContent.css** - `itc-` prefix, sync hints, sync actions, sync status\n\n\n5. **StyleSelector.css** - `stsel-` prefix, compact layout, grid, labels\n\nThe commonality across all of them is the reuse of certain styling patterns—muted text colors and small font sizes for hints and descriptive content, plus flex layouts with consistent gaps. However, these are really component-specific files with their own prefixed class names, so the similarity is just a natural consequence of following the same design system conventions rather than actual duplication.\n\nLooking at the overlap more closely, it's about 42% moderate similarity—the real shared element is just that muted hint text pattern showing up repeatedly across different components with slightly different class names but the same underlying styles.\n\nThe solution is to extract this common muted-text utility into the shared styles file, then replace all those repetitive declarations in each component file with a reference to it. Let me see what shared styles are already available to work with.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2784,"cache_read_input_tokens":51024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2784},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"par