{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013KRTmgwxxQPNPSp7uaVweJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * ConfigPanel - Model and API configuration\n     3→ *\n     4→ * Contains settings for:\n     5→ * - LLM call configuration (per-call model and thinking settings)\n     6→ * - Image model, size, and quality options\n     7→ * - Multishot prompting options\n     8→ * - Performance settings\n     9→ */\n    10→\n    11→import LLMCallConfigPanel from \"./LLMCallConfigPanel\";\n    12→import { LocalTextArea } from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\n    13→import { IMAGE_MODELS } from \"../lib/imageSettings\";\n    14→import \"./ConfigPanel.css\";\n    15→import React from \"react\";\n    16→import PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\n    17→\n    18→const DEFAULT_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = `Transform the structured prompt below into a single, coherent image prompt for {{modelName}}. Do NOT simply reformat—actively synthesize and reshape:\n    19→\n    20→Honor the VISUAL THESIS: This is the primary visual signal. The thesis describes the dominant silhouette feature that makes this entity instantly recognizable. Build the entire image around it.\n    21→\n    22→Synthesize, don't list:\n    23→- Merge SUBJECT + CONTEXT + CULTURAL IDENTITY into a unified visual\n    24→- Apply STYLE (artistic approach) and COMPOSITION (framing/perspective) to shape the rendering\n    25→- Translate SUPPORTING TRAITS into concrete visual details that reinforce the thesis\n    26→- Incorporate COLOR PALETTE if provided\n    27→\n    28→Establish clear composition and perspective:\n    29→- Honor the COMPOSITION directive for framing and vantage point\n    30→- Use environmental storytelling (objects, weathering, traces) to convey history\n    31→- The SETTING provides world context but the subject is the focus\n    32→\n    33→Create specific visual instructions: Rather than listing adjectives, use concrete visual language: \"weathered by decades of X,\" \"visible scars of Y,\" \"rendered in the style of Z\"\n    34→\n    35→Respect the AVOID list: These are hard constraints—elements that break the visual language.\n    36→\n    37→Condense to a single, authoritative prompt: Output should be 150-300 words, reading as clear artistic direction that could be handed to a concept artist—not a bulleted list.\n    38→{{globalImageRules}}\n    39→Original prompt:\n    40→{{prompt}}`;\n    41→\n    42→const DEFAULT_CHRONICLE_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = `Synthesize the structured prompt below into a single, coherent image prompt for {{modelName}}.\n    43→\n    44→The SCENE describes what to depict. Do not invent new elements or characters not in the scene.\n    45→\n    46→Apply the rendering directives:\n    47→- STYLE defines the artistic rendering approach — apply it to the entire image\n    48→- COLOR PALETTE defines the dominant color language — it overrides any colors the scene describes\n    49→- COMPOSITION defines framing, perspective, and spatial arrangement\n    50→\n    51→Maintain all SPECIES and AVOID constraints absolutely.\n    52→\n    53→Output 150-250 words of concrete visual direction. Write as unified artistic direction, not sections or lists.\n    54→{{globalImageRules}}\n    55→Original prompt:\n    56→{{prompt}}`;\n    57→\n    58→export default function ConfigPanel({ config, onConfigChange }) {\n    59→  const handleModelChange = (newModel) => {\n    60→    onConfigChange({ imageModel: newModel });\n    61→  };\n    62→\n    63→  return (\n    64→    <div>\n    65→      {/* LLM Call Configuration - per-call model and thinking settings */}\n    66→      <LLMCallConfigPanel />\n    67→\n    68→      <div className=\"illuminator-card\">\n    69→        <div className=\"illuminator-card-header\">\n    70→          <h2 className=\"illuminator-card-title\">Image Generation</h2>\n    71→        </div>\n    72→\n    73→        <div className=\"illuminator-form-group\">\n    74→          <label htmlFor=\"model-openai\" className=\"illuminator-label\">Model (OpenAI)</label>\n    75→          <select id=\"model-openai\"\n    76→            value={config.imageModel}\n    77→            onChange={(e) => handleModelChange(e.target.value)}\n    78→            className=\"illuminator-select\"\n    79→          >\n    80→            {IMAGE_MODELS.map((model) => (\n    81→              <option key={model.value} value={model.value}>\n    82→                {model.label}\n    83→              </option>\n    84→            ))}\n    85→          </select>\n    86→        </div>\n    87→\n    88→        <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n    89→          Size and quality settings are in the Image Settings panel (sidebar).\n    90→        </p>\n    91→      </div>\n    92→\n    93→      <div className=\"illuminator-card\">\n    94→        <div className=\"illuminator-card-header\">\n    95→          <h2 className=\"illuminator-card-title\">Multishot Prompting</h2>\n    96→        </div>\n    97→        <p className=\"cfgp-section-desc\">Improve image generation by chaining multiple AI calls.</p>\n    98→\n    99→        <div className=\"illuminator-checkbox-group cfgp-checkbox-spacer\">\n   100→          <input\n   101→            type=\"checkbox\"\n   102→            id=\"requireDescription\"\n   103→            checked={config.requireDescription || false}\n   104→            onChange={(e) => onConfigChange({ requireDescription: e.target.checked })}\n   105→            className=\"illuminator-checkbox\"\n   106→          />\n   107→          <label htmlFor=\"requireDescription\">Require description before image</label>\n   108→        </div>\n   109→        <p className=\"cfgp-checkbox-hint\">\n   110→          Enforces description generation before image generation. The description will be included\n   111→          in the image prompt.\n   112→        </p>\n   113→\n   114→        <div className=\"illuminator-checkbox-group cfgp-checkbox-spacer\">\n   115→          <input\n   116→            type=\"checkbox\"\n   117→            id=\"useClaudeForImagePrompt\"\n   118→            checked={config.useClaudeForImagePrompt || false}\n   119→            onChange={(e) => onConfigChange({ useClaudeForImagePrompt: e.target.checked })}\n   120→            className=\"illuminator-checkbox\"\n   121→          />\n   122→          <label htmlFor=\"useClaudeForImagePrompt\">Use Claude to format image prompt</label>\n   123→        </div>\n   124→        <p className=\"cfgp-checkbox-hint-tight\">\n   125→          Sends the image prompt through Claude first to optimize it for the image model.\n   126→        </p>\n   127→\n   128→        {config.useClaudeForImagePrompt && (\n   129→          <>\n   130→            <div className=\"illuminator-form-group cfgp-indented-group\">\n   131→              <label className=\"illuminator-label\">Global Image Rules\n   132→              <LocalTextArea\n   133→                value={config.globalImageRules || \"\"}\n   134→                onChange={(value) => onConfigChange({ globalImageRules: value })}\n   135→                className=\"illuminator-template-textarea\"\n   136→                placeholder=\"SPECIES RULE: This world contains only [species]. Any figures depicted must be explicitly described as [species], never as humans or generic figures.\"\n   137→                rows={4}\n   138→              />\n   139→              </label>\n   140→              <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n   141→                Domain-specific rules injected into all image prompts. Use this to enforce species,\n   142→                setting constraints, or other world-specific requirements.\n   143→              </p>\n   144→            </div>\n   145→            <div className=\"illuminator-form-group cfgp-indented-group\">\n   146→              <label className=\"illuminator-label\">Entity image prompt template\n   147→              <LocalTextArea\n   148→                value={config.claudeImagePromptTemplate || DEFAULT_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE}\n   149→                onChange={(value) => onConfigChange({ claudeImagePromptTemplate: value })}\n   150→                className=\"illuminator-template-textarea\"\n   151→                placeholder={DEFAULT_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE}\n   152→              />\n   153→              </label>\n   154→              <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n   155→                Used for entity portrait images. Use {\"{{modelName}}\"} for the image model name,{\" \"}\n   156→                {\"{{prompt}}\"} for the original prompt, and {\"{{globalImageRules}}\"} for the global\n   157→                rules above.\n   158→              </p>\n   159→            </div>\n   160→            <div className=\"illuminator-form-group cfgp-indented-group\">\n   161→              <label className=\"illuminator-label\">Chronicle image prompt template\n   162→              <LocalTextArea\n   163→                value={\n   164→                  config.claudeChronicleImagePromptTemplate ||\n   165→                  DEFAULT_CHRONICLE_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE\n   166→                }\n   167→                onChange={(value) => onConfigChange({ claudeChronicleImagePromptTemplate: value })}\n   168→                className=\"illuminator-template-textarea\"\n   169→                placeholder={DEFAULT_CHRONICLE_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE}\n   170→              />\n   171→              </label>\n   172→              <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n   173→                Used for chronicle cover and scene images. Use {\"{{modelName}}\"} for the image model\n   174→                name, {\"{{prompt}}\"} for the original prompt, and {\"{{globalImageRules}}\"} for the\n   175→                global rules above.\n   176→              </p>\n   177→            </div>\n   178→          </>\n   179→        )}\n   180→      </div>\n   181→\n   182→      <div className=\"illuminator-card\">\n   183→        <div className=\"illuminator-card-header\">\n   184→          <h2 className=\"illuminator-card-title\">Performance</h2>\n   185→        </div>\n   186→\n   187→        <div className=\"illuminator-form-group\">\n   188→          <span className=\"illuminator-label\">Parallel workers</span>\n   189→          <div className=\"cfgp-workers-row\">\n   190→            <input\n   191→              type=\"range\"\n   192→              min=\"1\"\n   193→              max=\"8\"\n   194→              value={config.numWorkers || 4}\n   195→              onChange={(e) => onConfigChange({ numWorkers: parseInt(e.target.value, 10) })}\n   196→              className=\"cfgp-range-input\"\n   197→            />\n   198→            <span className=\"cfgp-worker-count\">{config.numWorkers || 4}</span>\n   199→          </div>\n   200→          <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n   201→            Number of concurrent API calls. Higher = faster but may hit rate limits.\n   202→          </p>\n   203→        </div>\n   204→      </div>\n   205→\n   206→      <div className=\"illuminator-card\">\n   207→        <div className=\"illuminator-card-header\">\n   208→          <h2 className=\"illuminator-card-title\">About</h2>\n   209→        </div>\n   210→        <p className=\"cfgp-about-text\">\n   211→          Illuminator enriches your world simulation with LLM-generated content. Use the{\" \"}\n   212→          <strong>Entities</strong> tab to generate descriptions and images for entities. Use the{\" \"}\n   213→          <strong>Chronicle</strong> tab to generate multi-entity narratives and in-world documents.\n   214→        </p>\n   215→        <p className=\"cfgp-about-text-spaced\">\n   216→          All enrichments are saved automatically to your current world slot.\n   217→        </p>\n   218→      </div>\n   219→    </div>\n   220→  );\n   221→}\n   222→\n   223→ConfigPanel.propTypes = {\n   224→  config: PropTypes.object,\n   225→  onConfigChange: PropTypes.func,\n   226→};\n   227→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32340847-edea-48f0-bd01-a0b1ba1c9fbd","uuid":"fca17153-f4af-4c4d-af9c-60643e7580ae","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/apps/illuminator/webui/src/components/ConfigPanel.jsx","content":"/**\n * ConfigPanel - Model and API configuration\n *\n * Contains settings for:\n * - LLM call configuration (per-call model and thinking settings)\n * - Image model, size, and quality options\n * - Multishot prompting options\n * - Performance settings\n */\n\nimport LLMCallConfigPanel from \"./LLMCallConfigPanel\";\nimport { LocalTextArea } from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\nimport { IMAGE_MODELS } from \"../lib/imageSettings\";\nimport \"./ConfigPanel.css\";\nimport React from \"react\";\nimport PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\n\nconst DEFAULT_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = `Transform the structured prompt below into a single, coherent image prompt for {{modelName}}. Do NOT simply reformat—actively synthesize and reshape:\n\nHonor the VISUAL THESIS: This is the primary visual signal. The thesis describes the dominant silhouette feature that makes this entity instantly recognizable. Build the entire image around it.\n\nSynthesize, don't list:\n- Merge SUBJECT + CONTEXT + CULTURAL IDENTITY into a unified visual\n- Apply STYLE (artistic approach) and COMPOSITION (framing/perspective) to shape the rendering\n- Translate SUPPORTING TRAITS into concrete visual details that reinforce the thesis\n- Incorporate COLOR PALETTE if provided\n\nEstablish clear composition and perspective:\n- Honor the COMPOSITION directive for framing and vantage point\n- Use environmental storytelling (objects, weathering, traces) to convey history\n- The SETTING provides world context but the subject is the focus\n\nCreate specific visual instructions: Rather than listing adjectives, use concrete visual language: \"weathered by decades of X,\" \"visible scars of Y,\" \"rendered in the style of Z\"\n\nRespect the AVOID list: These are hard constraints—elements that break the visual language.\n\nCondense to a single, authoritative prompt: Output should be 150-300 words, reading as clear artistic direction that could be handed to a concept artist—not a bulleted list.\n{{globalImageRules}}\nOriginal prompt:\n{{prompt}}`;\n\nconst DEFAULT_CHRONICLE_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = `Synthesize the structured prompt below into a single, coherent image prompt for {{modelName}}.\n\nThe SCENE describes what to depict. Do not invent new elements or characters not in the scene.\n\nApply the rendering directives:\n- STYLE defines the artistic rendering approach — apply it to the entire image\n- COLOR PALETTE defines the dominant color language — it overrides any colors the scene describes\n- COMPOSITION defines framing, perspective, and spatial arrangement\n\nMaintain all SPECIES and AVOID constraints absolutely.\n\nOutput 150-250 words of concrete visual direction. Write as unified artistic direction, not sections or lists.\n{{globalImageRules}}\nOriginal prompt:\n{{prompt}}`;\n\nexport default function ConfigPanel({ config, onConfigChange }) {\n  const handleModelChange = (newModel) => {\n    onConfigChange({ imageModel: newModel });\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* LLM Call Configuration - per-call model and thinking settings */}\n      <LLMCallConfigPanel />\n\n      <div className=\"illuminator-card\">\n        <div className=\"illuminator-card-header\">\n          <h2 className=\"illuminator-card-title\">Image Generation</h2>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"illuminator-form-group\">\n          <label htmlFor=\"model-openai\" className=\"illuminator-label\">Model (OpenAI)</label>\n          <select id=\"model-openai\"\n            value={config.imageModel}\n            onChange={(e) => handleModelChange(e.target.value)}\n            className=\"illuminator-select\"\n          >\n            {IMAGE_MODELS.map((model) => (\n              <option key={model.value} value={model.value}>\n                {model.label}\n              </option>\n            ))}\n          </select>\n        </div>\n\n        <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n          Size and quality settings are in the Image Settings panel (sidebar).\n        </p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"illuminator-card\">\n        <div className=\"illuminator-card-header\">\n          <h2 className=\"illuminator-card-title\">Multishot Prompting</h2>\n        </div>\n        <p className=\"cfgp-section-desc\">Improve image generation by chaining multiple AI calls.</p>\n\n        <div className=\"illuminator-checkbox-group cfgp-checkbox-spacer\">\n          <input\n            type=\"checkbox\"\n            id=\"requireDescription\"\n            checked={config.requireDescription || false}\n            onChange={(e) => onConfigChange({ requireDescription: e.target.checked })}\n            className=\"illuminator-checkbox\"\n          />\n          <label htmlFor=\"requireDescription\">Require description before image</label>\n        </div>\n        <p className=\"cfgp-checkbox-hint\">\n          Enforces description generation before image generation. The description will be included\n          in the image prompt.\n        </p>\n\n        <div className=\"illuminator-checkbox-group cfgp-checkbox-spacer\">\n          <input\n            type=\"checkbox\"\n            id=\"useClaudeForImagePrompt\"\n            checked={config.useClaudeForImagePrompt || false}\n            onChange={(e) => onConfigChange({ useClaudeForImagePrompt: e.target.checked })}\n            className=\"illuminator-checkbox\"\n          />\n          <label htmlFor=\"useClaudeForImagePrompt\">Use Claude to format image prompt</label>\n        </div>\n        <p className=\"cfgp-checkbox-hint-tight\">\n          Sends the image prompt through Claude first to optimize it for the image model.\n        </p>\n\n        {config.useClaudeForImagePrompt && (\n          <>\n            <div className=\"illuminator-form-group cfgp-indented-group\">\n              <label className=\"illuminator-label\">Global Image Rules\n              <LocalTextArea\n                value={config.globalImageRules || \"\"}\n                onChange={(value) => onConfigChange({ globalImageRules: value })}\n                className=\"illuminator-template-textarea\"\n                placeholder=\"SPECIES RULE: This world contains only [species]. Any figures depicted must be explicitly described as [species], never as humans or generic figures.\"\n                rows={4}\n              />\n              </label>\n              <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n                Domain-specific rules injected into all image prompts. Use this to enforce species,\n                setting constraints, or other world-specific requirements.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"illuminator-form-group cfgp-indented-group\">\n              <label className=\"illuminator-label\">Entity image prompt template\n              <LocalTextArea\n                value={config.claudeImagePromptTemplate || DEFAULT_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE}\n                onChange={(value) => onConfigChange({ claudeImagePromptTemplate: value })}\n                className=\"illuminator-template-textarea\"\n                placeholder={DEFAULT_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE}\n              />\n              </label>\n              <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n                Used for entity portrait images. Use {\"{{modelName}}\"} for the image model name,{\" \"}\n                {\"{{prompt}}\"} for the original prompt, and {\"{{globalImageRules}}\"} for the global\n                rules above.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"illuminator-form-group cfgp-indented-group\">\n              <label className=\"illuminator-label\">Chronicle image prompt template\n              <LocalTextArea\n                value={\n                  config.claudeChronicleImagePromptTemplate ||\n                  DEFAULT_CHRONICLE_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE\n                }\n                onChange={(value) => onConfigChange({ claudeChronicleImagePromptTemplate: value })}\n                className=\"illuminator-template-textarea\"\n                placeholder={DEFAULT_CHRONICLE_IMAGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE}\n              />\n              </label>\n              <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n                Used for chronicle cover and scene images. Use {\"{{modelName}}\"} for the image model\n                name, {\"{{prompt}}\"} for the original prompt, and {\"{{globalImageRules}}\"} for the\n                global rules above.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n          </>\n        )}\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"illuminator-card\">\n        <div className=\"illuminator-card-header\">\n          <h2 className=\"illuminator-card-title\">Performance</h2>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"illuminator-form-group\">\n          <span className=\"illuminator-label\">Parallel workers</span>\n          <div className=\"cfgp-workers-row\">\n            <input\n              type=\"range\"\n              min=\"1\"\n              max=\"8\"\n              value={config.numWorkers || 4}\n              onChange={(e) => onConfigChange({ numWorkers: parseInt(e.target.value, 10) })}\n              className=\"cfgp-range-input\"\n            />\n            <span className=\"cfgp-worker-count\">{config.numWorkers || 4}</span>\n          </div>\n          <p className=\"cfgp-hint\">\n            Number of concurrent API calls. Higher = faster but may hit rate limits.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"illuminator-card\">\n        <div className=\"illuminator-card-header\">\n          <h2 className=\"illuminator-card-title\">About</h2>\n        </div>\n        <p className=\"cfgp-about-text\">\n          Illuminator enriches your world simulation with LLM-generated content. Use the{\" \"}\n          <strong>Entities</strong> tab to generate descriptions and images for entities. Use the{\" \"}\n          <strong>Chronicle</strong> tab to generate multi-entity narratives and in-world documents.\n        </p>\n        <p className=\"cfgp-about-text-spaced\">\n          All enrichments are saved automatically to your current world slot.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nConfigPanel.propTypes = {\n  config: PropTypes.object,\n  onConfigChange: PropTypes.func,\n};\n","numLines":227,"startLine":1,"totalLines":227}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0141C46yfWPzoceoa8VwvhGL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll update ConfigPanel. The duplicated patterns are:\n- `cfgp-hint`: `font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 4px` → `ilu-hint-sm` + keep `margin-top: 4px`\n- `cfgp-section-desc`: `font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 16px` → `ilu-hint` + keep `margin-bottom: 16px`\n- `cfgp-checkbox-hint`: `font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 16px; margin-left: 24px` → `ilu-hint-sm` + keep margins\n\n\n- `cfgp-checkbox-hint-tight`: same but with `margin-bottom: 12px` → `ilu-hint-sm` + keep margins\n- `cfgp-about-text`: `font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6` → `ilu-hint` + keep `line-height`\n- `cfgp-about-text-spaced`: same plus `margin-top: 12px` → `ilu-hint` + keep `line-height; margin-top`\n\nFor the JSX, I'll add `ilu-hint-sm` or `ilu-hint` classes alongside the existing styles.\n\nUpdating CSS to remove typography properties...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3264,"cache_read_input_tokens":77880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3264},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32340847-edea-48f0-bd01-a0b1ba1c9fbd","uuid":"694c6c69-a14d-4475-980c-2fec1a2a297f"}
