{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TYCWv8VqNLcuSeayEajEQ5","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→<!-- drift-generated -->\n     2→# CSS Architecture Pattern Guide\n     3→\n     4→**ADR:** [009-css-architecture-no-inline-styles](../adr/009-css-architecture-no-inline-styles.md)\n     5→**ESLint rule:** `local/no-inline-styles` (warn)\n     6→\n     7→## Quick Rules\n     8→\n     9→1. **No `style={{}}`** — all styling goes in `index.css` or component-scoped CSS\n    10→2. **Use utility classes** — `.flex-row`, `.mb-2`, `.ml-auto`, `.text-sm`, `.text-secondary`, etc.\n    11→3. **Use panel/metric/badge classes** — the design system provides `.panel`, `.metric-card`, `.badge`, etc.\n    12→4. **CSS custom properties** for theme tokens — never hardcode colors\n    13→\n    14→## Global Styles\n    15→\n    16→SVAP uses a single `index.css` for all styles. Views import no CSS files directly.\n    17→\n    18→| Section | Purpose |\n    19→|---------|---------|\n    20→| `:root` variables | Color tokens, spacing, typography |\n    21→| Layout classes | `.panel`, `.panel-header`, `.panel-body`, `.view-header` |\n    22→| Metric classes | `.metrics-row`, `.metric-card`, `.metric-label`, `.metric-value` |\n    23→| Data classes | `.data-table`, `.td-mono`, `.td-muted` |\n    24→| Utility classes | `.flex-row`, `.mb-2`, `.ml-auto`, `.font-semibold`, `.text-sm`, `.text-secondary`, `.cursor-pointer` |\n    25→| Component classes | `.badge`, `.btn`, `.error-banner`, `.stage-chip` |\n    26→\n    27→## Component Pattern\n    28→\n    29→```tsx\n    30→// Use existing CSS classes — no inline styles\n    31→export function SomeView() {\n    32→  return (\n    33→    <div className=\"panel stagger-in\">\n    34→      <div className=\"panel-header\">\n    35→        <h3>Title</h3>\n    36→        <button className=\"btn btn-accent\">Action</button>\n    37→      </div>\n    38→      <div className=\"panel-body\">\n    39→        <div className=\"flex-row\">\n    40→          <span className=\"font-semibold\">Label</span>\n    41→          <span className=\"text-secondary ml-auto\">Value</span>\n    42→        </div>\n    43→      </div>\n    44→    </div>\n    45→  );\n    46→}\n    47→```\n    48→\n    49→## Dynamic Values (Only Acceptable `style={}` Use)\n    50→\n    51→When a value is genuinely computed at runtime, use CSS custom properties:\n    52→\n    53→```tsx\n    54→{/* eslint-disable-next-line local/no-inline-styles -- dynamic width from data */}\n    55→<div className=\"bar-fill\" style={{ width: `${pct}%` }} />\n    56→```\n    57→\n    58→This is the **only** acceptable use of `style={}`. Add an `eslint-disable` comment.\n    59→\n    60→## Conditional Classes\n    61→\n    62→Use template literals for simple conditionals:\n    63→\n    64→```tsx\n    65→<div className={`panel ${isExpanded ? \"expanded\" : \"\"}`}>\n    66→<span className={`badge ${level}`}>{label}</span>\n    67→<span className={status === \"completed\" ? \"stage-chip completed\" : \"stage-chip\"}>\n    68→```\n    69→\n    70→## What NOT To Do\n    71→\n    72→```tsx\n    73→// BAD: inline style object\n    74→<div style={{ display: \"flex\", gap: \"8px\", padding: \"12px\" }}>\n    75→\n    76→// BAD: style variable\n    77→const boxStyle = { border: \"1px solid var(--border)\" };\n    78→<div style={boxStyle}>\n    79→\n    80→// GOOD: CSS class\n    81→<div className=\"flex-row\">\n    82→\n    83→// GOOD: utility class\n    84→<div className=\"mb-2 text-sm text-secondary\">\n    85→```\n    86→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63b294a3-cb88-4d6f-836a-2de3de08695c","uuid":"f205a428-95ce-4e37-b7b0-f9694a794a42","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/patterns/css-architecture.md","content":"<!-- drift-generated -->\n# CSS Architecture Pattern Guide\n\n**ADR:** [009-css-architecture-no-inline-styles](../adr/009-css-architecture-no-inline-styles.md)\n**ESLint rule:** `local/no-inline-styles` (warn)\n\n## Quick Rules\n\n1. **No `style={{}}`** — all styling goes in `index.css` or component-scoped CSS\n2. **Use utility classes** — `.flex-row`, `.mb-2`, `.ml-auto`, `.text-sm`, `.text-secondary`, etc.\n3. **Use panel/metric/badge classes** — the design system provides `.panel`, `.metric-card`, `.badge`, etc.\n4. **CSS custom properties** for theme tokens — never hardcode colors\n\n## Global Styles\n\nSVAP uses a single `index.css` for all styles. Views import no CSS files directly.\n\n| Section | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `:root` variables | Color tokens, spacing, typography |\n| Layout classes | `.panel`, `.panel-header`, `.panel-body`, `.view-header` |\n| Metric classes | `.metrics-row`, `.metric-card`, `.metric-label`, `.metric-value` |\n| Data classes | `.data-table`, `.td-mono`, `.td-muted` |\n| Utility classes | `.flex-row`, `.mb-2`, `.ml-auto`, `.font-semibold`, `.text-sm`, `.text-secondary`, `.cursor-pointer` |\n| Component classes | `.badge`, `.btn`, `.error-banner`, `.stage-chip` |\n\n## Component Pattern\n\n```tsx\n// Use existing CSS classes — no inline styles\nexport function SomeView() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"panel stagger-in\">\n      <div className=\"panel-header\">\n        <h3>Title</h3>\n        <button className=\"btn btn-accent\">Action</button>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"panel-body\">\n        <div className=\"flex-row\">\n          <span className=\"font-semibold\">Label</span>\n          <span className=\"text-secondary ml-auto\">Value</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Dynamic Values (Only Acceptable `style={}` Use)\n\nWhen a value is genuinely computed at runtime, use CSS custom properties:\n\n```tsx\n{/* eslint-disable-next-line local/no-inline-styles -- dynamic width from data */}\n<div className=\"bar-fill\" style={{ width: `${pct}%` }} />\n```\n\nThis is the **only** acceptable use of `style={}`. Add an `eslint-disable` comment.\n\n## Conditional Classes\n\nUse template literals for simple conditionals:\n\n```tsx\n<div className={`panel ${isExpanded ? \"expanded\" : \"\"}`}>\n<span className={`badge ${level}`}>{label}</span>\n<span className={status === \"completed\" ? \"stage-chip completed\" : \"stage-chip\"}>\n```\n\n## What NOT To Do\n\n```tsx\n// BAD: inline style object\n<div style={{ display: \"flex\", gap: \"8px\", padding: \"12px\" }}>\n\n// BAD: style variable\nconst boxStyle = { border: \"1px solid var(--border)\" };\n<div style={boxStyle}>\n\n// GOOD: CSS class\n<div className=\"flex-row\">\n\n// GOOD: utility class\n<div className=\"mb-2 text-sm text-secondary\">\n```\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
