{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RaWPBBNbhBZ1RBsTyLkyyS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"RelationshipStoryModal is another modal component in archivist — it probably uses a similar pattern and would benefit from the shared base. But the lint rule is currently too broad — it fires on ANY archivist component with a CSS import. This will produce false positives for components like `EntityDetail`, `FilterPanel`, `StatsPanel` etc. that have their own CSS but aren't content-section components.\n\nThe rule should be more targeted. Let me think about how to make it more precise. The current behavior is actually OK as a \"suggestion\" severity warning — it serves as a reminder for developers to consider whether their component should use the shared base. Components that genuinely don't need the base can add an `eslint-disable` comment.\n \nLooking at the actual component inventory, most of these are specialized views and panels — entity details, map views, timelines, stats, filters, menus, graph visualizations — that don't fit the content-section pattern. RelationshipStoryModal is the only one that might genuinely benefit from shared overlay patterns, but the rest are distinct enough that they shouldn't trigger the rule.\n\nThe real issue is that the rule fires on any archivist component with CSS imports, creating too many false positives. I need to be more selective — either by looking for CSS filenames that suggest content sections (keywords like \"Section\", \"Story\", \"Narrative\", \"Lore\") or by checking for specific structural patterns and custom properties that indicate a component is actually a content section or modal. Otherwise I'm going to flag components that have nothing to do with the shared section styling. I think the simplest solution is to just narrow the rule by checking if the imported CSS filename contains section-related keywords — that way it only triggers for actual section components and avoids the noise from existing archivist files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":120398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":343},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63b294a3-cb88-4d6f-836a-2de3de08695c","uuid":"d71d3e41-7fbe-4b8b-92c7-844a3d91f1bc"}
