{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HKwsodzpA7YnNjsmRLWPn5","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \"react\";\n     2→import PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\n     3→import \"./WorkspaceHeader.css\";\n     4→\n     5→export default function WorkspaceHeader({\n     6→  item,\n     7→  wordCount,\n     8→  isGenerating,\n     9→  isComplete,\n    10→  onAccept,\n    11→  onRegenerate,\n    12→  onExport,\n    13→  onUnpublish,\n    14→}) {\n    15→  const [menuOpen, setMenuOpen] = useState(false);\n    16→  const menuRef = useRef(null);\n    17→\n    18→  useEffect(() => {\n    19→    if (!menuOpen) return;\n    20→    const handleClick = (e) => {\n    21→      if (menuRef.current && !menuRef.current.contains(e.target)) setMenuOpen(false);\n    22→    };\n    23→    document.addEventListener(\"mousedown\", handleClick);\n    24→    return () => document.removeEventListener(\"mousedown\", handleClick);\n    25→  }, [menuOpen]);\n    26→\n    27→  return (\n    28→    <div className=\"chronicle-workspace-header\">\n    29→      <div className=\"chronicle-workspace-header-info\">\n    30→        <h3>{item.title || item.name || \"Untitled Chronicle\"}</h3>\n    31→        <div className=\"chronicle-workspace-header-stats\">\n    32→          {wordCount.toLocaleString()} words\n    33→          {item.selectionSummary && (\n    34→            <span>\n    35→              {\" \"}\n    36→              &middot; {item.selectionSummary.entityCount} entities,{\" \"}\n    37→              {item.selectionSummary.eventCount} events\n    38→            </span>\n    39→          )}\n    40→          {item.focusType && (\n    41→            <span> &middot; {item.focusType === \"single\" ? \"Single focus\" : \"Ensemble\"}</span>\n    42→          )}\n    43→          <span> &middot; sampling {item.generationSampling ?? \"unspecified\"}</span>\n    44→        </div>\n    45→      </div>\n    46→      <div className=\"chronicle-workspace-header-actions\">\n    47→        {!isComplete && onAccept && (\n    48→          <button onClick={onAccept} disabled={isGenerating} className=\"wsh-btn-accept\">\n    49→            Accept &#x2713;\n    50→          </button>\n    51→        )}\n    52→        {isComplete && onUnpublish && (\n    53→          <button\n    54→            onClick={onUnpublish}\n    55→            className=\"wsh-btn-unpublish\"\n    56→            title=\"Revert to assembly review without discarding content\"\n    57→          >\n    58→            Unpublish\n    59→          </button>\n    60→        )}\n    61→        <button onClick={onRegenerate} disabled={isGenerating} className=\"wsh-btn-regenerate\">\n    62→          &#x27F3; {isComplete ? \"Restart\" : \"Regenerate\"}\n    63→        </button>\n    64→        <div className=\"workspace-overflow-menu\" ref={menuRef}>\n    65→          <button onClick={() => setMenuOpen(!menuOpen)} className=\"wsh-btn-overflow\">\n    66→            &hellip;\n    67→          </button>\n    68→          {menuOpen && (\n    69→            <div className=\"workspace-overflow-dropdown\">\n    70→              {onExport && (\n    71→                <button\n    72→                  className=\"workspace-overflow-item\"\n    73→                  onClick={() => {\n    74→                    onExport();\n    75→                    setMenuOpen(false);\n    76→                  }}\n    77→                  title=\"Export chronicle with full generation context as JSON\"\n    78→                >\n    79→                  Export\n    80→                </button>\n    81→              )}\n    82→            </div>\n    83→          )}\n    84→        </div>\n    85→      </div>\n    86→    </div>\n    87→  );\n    88→}\n    89→\n    90→WorkspaceHeader.propTypes = {\n    91→  item: PropTypes.object,\n    92→  wordCount: PropTypes.oneOfType([PropTypes.string, PropTypes.number]),\n    93→  isGenerating: PropTypes.bool,\n    94→  isComplete: PropTypes.bool,\n    95→  onAccept: PropTypes.func,\n    96→  onRegenerate: PropTypes.func,\n    97→  onExport: PropTypes.func,\n    98→  onUnpublish: PropTypes.func,\n    99→};\n   100→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"012353ca-34db-4cb3-82b9-4cf23efde1ac","uuid":"5bd437a5-db10-4c7a-9327-dcde9ae2b92d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/apps/illuminator/webui/src/components/chronicle-workspace/WorkspaceHeader.jsx","content":"import React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \"react\";\nimport PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\nimport \"./WorkspaceHeader.css\";\n\nexport default function WorkspaceHeader({\n  item,\n  wordCount,\n  isGenerating,\n  isComplete,\n  onAccept,\n  onRegenerate,\n  onExport,\n  onUnpublish,\n}) {\n  const [menuOpen, setMenuOpen] = useState(false);\n  const menuRef = useRef(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!menuOpen) return;\n    const handleClick = (e) => {\n      if (menuRef.current && !menuRef.current.contains(e.target)) setMenuOpen(false);\n    };\n    document.addEventListener(\"mousedown\", handleClick);\n    return () => document.removeEventListener(\"mousedown\", handleClick);\n  }, [menuOpen]);\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"chronicle-workspace-header\">\n      <div className=\"chronicle-workspace-header-info\">\n        <h3>{item.title || item.name || \"Untitled Chronicle\"}</h3>\n        <div className=\"chronicle-workspace-header-stats\">\n          {wordCount.toLocaleString()} words\n          {item.selectionSummary && (\n            <span>\n              {\" \"}\n              &middot; {item.selectionSummary.entityCount} entities,{\" \"}\n              {item.selectionSummary.eventCount} events\n            </span>\n          )}\n          {item.focusType && (\n            <span> &middot; {item.focusType === \"single\" ? \"Single focus\" : \"Ensemble\"}</span>\n          )}\n          <span> &middot; sampling {item.generationSampling ?? \"unspecified\"}</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"chronicle-workspace-header-actions\">\n        {!isComplete && onAccept && (\n          <button onClick={onAccept} disabled={isGenerating} className=\"wsh-btn-accept\">\n            Accept &#x2713;\n          </button>\n        )}\n        {isComplete && onUnpublish && (\n          <button\n            onClick={onUnpublish}\n            className=\"wsh-btn-unpublish\"\n            title=\"Revert to assembly review without discarding content\"\n          >\n            Unpublish\n          </button>\n        )}\n        <button onClick={onRegenerate} disabled={isGenerating} className=\"wsh-btn-regenerate\">\n          &#x27F3; {isComplete ? \"Restart\" : \"Regenerate\"}\n        </button>\n        <div className=\"workspace-overflow-menu\" ref={menuRef}>\n          <button onClick={() => setMenuOpen(!menuOpen)} className=\"wsh-btn-overflow\">\n            &hellip;\n          </button>\n          {menuOpen && (\n            <div className=\"workspace-overflow-dropdown\">\n              {onExport && (\n                <button\n                  className=\"workspace-overflow-item\"\n                  onClick={() => {\n                    onExport();\n                    setMenuOpen(false);\n                  }}\n                  title=\"Export chronicle with full generation context as JSON\"\n                >\n                  Export\n                </button>\n              )}\n            </div>\n          )}\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nWorkspaceHeader.propTypes = {\n  item: PropTypes.object,\n  wordCount: PropTypes.oneOfType([PropTypes.string, PropTypes.number]),\n  isGenerating: PropTypes.bool,\n  isComplete: PropTypes.bool,\n  onAccept: PropTypes.func,\n  onRegenerate: PropTypes.func,\n  onExport: PropTypes.func,\n  onUnpublish: PropTypes.func,\n};\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":100}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GkHBbQTTGDNn5VvxFbhoGM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me analyze the shared patterns:\n\n**Pattern 1: Compact tertiary action button**\nUsed in all three files. The pattern is:\n```css\npadding: 4-8px 10-18px;\nfont-size: 11-13px;\nbackground: var(--bg-tertiary);\nborder: 1px solid var(--border-color);\nborder-radius: 6px;\ncolor: var(--text-secondary);\ncursor: pointer;\n```\nWith a disabled state: `cursor: not-allowed; opacity: 0.6;`\n\nThese buttons appear in toolbar/header contexts — they're \"compact action buttons\" that sit in a row alongside version selectors and status badges.\n\n\nI'm also seeing a green pill-shaped badge for active versions that uses a semi-transparent emerald background with matching text color and rounded corners, appearing in the version selector components. There's also a compact version select dropdown that auto-sizes based on content with a 12px font size.\n\nNow I'm noticing the shared button styles use different CSS variable names than what's in these component files—the shared styles reference `--color-bg-card` and `--color-border` while the components use `--bg-tertiary` and `--border-color`. I need to figure out if these are mapped to the same values or if they're distinct. Looking at the existing `.btn-secondary` class, it has standard padding of 10px 16px, but these components need a more compact variant with tighter spacing around 4-8px. plan:\n1. Add `.btn-compact` modifier to shared button.css (reduces size for toolbar contexts)\n2. Add `.badge-active-version` to shared badge.css (the green pill)  \n3. Don't create a shared select class — the selects are already using `.illuminator-select` with component-specific size overrides which is fine\n\nWait, I need to check the CSS variable names more carefully. The shared button.css uses `--color-bg-card`, `--color-border`, and `--color-text-muted`, but the components are using `--bg-tertiary`, `--border-color`, and `--text-secondary` — these are likely different tokens, so I should verify against the theme file.\n\nActually, looking at the ADR-004 and existing patterns, the cleaner approach is to use component-local CSS co-located with components, compose shared base classes with component-specific overrides, and extract the duplicated patterns into shared utilities. So I'll add `.btn-toolbar` to shared button.css for the compact tertiary buttons, add `.badge-active-version` to shared badge.css, and then update each component to use these shared classes instead of duplicating the rules.\n\nChecking the theme file now to verify the CSS variable mappings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6473,"cache_read_input_tokens":64701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6473},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"012353ca-34db-4cb3-82b9-4cf23efde1ac","uuid":"70257470-446d-4974-a587-5304d0d67e09"}
