olor: #a855f7;\n  --accent-hover: #c084fc;\n\n  /* Arctic theme variables */\n  --arctic-deep: #0a1929;\n  --arctic-dark: #1e3a5f;\n  --arctic-mid: #2d4a6f;\n  --arctic-ice: #3b82f6;\n  --arctic-frost: #60a5fa;\n  --arctic-light: #93c5fd;\n  --purple-accent: #a855f7;\n  --purple-dark: #9333ea;","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":3359}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DKSJ5bRqwaDintxw1P56Ep","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full picture. The illuminator app has its own theme variables (`--bg-tertiary`, `--border-color`, `--text-secondary`) that differ from the shared theme (`--color-bg-card`, `--color-border`, `--color-text-muted`). However, looking at the theme values:\n- `--bg-tertiary: #2d4a6f` vs `--color-bg-card: #1e3a5f` — different\n- `--border-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 30%)` vs `--color-border: rgb(59 130 246 / 30%)` — same!\n\n\n- `--text-secondary: #93c5fd` vs `--color-text-muted: #93c5fd` — same!\n\nSo two of the three variables already align with the shared theme, but `--bg-tertiary` stands apart. Since all three files live within the illuminator app, I should consolidate the shared toolbar patterns there by creating a new utilities file that uses illuminator's theme variables, then importing it across the three CSS files.\n\nLet me first check whether illuminator already has a styles directory set up.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2541,"cache_read_input_tokens":74258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2541},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"012353ca-34db-4cb3-82b9-4cf23efde1ac","uuid":"1d0a51b0-c0eb-45ce-8bc2-6d020dea6311"}
