{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DFfNDj19RWdiT1JZvTiSPR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No styles directory exists in illuminator. Let me reconsider the approach.\n\nLooking at the codebase patterns:\n- Shared styles live in `packages/shared-components/src/styles/`\n- Component-local CSS is co-located with each component\n- The illuminator's App.css defines the theme\n\nThe three files share:\n1. **Compact tertiary buttons** — could be added to `packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/button.css` as a new variant, but it would need to work with both the shared theme variables AND illuminator's theme variables\n2. **Active version badge** — could be added to `packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/badge.css`\n\n\n3. **Disabled button state** — already exists in shared button.css as `.btn:disabled`\n\nI'm noticing the theme variables overlap significantly. The illuminator's `--border-color` and shared `--color-border` both use `rgb(59 130 246 / 30%)`, and `--text-secondary` matches `--color-text-muted` at `#93c5fd`. The `--bg-tertiary: #2d4a6f` doesn't have a shared equivalent. Now I'm examining the shared button secondary styles to see how padding and other properties are structured.\n\nComparing the component buttons to the shared secondary button, the only real difference is the background color — `--bg-tertiary` versus `--color-bg-card`. Since I'm consolidating within the illuminator's own variables, I should stick with what's already defined there rather than mixing in shared theme values.\n\nLooking at the actual button patterns across the three components, I'm seeing a mix of compact tertiary buttons with varying padding, one primary accent button, and some unique states like the danger override for the delete confirmation. The tertiary buttons are mostly consistent, but the padding differs slightly between components.\n\nI think the best approach is to create a shared `.btn-toolbar` class in the common button styles that captures this compact tertiary pattern using the theme variables that map across all the apps—like using `--color-border` and `--color-text-muted` for consistency, and falling back to `--color-bg-card` for the background when needed.\n\nActually, I should check how other consolidations have been handled in this project to see if there's an established pattern I should follow.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":76799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":468},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"012353ca-34db-4cb3-82b9-4cf23efde1ac","uuid":"3e023e5c-8f78-41e0-b257-e3d3aee153a3"}
