{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EMzpcR8mYQ5PZc3azRTYnL","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * Panel utility classes — shared structural patterns for dense information panels.\n     3→ *\n     4→ * These classes extract the most commonly duplicated CSS patterns across\n     5→ * Illuminator panel/tab components. Components should compose these alongside\n     6→ * their prefixed component-specific classes.\n     7→ *\n     8→ * Usage:  className=\"ilu-section htab-section\"\n     9→ *   The ilu-* class provides the base structural pattern.\n    10→ *   The component-prefixed class adds/overrides unique properties.\n    11→ *\n    12→ * Canonical reference: apps/illuminator/webui/src/components/ActivityPanel.css\n    13→ * ADR: docs/adr/029-panel-css-utilities.md\n    14→ */\n    15→\n    16→/* ── Section card container ──\n    17→ * Padded container with bg-secondary, border, radius.\n    18→ * Used by: htab-section, pt-checklist, vtab-section, itab-cover-section,\n    19→ *          itab-compat-panel, enrtab-container, crv-refinements, crv-panel, etc.\n    20→ */\n    21→.ilu-section {\n    22→  padding: 16px;\n    23→  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n    24→  border-radius: 8px;\n    25→  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    26→}\n    27→\n    28→.ilu-section-title {\n    29→  font-size: 14px;\n    30→  font-weight: 600;\n    31→}\n    32→\n    33→.ilu-section-mb {\n    34→  margin-bottom: 16px;\n    35→}\n    36→\n    37→/* ── Overflow container ──\n    38→ * Container without padding, with overflow hidden. For containers that have\n    39→ * a separate header bar and body section.\n    40→ * Used by: crv-checks-panel, crp-synth, crp-acv, ref-tab-synth, ref-tab-fcv,\n    41→ *          ctab-viewer, ctab-summary-section, ctab-tertiary-section, etc.\n    42→ */\n    43→.ilu-container {\n    44→  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n    45→  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    46→  border-radius: 8px;\n    47→  overflow: hidden;\n    48→}\n    49→\n    50→/* ── Collapsible header bar ──\n    51→ * Header bar inside a container, with bg-tertiary background.\n    52→ * Used by: crp-synth-header, crp-acv-header, ref-tab-synth-header,\n    53→ *          ref-tab-fcv-header, ctab-viewer-toolbar, ctab-summary-header,\n    54→ *          vtab-report-header, etc.\n    55→ */\n    56→.ilu-container-header {\n    57→  padding: 12px 16px;\n    58→  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n    59→  display: flex;\n    60→  align-items: center;\n    61→}\n    62→\n    63→.ilu-container-header-bordered {\n    64→  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    65→}\n    66→\n    67→/* ── Action button ──\n    68→ * Standard action button with bg-tertiary, border, rounded.\n    69→ * Used by: cic-action-btn, enrtab-button, htab-annotate-btn, htab-prep-btn,\n    70→ *          htab-backport-btn, pt-refrow-btn, vtab-action-btn, vtab-regen-btn,\n    71→ *          events-panel-export-btn, events-panel-clear-filters-btn, etc.\n    72→ */\n    73→.ilu-action-btn {\n    74→  padding: 8px 14px;\n    75→  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n    76→  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    77→  border-radius: 6px;\n    78→  color: var(--text-secondary);\n    79→  font-size: 12px;\n    80→}\n    81→\n    82→.ilu-action-btn:not(:disabled) {\n    83→  cursor: pointer;\n    84→}\n    85→\n    86→.ilu-action-btn:disabled {\n    87→  cursor: not-allowed;\n    88→  opacity: 0.6;\n    89→}\n    90→\n    91→/* Smaller variant */\n    92→.ilu-action-btn-sm {\n    93→  padding: 6px 12px;\n    94→  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n    95→  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    96→  border-radius: 4px;\n    97→  color: var(--text-secondary);\n    98→  font-size: 12px;\n    99→}\n   100→\n   101→.ilu-action-btn-sm:not(:disabled) {\n   102→  cursor: pointer;\n   103→}\n   104→\n   105→.ilu-action-btn-sm:disabled {\n   106→  cursor: not-allowed;\n   107→  opacity: 0.6;\n   108→}\n   109→\n   110→/* ── Empty state ──\n   111→ * Centered empty state text.\n   112→ * Used by: ap-empty-state, cip-empty-state, events-panel-empty,\n   113→ *          crv-empty, dmw-empty-state, htab-empty, itab-empty, etc.\n   114→ */\n   115→.ilu-empty {\n   116→  font-size: 13px;\n   117→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   118→  padding: 24px;\n   119→  text-align: center;\n   120→}\n   121→\n   122→/* ── Footer actions row ──\n   123→ * Row of actions at the bottom of a dialog or panel.\n   124→ * Used by: bcm-footer, dmw-footer, cfr-footer.\n   125→ */\n   126→.ilu-footer {\n   127→  padding: 12px 20px;\n   128→  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n   129→  display: flex;\n   130→  justify-content: flex-end;\n   131→  gap: 8px;\n   132→  flex-shrink: 0;\n   133→}\n   134→\n   135→/* ── Warning banner ──\n   136→ * Amber-tinted warning banner.\n   137→ * Used by: pp-key-warning, itab-version-warning, crv-stale-warning.\n   138→ */\n   139→.ilu-warning-banner {\n   140→  padding: 12px 16px;\n   141→  background: rgb(245 158 11 / 10%);\n   142→  border: 1px solid rgb(245 158 11 / 30%);\n   143→  border-radius: 4px;\n   144→}\n   145→\n   146→/* ── Error banner ──\n   147→ * Red-tinted error banner.\n   148→ * Used by: cfr-error-banner, dmw-review-error, cip-error-message.\n   149→ */\n   150→.ilu-error-banner {\n   151→  padding: 8px 14px;\n   152→  background: rgb(239 68 68 / 10%);\n   153→  border-radius: 6px;\n   154→  border: 1px solid rgb(239 68 68 / 30%);\n   155→  font-size: 11px;\n   156→  color: #ef4444;\n   157→}\n   158→\n   159→/* ── Status colors ──\n   160→ * Inline status color utilities. Used pervasively across all panel CSS.\n   161→ */\n   162→.ilu-status-success { color: #10b981; }\n   163→.ilu-status-warning { color: #f59e0b; }\n   164→.ilu-status-error { color: #ef4444; }\n   165→\n   166→/* ── Footer button sizing ──\n   167→ * Standard footer button sizing for dialog footers.\n   168→ * Used by: bcm-footer-btn, rfm-footer-btn, dmw-footer-btn.\n   169→ */\n   170→.ilu-footer-btn {\n   171→  padding: 6px 16px;\n   172→  font-size: 12px;\n   173→}\n   174→\n   175→/* ── Section heading (uppercase label) ──\n   176→ * Small uppercase label for section headings within panels.\n   177→ * Used by: bcm-section-label, cfr-context-heading, cfr-field-label, etc.\n   178→ */\n   179→.ilu-section-label {\n   180→  font-size: 11px;\n   181→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   182→  text-transform: uppercase;\n   183→  font-weight: 600;\n   184→  letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n   185→}\n   186→\n   187→/* ── Selection bar ──\n   188→ * Sticky bar showing selected-item count with bulk actions.\n   189→ * Used by: eq-selection-bar, eb-selection-bar, rp-selection-bar.\n   190→ */\n   191→.ilu-selection-bar {\n   192→  display: flex;\n   193→  align-items: center;\n   194→  justify-content: space-between;\n   195→  padding: 12px 16px;\n   196→  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n   197→  border: 1px solid var(--accent-color);\n   198→  border-radius: 6px;\n   199→}\n   200→\n   201→/* ── Stats grid ──\n   202→ * Grid of stat cards with large values and muted labels.\n   203→ * Used by: tps-stats-grid, storage-panel-stats-grid, rp-stats-bar.\n   204→ */\n   205→.ilu-stats-grid {\n   206→  display: grid;\n   207→  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(100px, 1fr));\n   208→  gap: 12px;\n   209→  margin-bottom: 16px;\n   210→}\n   211→\n   212→.ilu-stat-card {\n   213→  padding: 10px;\n   214→  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n   215→  border-radius: 6px;\n   216→  text-align: center;\n   217→}\n   218→\n   219→.ilu-stat-value {\n   220→  font-size: 20px;\n   221→  font-weight: 600;\n   222→}\n   223→\n   224→.ilu-stat-label {\n   225→  font-size: 11px;\n   226→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   227→}\n   228→\n   229→/* ── Thumbnail cover image ──\n   230→ * Absolute-positioned image filling its container with cover fit.\n   231→ * Used by: cip-thumb-img, ipm-thumbnail-img, storage-panel-thumbnail-img.\n   232→ */\n   233→.ilu-thumb-cover {\n   234→  position: absolute;\n   235→  top: 0;\n   236→  left: 0;\n   237→  width: 100%;\n   238→  height: 100%;\n   239→  object-fit: cover;\n   240→}\n   241→\n   242→/* ── Muted hint text (12px) ──\n   243→ * Base muted description / hint text at standard size.\n   244→ * Compose with component-prefixed classes for spacing overrides.\n   245→ * Used by: cfgp-section-desc, cfgp-about-text, cpanel-section-hint,\n   246→ *          cpanel-empty-hint, itc-sync-hint, stsel-compact-label, stsel-label, etc.\n   247→ */\n   248→.ilu-hint {\n   249→  font-size: 12px;\n   250→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   251→}\n   252→\n   253→/* ── Muted hint text (11px) ──\n   254→ * Smaller muted text for secondary annotations, sub-hints, descriptions.\n   255→ * Used by: cfgp-hint, cfgp-checkbox-hint, bcam-chronicle-tone,\n   256→ *          itc-sync-summary, stsel-description, cpanel-clear-button, etc.\n   257→ */\n   258→.ilu-hint-sm {\n   259→  font-size: 11px;\n   260→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   261→}\n   262→\n   263→/* ── Thumbnail placeholder ──\n   264→ * Absolute-positioned centered placeholder for loading/missing thumbnails.\n   265→ * Used by: cip-thumb-loading, ipm-thumbnail-placeholder, storage-panel-thumbnail-placeholder.\n   266→ */\n   267→.ilu-thumb-placeholder {\n   268→  position: absolute;\n   269→  top: 0;\n   270→  left: 0;\n   271→  width: 100%;\n   272→  height: 100%;\n   273→  display: flex;\n   274→  align-items: center;\n   275→  justify-content: center;\n   276→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   277→  font-size: 11px;\n   278→}\n   279→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"012353ca-34db-4cb3-82b9-4cf23efde1ac","uuid":"3ee2b3c3-a0a4-4a07-afdd-3d03c829cf0a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/panel-utilities.css","content":"/**\n * Panel utility classes — shared structural patterns for dense information panels.\n *\n * These classes extract the most commonly duplicated CSS patterns across\n * Illuminator panel/tab components. Components should compose these alongside\n * their prefixed component-specific classes.\n *\n * Usage:  className=\"ilu-section htab-section\"\n *   The ilu-* class provides the base structural pattern.\n *   The component-prefixed class adds/overrides unique properties.\n *\n * Canonical reference: apps/illuminator/webui/src/components/ActivityPanel.css\n * ADR: docs/adr/029-panel-css-utilities.md\n */\n\n/* ── Section card container ──\n * Padded container with bg-secondary, border, radius.\n * Used by: htab-section, pt-checklist, vtab-section, itab-cover-section,\n *          itab-compat-panel, enrtab-container, crv-refinements, crv-panel, etc.\n */\n.ilu-section {\n  padding: 16px;\n  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n}\n\n.ilu-section-title {\n  font-size: 14px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.ilu-section-mb {\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n\n/* ── Overflow container ──\n * Container without padding, with overflow hidden. For containers that have\n * a separate header bar and body section.\n * Used by: crv-checks-panel, crp-synth, crp-acv, ref-tab-synth, ref-tab-fcv,\n *          ctab-viewer, ctab-summary-section, ctab-tertiary-section, etc.\n */\n.ilu-container {\n  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n/* ── Collapsible header bar ──\n * Header bar inside a container, with bg-tertiary background.\n * Used by: crp-synth-header, crp-acv-header, ref-tab-synth-header,\n *          ref-tab-fcv-header, ctab-viewer-toolbar, ctab-summary-header,\n *          vtab-report-header, etc.\n */\n.ilu-container-header {\n  padding: 12px 16px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n\n.ilu-container-header-bordered {\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n}\n\n/* ── Action button ──\n * Standard action button with bg-tertiary, border, rounded.\n * Used by: cic-action-btn, enrtab-button, htab-annotate-btn, htab-prep-btn,\n *          htab-backport-btn, pt-refrow-btn, vtab-action-btn, vtab-regen-btn,\n *          events-panel-export-btn, events-panel-clear-filters-btn, etc.\n */\n.ilu-action-btn {\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  color: var(--text-secondary);\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn:not(:disabled) {\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn:disabled {\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n}\n\n/* Smaller variant */\n.ilu-action-btn-sm {\n  padding: 6px 12px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  color: var(--text-secondary);\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn-sm:not(:disabled) {\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn-sm:disabled {\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n}\n\n/* ── Empty state ──\n * Centered empty state text.\n * Used by: ap-empty-state, cip-empty-state, events-panel-empty,\n *          crv-empty, dmw-empty-state, htab-empty, itab-empty, etc.\n */\n.ilu-empty {\n  font-size: 13px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  padding: 24px;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n/* ── Footer actions row ──\n * Row of actions at the bottom of a dialog or panel.\n * Used by: bcm-footer, dmw-footer, cfr-footer.\n */\n.ilu-footer {\n  padding: 12px 20px;\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: flex-end;\n  gap: 8px;\n  flex-shrink: 0;\n}\n\n/* ── Warning banner ──\n * Amber-tinted warning banner.\n * Used by: pp-key-warning, itab-version-warning, crv-stale-warning.\n */\n.ilu-warning-banner {\n  padding: 12px 16px;\n  background: rgb(245 158 11 / 10%);\n  border: 1px solid rgb(245 158 11 / 30%);\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n/* ── Error banner ──\n * Red-tinted error banner.\n * Used by: cfr-error-banner, dmw-review-error, cip-error-message.\n */\n.ilu-error-banner {\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  background: rgb(239 68 68 / 10%);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  border: 1px solid rgb(239 68 68 / 30%);\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: #ef4444;\n}\n\n/* ── Status colors ──\n * Inline status color utilities. Used pervasively across all panel CSS.\n */\n.ilu-status-success { color: #10b981; }\n.ilu-status-warning { color: #f59e0b; }\n.ilu-status-error { color: #ef4444; }\n\n/* ── Footer button sizing ──\n * Standard footer button sizing for dialog footers.\n * Used by: bcm-footer-btn, rfm-footer-btn, dmw-footer-btn.\n */\n.ilu-footer-btn {\n  padding: 6px 16px;\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n/* ── Section heading (uppercase label) ──\n * Small uppercase label for section headings within panels.\n * Used by: bcm-section-label, cfr-context-heading, cfr-field-label, etc.\n */\n.ilu-section-label {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n}\n\n/* ── Selection bar ──\n * Sticky bar showing selected-item count with bulk actions.\n * Used by: eq-selection-bar, eb-selection-bar, rp-selection-bar.\n */\n.ilu-selection-bar {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  padding: 12px 16px;\n  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--accent-color);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n}\n\n/* ── Stats grid ──\n * Grid of stat cards with large values and muted labels.\n * Used by: tps-stats-grid, storage-panel-stats-grid, rp-stats-bar.\n */\n.ilu-stats-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(100px, 1fr));\n  gap: 12px;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n\n.ilu-stat-card {\n  padding: 10px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.ilu-stat-value {\n  font-size: 20px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.ilu-stat-label {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n/* ── Thumbnail cover image ──\n * Absolute-positioned image filling its container with cover fit.\n * Used by: cip-thumb-img, ipm-thumbnail-img, storage-panel-thumbnail-img.\n */\n.ilu-thumb-cover {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 0;\n  left: 0;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  object-fit: cover;\n}\n\n/* ── Muted hint text (12px) ──\n * Base muted description / hint text at standard size.\n * Compose with component-prefixed classes for spacing overrides.\n * Used by: cfgp-section-desc, cfgp-about-text, cpanel-section-hint,\n *          cpanel-empty-hint, itc-sync-hint, stsel-compact-label, stsel-label, etc.\n */\n.ilu-hint {\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n/* ── Muted hint text (11px) ──\n * Smaller muted text for secondary annotations, sub-hints, descriptions.\n * Used by: cfgp-hint, cfgp-checkbox-hint, bcam-chronicle-tone,\n *          itc-sync-summary, stsel-description, cpanel-clear-button, etc.\n */\n.ilu-hint-sm {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n/* ── Thumbnail placeholder ──\n * Absolute-positioned centered placeholder for loading/missing thumbnails.\n * Used by: cip-thumb-loading, ipm-thumbnail-placeholder, storage-panel-thumbnail-placeholder.\n */\n.ilu-thumb-placeholder {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 0;\n  left: 0;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  font-size: 11px;\n}\n","numLines":279,"startLine":1,"totalLines":279}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YJtJSKzeRrFBHWgYPjnuFd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! There's already a `.ilu-action-btn` class in `panel-utilities.css` that's exactly the same pattern I was about to create! It's:\n\n```css\n.ilu-action-btn {\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  color: var(--text-secondary);\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn:not(:disabled) {\n  cursor: pointer;\n\n\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn:disabled {\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n}\n```\n\nAnd there's also `.ilu-action-btn-sm` with slightly smaller padding. So the shared infrastructure already exists! The three CSS files are duplicating what `.ilu-action-btn` already provides. I can consolidate by replacing `.hec-make-active-btn` and `.hec-export-btn` with the existing utility classes, adjusting padding with component overrides if needed.\n\nFor ChronicleVersionSelector, I'll map `.cvs-btn-make-active` to `ilu-action-btn-sm` since the padding matches, and `.cvs-btn-delete` can also use the small variant with just a transition override. The disabled states are already handled by the base utility.\n\nContinuing through the remaining component-specific styles to identify what truly needs to stay local versus what can leverage the shared button infrastructure. I found a status utility with green styling, but it's not quite the pill badge I need. Let me create a dedicated `.ilu-active-badge` class in the utilities stylesheet with the appropriate sizing, background, and rounded styling. Now I'm looking at the compact select pattern across both components—they share the same width, font size, and padding properties.\n\nSo my plan is to add two new utility classes to consolidate the duplicated styles: one for the active badge styling and another for the compact select inputs, then remove the redundant declarations from the HistorianEditionComparison stylesheet and have those components reference the new utilities instead. I need to check the padding differences between the button utilities—`.hec-make-active-btn` uses `4px 10px` while `.ilu-action-btn` has `8px 14px`, so I might need to use the smaller `.ilu-action-btn-sm` variant instead or create a component override for the HistorianEditionComparison buttons. I'm seeing that `.ilu-action-btn` at 8px 14px with 12px font aligns well with the WorkspaceHeader buttons, while `.ilu-action-btn-sm` at 6px 12px matches the CVS buttons. The HEC buttons are smaller still, so I'll use `.ilu-action-btn-sm` with a component-level override for the tighter padding and 11px font size rather than creating another variant.\n\nAdding CSS styles... Writing component styles... Still writing styles... Still writing component styles... I'm noticing a font-size mismatch — the old CVS button classes used 11px while the new `ilu-action-btn-sm` uses 12px, and I need to decide if that 1px difference matters for consistency across the different button systems. Still writing CSS overrides... select` and `.hec-compare-select` duplicate properties, keep only `min-width`\n\n**HistorianEditionComparison.tsx:**\n- Update className to compose shared + component classes\n\n**ChronicleVersionSelector.css:**\n- Remove button declarations except component-specific overrides\n- Remove `.cvs-active-badge` entirely\n- Remove select duplicate properties, keep only `min-width`\n- Remove `:disabled` states (covered by shared)\n\n**ChronicleVersionSelector.jsx:**\n- Update className to compose shared + component classes\n\n**WorkspaceHeader.css:**\n- `.wsh-btn-accept` — keep as-is (primary button, unique)\n- Remove `.wsh-btn-unpublish`, `.wsh-btn-regenerate`, `.wsh-btn-overflow` full declarations, keep only delta properties\n- Remove `:disabled` states (covered by shared)\n\n**WorkspaceHeader.jsx:**\n- Update className to compose shared + component classes\n\nNow I'll implement all these changes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5059,"cache_read_input_tokens":77267,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5059},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"012353ca-34db-4cb3-82b9-4cf23efde1ac","uuid":"303c788f-0192-4fb8-b289-102da19beb0b"}
