{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01U3HBzoP5b8VQPHMChasahp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the ESLint config structure. I need to:\n\n1. Create a custom ESLint rule that catches dashboard CSS class names with per-component section-spacer/section-label prefixes (the old pattern) in JSX files\n2. Wire it into the config\n\nThe rule should detect when someone uses a component-prefixed section class (e.g., `et-section-spacer`, `fd-section-label`, `xx-section-spacer`, `xx-section-label`) instead of the shared `lw-section-spacer` / `lw-section-label` classes.\n\nSince these classes are used in `className` string literals in JSX, I can write a rule that detects literal strings containing prefixed section-spacer/section-label patterns.\n\n\nLet me check how existing rules are structured to understand the pattern I should follow.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3346,"cache_read_input_tokens":83762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3346},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7d177e3-e480-46d9-92de-1155938b93f7","uuid":"251e1ca5-f736-469e-a445-9bb95b8cecb5"}
