{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018EwA73VLKFGGQstUBfJNfF","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * RelationshipKindEditor - Edit relationship kinds\n     3→ */\n     4→\n     5→import React, { useMemo, useState, useCallback } from \"react\";\n     6→import PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\n     7→import {\n     8→  ExpandableCard,\n     9→  FormGroup,\n    10→  SectionHeader,\n    11→  EmptyState,\n    12→} from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\n    13→import {\n    14→  ToolUsageBadges as UsageBadges,\n    15→  getRelationshipKindUsageSummary,\n    16→} from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\n    17→import \"./RelationshipKindEditor.css\";\n    18→\n    19→export default function RelationshipKindEditor({\n    20→  relationshipKinds,\n    21→  entityKinds,\n    22→  onChange,\n    23→  schemaUsage = {},\n    24→}) {\n    25→  const [expandedRels, setExpandedRels] = useState({});\n    26→\n    27→  const getStableKey = (rel) => rel._key || rel.kind;\n    28→\n    29→  const toggleRel = useCallback((stableKey) => {\n    30→    setExpandedRels((prev) => ({ ...prev, [stableKey]: !prev[stableKey] }));\n    31→  }, []);\n    32→\n    33→  const addRelationship = () => {\n    34→    const stableKey = `rel_${Date.now()}`;\n    35→    const newRel = {\n    36→      kind: stableKey,\n    37→      description: \"New Relationship\",\n    38→      srcKinds: [],\n    39→      dstKinds: [],\n    40→      cullable: true,\n    41→      decayRate: \"medium\",\n    42→      polarity: \"neutral\",\n    43→      _key: stableKey,\n    44→    };\n    45→    onChange([...relationshipKinds, newRel]);\n    46→    setExpandedRels((prev) => ({ ...prev, [stableKey]: true }));\n    47→  };\n    48→\n    49→  const updateRel = (relKind, updates) => {\n    50→    const existing = relationshipKinds.find((r) => r.kind === relKind);\n    51→    if (existing?.isFramework) return;\n    52→    onChange(relationshipKinds.map((r) => (r.kind === relKind ? { ...r, ...updates } : r)));\n    53→  };\n    54→\n    55→  const deleteRel = (relKind) => {\n    56→    const existing = relationshipKinds.find((r) => r.kind === relKind);\n    57→    if (existing?.isFramework) return;\n    58→    if (confirm(\"Delete this relationship kind?\")) {\n    59→      onChange(relationshipKinds.filter((r) => r.kind !== relKind));\n    60→    }\n    61→  };\n    62→\n    63→  const toggleEntityKind = (relKind, field, entityKindId) => {\n    64→    const rel = relationshipKinds.find((r) => r.kind === relKind);\n    65→    if (!rel || rel.isFramework) return;\n    66→    const current = rel[field] || [];\n    67→    const updated = current.includes(entityKindId)\n    68→      ? current.filter((k) => k !== entityKindId)\n    69→      : [...current, entityKindId];\n    70→    updateRel(relKind, { [field]: updated });\n    71→  };\n    72→\n    73→  const getSummary = (rel) => {\n    74→    const srcNames =\n    75→      rel.srcKinds?.length > 0\n    76→        ? rel.srcKinds\n    77→            .map((k) => entityKinds.find((ek) => ek.kind === k)?.description || k)\n    78→            .slice(0, 2)\n    79→        : [\"Any\"];\n    80→    const dstNames =\n    81→      rel.dstKinds?.length > 0\n    82→        ? rel.dstKinds\n    83→            .map((k) => entityKinds.find((ek) => ek.kind === k)?.description || k)\n    84→            .slice(0, 2)\n    85→        : [\"Any\"];\n    86→    return { srcNames, dstNames };\n    87→  };\n    88→\n    89→  const renderHeaderActions = () => (\n    90→    <button className=\"btn btn-primary\" onClick={addRelationship}>\n    91→      + Add Relationship\n    92→    </button>\n    93→  );\n    94→\n    95→  const renderRelationshipActions = (rel, srcNames, dstNames, isFramework) => (\n    96→    <>\n    97→      <UsageBadges usage={getRelationshipKindUsageSummary(schemaUsage, rel.kind)} compact />\n    98→      {isFramework && <span className=\"badge badge-info\">framework</span>}\n    99→      {rel.cullable === false && <span className=\"badge badge-info\">protected</span>}\n   100→      <div className=\"text-muted text-small rke-actions-flow\">\n   101→        {srcNames.map((name, i) => (\n   102→          <span key={i} className=\"badge\">\n   103→            {name}\n   104→          </span>\n   105→        ))}\n   106→        {rel.srcKinds?.length > 2 && <span>+{rel.srcKinds.length - 2}</span>}\n   107→        <span>→</span>\n   108→        {dstNames.map((name, i) => (\n   109→          <span key={i} className=\"badge\">\n   110→            {name}\n   111→          </span>\n   112→        ))}\n   113→        {rel.dstKinds?.length > 2 && <span>+{rel.dstKinds.length - 2}</span>}\n   114→      </div>\n   115→    </>\n   116→  );\n   117→\n   118→  return (\n   119→    <div className=\"editor-container rke-container\">\n   120→      <SectionHeader\n   121→        title=\"Relationship Kinds\"\n   122→        description=\"Define how entities can be connected to each other.\"\n   123→        count={relationshipKinds.length}\n   124→        actions={renderHeaderActions()}\n   125→      />\n   126→\n   127→      {relationshipKinds.length === 0 ? (\n   128→        <EmptyState\n   129→          icon=\"🔗\"\n   130→          title=\"No relationship kinds defined\"\n   131→          description=\"Add one to connect entities.\"\n   132→        />\n   133→      ) : (\n   134→        <div className=\"list-stack\">\n   135→          {relationshipKinds.map((rel) => {\n   136→            const stableKey = getStableKey(rel);\n   137→            const isExpanded = expandedRels[stableKey];\n   138→            const { srcNames, dstNames } = getSummary(rel);\n   139→            const isFramework = Boolean(rel.isFramework);\n   140→\n   141→            return (\n   142→              <ExpandableCard\n   143→                key={stableKey}\n   144→                expanded={isExpanded}\n   145→                onToggle={toggleRel}\n   146→                toggleId={stableKey}\n   147→                title={rel.description}\n   148→                subtitle={rel.kind}\n   149→                actions={renderRelationshipActions(rel, srcNames, dstNames, isFramework)}\n   150→              >\n   151→                {/* Display Name and Kind ID */}\n   152→                <div className=\"rke-name-row\">\n   153→                  <FormGroup label=\"Display Name\">\n   154→                    <input\n   155→                      className=\"input\"\n   156→                      value={rel.description}\n   157→                      disabled={isFramework}\n   158→                      onChange={(e) => updateRel(rel.kind, { description: e.target.value })}\n   159→                      placeholder=\"Relationship display name\"\n   160→                    />\n   161→                  </FormGroup>\n   162→                  <FormGroup label=\"Kind ID\">\n   163→                    <input\n   164→                      className=\"input\"\n   165→                      value={rel.kind}\n   166→                      disabled={isFramework}\n   167→                      onChange={(e) => {\n   168→                        const newKind = e.target.value.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9_]/g, \"\");\n   169→                        if (\n   170→                          newKind &&\n   171→                          !relationshipKinds.some((r) => r.kind === newKind && r.kind !== rel.kind)\n   172→                        ) {\n   173→                          updateRel(rel.kind, { kind: newKind });\n   174→                        }\n   175→                      }}\n   176→                      placeholder=\"relationship_kind_id\"\n   177→                    />\n   178→                  </FormGroup>\n   179→                </div>\n   180→\n   181→                {/* Entity Kind Constraints */}\n   182→                <div className=\"nested-section-compact\">\n   183→                  <div className=\"label rke-constraint-label\">\n   184→                    Entity Kind Constraints\n   185→                  </div>\n   186→                  {entityKinds.length === 0 ? (\n   187→                    <div className=\"text-muted text-small\">\n   188→                      Define entity kinds first to set constraints.\n   189→                    </div>\n   190→                  ) : (\n   191→                    <div className=\"rke-constraint-row\">\n   192→                      <div className=\"rke-constraint-col\">\n   193→                        <div className=\"rke-constraint-header\">\n   194→                          <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Source</span>\n   195→                          {rel.srcKinds?.length === 0 && (\n   196→                            <span className=\"text-muted text-small\">any</span>\n   197→                          )}\n   198→                        </div>\n   199→                        <div className=\"chip-list rke-chip-list-flush\">\n   200→                          {entityKinds.map((ek) => (\n   201→                            <div\n   202→                              key={ek.kind}\n   203→                              className={`chip chip-clickable ${rel.srcKinds?.includes(ek.kind) ? \"chip-active\" : \"\"} ${isFramework ? \"rke-chip-framework\" : \"\"}`}\n   204→                              onClick={() => toggleEntityKind(rel.kind, \"srcKinds\", ek.kind)}\n   205→                              role=\"button\"\n   206→                              tabIndex={0}\n   207→                              onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }}\n   208→                            >\n   209→                              {ek.description}\n   210→                            </div>\n   211→                          ))}\n   212→                        </div>\n   213→                      </div>\n   214→                      <div className=\"text-dim rke-arrow\">\n   215→                        →\n   216→                      </div>\n   217→                      <div className=\"rke-constraint-col\">\n   218→                        <div className=\"rke-constraint-header\">\n   219→                          <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Destination</span>\n   220→                          {rel.dstKinds?.length === 0 && (\n   221→                            <span className=\"text-muted text-small\">any</span>\n   222→                          )}\n   223→                        </div>\n   224→                        <div className=\"chip-list rke-chip-list-flush\">\n   225→                          {entityKinds.map((ek) => (\n   226→                            <div\n   227→                              key={ek.kind}\n   228→                              className={`chip chip-clickable ${rel.dstKinds?.includes(ek.kind) ? \"chip-active\" : \"\"} ${isFramework ? \"rke-chip-framework\" : \"\"}`}\n   229→                              onClick={() => toggleEntityKind(rel.kind, \"dstKinds\", ek.kind)}\n   230→                              role=\"button\"\n   231→                              tabIndex={0}\n   232→                              onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }}\n   233→                            >\n   234→                              {ek.description}\n   235→                            </div>\n   236→                          ))}\n   237→                        </div>\n   238→                      </div>\n   239→                    </div>\n   240→                  )}\n   241→                </div>\n   242→\n   243→                {/* Maintenance Settings */}\n   244→                <div className=\"nested-section-compact\">\n   245→                  <div className=\"label rke-maintenance-label\">\n   246→                    Maintenance Settings\n   247→                  </div>\n   248→                  <div className=\"rke-maintenance-row\">\n   249→                    <div className=\"rke-maintenance-field\">\n   250→                      <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Decay</span>\n   251→                      <select\n   252→                        className=\"input rke-select-compact\"\n   253→                        value={rel.decayRate || \"medium\"}\n   254→                        disabled={isFramework}\n   255→                        onChange={(e) => updateRel(rel.kind, { decayRate: e.target.value })}\n   256→                      >\n   257→                        <option value=\"none\">None</option>\n   258→                        <option value=\"slow\">Slow</option>\n   259→                        <option value=\"medium\">Medium</option>\n   260→                        <option value=\"fast\">Fast</option>\n   261→                      </select>\n   262→                    </div>\n   263→                    <div className=\"rke-maintenance-field\">\n   264→                      <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Polarity</span>\n   265→                      <select\n   266→                        className=\"input rke-select-compact\"\n   267→                        value={rel.polarity || \"neutral\"}\n   268→                        disabled={isFramework}\n   269→                        onChange={(e) => updateRel(rel.kind, { polarity: e.target.value })}\n   270→                        title=\"Affects narrative event types\"\n   271→                      >\n   272→                        <option value=\"positive\">Positive</option>\n   273→                        <option value=\"neutral\">Neutral</option>\n   274→                        <option value=\"negative\">Negative</option>\n   275→                      </select>\n   276→                    </div>\n   277→                    <label className=\"rke-cullable-label\">\n   278→                      <input\n   279→                        type=\"checkbox\"\n   280→                        checked={rel.cullable !== false}\n   281→                        disabled={isFramework}\n   282→                        onChange={(e) => updateRel(rel.kind, { cullable: e.target.checked })}\n   283→                        className=\"rke-checkbox\"\n   284→                      />\n   285→                      <span className=\"text-small\">Cullable</span>\n   286→                    </label>\n   287→                  </div>\n   288→                </div>\n   289→\n   290→                {/* Narrative Verbs */}\n   291→                <div className=\"nested-section-compact\">\n   292→                  <div className=\"label rke-verbs-label\">\n   293→                    Narrative Verbs\n   294→                  </div>\n   295→                  <div className=\"text-muted text-small rke-verbs-hint\">\n   296→                    Verbs used in narrative event descriptions when this relationship is formed or\n   297→                    ended.\n   298→                  </div>\n   299→                  <div className=\"rke-verbs-row\">\n   300→                    <FormGroup label=\"Formed\" className=\"rke-verb-form\">\n   301→                      <input\n   302→                        className=\"input\"\n   303→                        value={rel.verbs?.formed || \"\"}\n   304→                        disabled={isFramework}\n   305→                        onChange={(e) =>\n   306→                          updateRel(rel.kind, {\n   307→                            verbs: { ...rel.verbs, formed: e.target.value },\n   308→                          })\n   309→                        }\n   310→                        placeholder=\"e.g., joined, allied with\"\n   311→                      />\n   312→                    </FormGroup>\n   313→                    <FormGroup label=\"Ended\" className=\"rke-verb-form\">\n   314→                      <input\n   315→                        className=\"input\"\n   316→                        value={rel.verbs?.ended || \"\"}\n   317→                        disabled={isFramework}\n   318→                        onChange={(e) =>\n   319→                          updateRel(rel.kind, {\n   320→                            verbs: { ...rel.verbs, ended: e.target.value },\n   321→                          })\n   322→                        }\n   323→                        placeholder=\"e.g., left, broke ties with\"\n   324→                      />\n   325→                    </FormGroup>\n   326→                  </div>\n   327→                </div>\n   328→\n   329→                {/* Delete */}\n   330→                <div className=\"danger-zone\">\n   331→                  <button\n   332→                    className=\"btn btn-danger\"\n   333→                    onClick={() => deleteRel(rel.kind)}\n   334→                    disabled={isFramework}\n   335→                  >\n   336→                    Delete Relationship\n   337→                  </button>\n   338→                </div>\n   339→              </ExpandableCard>\n   340→            );\n   341→          })}\n   342→        </div>\n   343→      )}\n   344→    </div>\n   345→  );\n   346→}\n   347→\n   348→RelationshipKindEditor.propTypes = {\n   349→  relationshipKinds: PropTypes.array.isRequired,\n   350→  entityKinds: PropTypes.array.isRequired,\n   351→  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   352→  schemaUsage: PropTypes.object,\n   353→};\n   354→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"283869e4-8656-46fb-b084-649222114059","uuid":"b2cdfd37-d89c-4496-9280-3a6a8dd14d72","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/apps/canonry/webui/src/components/SchemaEditor/RelationshipKindEditor.jsx","content":"/**\n * RelationshipKindEditor - Edit relationship kinds\n */\n\nimport React, { useMemo, useState, useCallback } from \"react\";\nimport PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\nimport {\n  ExpandableCard,\n  FormGroup,\n  SectionHeader,\n  EmptyState,\n} from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\nimport {\n  ToolUsageBadges as UsageBadges,\n  getRelationshipKindUsageSummary,\n} from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\nimport \"./RelationshipKindEditor.css\";\n\nexport default function RelationshipKindEditor({\n  relationshipKinds,\n  entityKinds,\n  onChange,\n  schemaUsage = {},\n}) {\n  const [expandedRels, setExpandedRels] = useState({});\n\n  const getStableKey = (rel) => rel._key || rel.kind;\n\n  const toggleRel = useCallback((stableKey) => {\n    setExpandedRels((prev) => ({ ...prev, [stableKey]: !prev[stableKey] }));\n  }, []);\n\n  const addRelationship = () => {\n    const stableKey = `rel_${Date.now()}`;\n    const newRel = {\n      kind: stableKey,\n      description: \"New Relationship\",\n      srcKinds: [],\n      dstKinds: [],\n      cullable: true,\n      decayRate: \"medium\",\n      polarity: \"neutral\",\n      _key: stableKey,\n    };\n    onChange([...relationshipKinds, newRel]);\n    setExpandedRels((prev) => ({ ...prev, [stableKey]: true }));\n  };\n\n  const updateRel = (relKind, updates) => {\n    const existing = relationshipKinds.find((r) => r.kind === relKind);\n    if (existing?.isFramework) return;\n    onChange(relationshipKinds.map((r) => (r.kind === relKind ? { ...r, ...updates } : r)));\n  };\n\n  const deleteRel = (relKind) => {\n    const existing = relationshipKinds.find((r) => r.kind === relKind);\n    if (existing?.isFramework) return;\n    if (confirm(\"Delete this relationship kind?\")) {\n      onChange(relationshipKinds.filter((r) => r.kind !== relKind));\n    }\n  };\n\n  const toggleEntityKind = (relKind, field, entityKindId) => {\n    const rel = relationshipKinds.find((r) => r.kind === relKind);\n    if (!rel || rel.isFramework) return;\n    const current = rel[field] || [];\n    const updated = current.includes(entityKindId)\n      ? current.filter((k) => k !== entityKindId)\n      : [...current, entityKindId];\n    updateRel(relKind, { [field]: updated });\n  };\n\n  const getSummary = (rel) => {\n    const srcNames =\n      rel.srcKinds?.length > 0\n        ? rel.srcKinds\n            .map((k) => entityKinds.find((ek) => ek.kind === k)?.description || k)\n            .slice(0, 2)\n        : [\"Any\"];\n    const dstNames =\n      rel.dstKinds?.length > 0\n        ? rel.dstKinds\n            .map((k) => entityKinds.find((ek) => ek.kind === k)?.description || k)\n            .slice(0, 2)\n        : [\"Any\"];\n    return { srcNames, dstNames };\n  };\n\n  const renderHeaderActions = () => (\n    <button className=\"btn btn-primary\" onClick={addRelationship}>\n      + Add Relationship\n    </button>\n  );\n\n  const renderRelationshipActions = (rel, srcNames, dstNames, isFramework) => (\n    <>\n      <UsageBadges usage={getRelationshipKindUsageSummary(schemaUsage, rel.kind)} compact />\n      {isFramework && <span className=\"badge badge-info\">framework</span>}\n      {rel.cullable === false && <span className=\"badge badge-info\">protected</span>}\n      <div className=\"text-muted text-small rke-actions-flow\">\n        {srcNames.map((name, i) => (\n          <span key={i} className=\"badge\">\n            {name}\n          </span>\n        ))}\n        {rel.srcKinds?.length > 2 && <span>+{rel.srcKinds.length - 2}</span>}\n        <span>→</span>\n        {dstNames.map((name, i) => (\n          <span key={i} className=\"badge\">\n            {name}\n          </span>\n        ))}\n        {rel.dstKinds?.length > 2 && <span>+{rel.dstKinds.length - 2}</span>}\n      </div>\n    </>\n  );\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"editor-container rke-container\">\n      <SectionHeader\n        title=\"Relationship Kinds\"\n        description=\"Define how entities can be connected to each other.\"\n        count={relationshipKinds.length}\n        actions={renderHeaderActions()}\n      />\n\n      {relationshipKinds.length === 0 ? (\n        <EmptyState\n          icon=\"🔗\"\n          title=\"No relationship kinds defined\"\n          description=\"Add one to connect entities.\"\n        />\n      ) : (\n        <div className=\"list-stack\">\n          {relationshipKinds.map((rel) => {\n            const stableKey = getStableKey(rel);\n            const isExpanded = expandedRels[stableKey];\n            const { srcNames, dstNames } = getSummary(rel);\n            const isFramework = Boolean(rel.isFramework);\n\n            return (\n              <ExpandableCard\n                key={stableKey}\n                expanded={isExpanded}\n                onToggle={toggleRel}\n                toggleId={stableKey}\n                title={rel.description}\n                subtitle={rel.kind}\n                actions={renderRelationshipActions(rel, srcNames, dstNames, isFramework)}\n              >\n                {/* Display Name and Kind ID */}\n                <div className=\"rke-name-row\">\n                  <FormGroup label=\"Display Name\">\n                    <input\n                      className=\"input\"\n                      value={rel.description}\n                      disabled={isFramework}\n                      onChange={(e) => updateRel(rel.kind, { description: e.target.value })}\n                      placeholder=\"Relationship display name\"\n                    />\n                  </FormGroup>\n                  <FormGroup label=\"Kind ID\">\n                    <input\n                      className=\"input\"\n                      value={rel.kind}\n                      disabled={isFramework}\n                      onChange={(e) => {\n                        const newKind = e.target.value.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9_]/g, \"\");\n                        if (\n                          newKind &&\n                          !relationshipKinds.some((r) => r.kind === newKind && r.kind !== rel.kind)\n                        ) {\n                          updateRel(rel.kind, { kind: newKind });\n                        }\n                      }}\n                      placeholder=\"relationship_kind_id\"\n                    />\n                  </FormGroup>\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Entity Kind Constraints */}\n                <div className=\"nested-section-compact\">\n                  <div className=\"label rke-constraint-label\">\n                    Entity Kind Constraints\n                  </div>\n                  {entityKinds.length === 0 ? (\n                    <div className=\"text-muted text-small\">\n                      Define entity kinds first to set constraints.\n                    </div>\n                  ) : (\n                    <div className=\"rke-constraint-row\">\n                      <div className=\"rke-constraint-col\">\n                        <div className=\"rke-constraint-header\">\n                          <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Source</span>\n                          {rel.srcKinds?.length === 0 && (\n                            <span className=\"text-muted text-small\">any</span>\n                          )}\n                        </div>\n                        <div className=\"chip-list rke-chip-list-flush\">\n                          {entityKinds.map((ek) => (\n                            <div\n                              key={ek.kind}\n                              className={`chip chip-clickable ${rel.srcKinds?.includes(ek.kind) ? \"chip-active\" : \"\"} ${isFramework ? \"rke-chip-framework\" : \"\"}`}\n                              onClick={() => toggleEntityKind(rel.kind, \"srcKinds\", ek.kind)}\n                              role=\"button\"\n                              tabIndex={0}\n                              onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }}\n                            >\n                              {ek.description}\n                            </div>\n                          ))}\n                        </div>\n                      </div>\n                      <div className=\"text-dim rke-arrow\">\n                        →\n                      </div>\n                      <div className=\"rke-constraint-col\">\n                        <div className=\"rke-constraint-header\">\n                          <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Destination</span>\n                          {rel.dstKinds?.length === 0 && (\n                            <span className=\"text-muted text-small\">any</span>\n                          )}\n                        </div>\n                        <div className=\"chip-list rke-chip-list-flush\">\n                          {entityKinds.map((ek) => (\n                            <div\n                              key={ek.kind}\n                              className={`chip chip-clickable ${rel.dstKinds?.includes(ek.kind) ? \"chip-active\" : \"\"} ${isFramework ? \"rke-chip-framework\" : \"\"}`}\n                              onClick={() => toggleEntityKind(rel.kind, \"dstKinds\", ek.kind)}\n                              role=\"button\"\n                              tabIndex={0}\n                              onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }}\n                            >\n                              {ek.description}\n                            </div>\n                          ))}\n                        </div>\n                      </div>\n                    </div>\n                  )}\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Maintenance Settings */}\n                <div className=\"nested-section-compact\">\n                  <div className=\"label rke-maintenance-label\">\n                    Maintenance Settings\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"rke-maintenance-row\">\n                    <div className=\"rke-maintenance-field\">\n                      <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Decay</span>\n                      <select\n                        className=\"input rke-select-compact\"\n                        value={rel.decayRate || \"medium\"}\n                        disabled={isFramework}\n                        onChange={(e) => updateRel(rel.kind, { decayRate: e.target.value })}\n                      >\n                        <option value=\"none\">None</option>\n                        <option value=\"slow\">Slow</option>\n                        <option value=\"medium\">Medium</option>\n                        <option value=\"fast\">Fast</option>\n                      </select>\n                    </div>\n                    <div className=\"rke-maintenance-field\">\n                      <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Polarity</span>\n                      <select\n                        className=\"input rke-select-compact\"\n                        value={rel.polarity || \"neutral\"}\n                        disabled={isFramework}\n                        onChange={(e) => updateRel(rel.kind, { polarity: e.target.value })}\n                        title=\"Affects narrative event types\"\n                      >\n                        <option value=\"positive\">Positive</option>\n                        <option value=\"neutral\">Neutral</option>\n                        <option value=\"negative\">Negative</option>\n                      </select>\n                    </div>\n                    <label className=\"rke-cullable-label\">\n                      <input\n                        type=\"checkbox\"\n                        checked={rel.cullable !== false}\n                        disabled={isFramework}\n                        onChange={(e) => updateRel(rel.kind, { cullable: e.target.checked })}\n                        className=\"rke-checkbox\"\n                      />\n                      <span className=\"text-small\">Cullable</span>\n                    </label>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Narrative Verbs */}\n                <div className=\"nested-section-compact\">\n                  <div className=\"label rke-verbs-label\">\n                    Narrative Verbs\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"text-muted text-small rke-verbs-hint\">\n                    Verbs used in narrative event descriptions when this relationship is formed or\n                    ended.\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"rke-verbs-row\">\n                    <FormGroup label=\"Formed\" className=\"rke-verb-form\">\n                      <input\n                        className=\"input\"\n                        value={rel.verbs?.formed || \"\"}\n                        disabled={isFramework}\n                        onChange={(e) =>\n                          updateRel(rel.kind, {\n                            verbs: { ...rel.verbs, formed: e.target.value },\n                          })\n                        }\n                        placeholder=\"e.g., joined, allied with\"\n                      />\n                    </FormGroup>\n                    <FormGroup label=\"Ended\" className=\"rke-verb-form\">\n                      <input\n                        className=\"input\"\n                        value={rel.verbs?.ended || \"\"}\n                        disabled={isFramework}\n                        onChange={(e) =>\n                          updateRel(rel.kind, {\n                            verbs: { ...rel.verbs, ended: e.target.value },\n                          })\n                        }\n                        placeholder=\"e.g., left, broke ties with\"\n                      />\n                    </FormGroup>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Delete */}\n                <div className=\"danger-zone\">\n                  <button\n                    className=\"btn btn-danger\"\n                    onClick={() => deleteRel(rel.kind)}\n                    disabled={isFramework}\n                  >\n                    Delete Relationship\n                  </button>\n                </div>\n              </ExpandableCard>\n            );\n          })}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nRelationshipKindEditor.propTypes = {\n  relationshipKinds: PropTypes.array.isRequired,\n  entityKinds: PropTypes.array.isRequired,\n  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n  schemaUsage: PropTypes.object,\n};\n","numLines":354,"startLine":1,"totalLines":354}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Urt32aGB8mHkFTzARuyBQu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013BG9ZnT4jhHQJM7XBxW4cJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/apps/canonry/webui/src/components/SchemaEditor/TagRegistryEditor.jsx"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":54183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":573},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"283869e4-8656-46fb-b084-649222114059","uuid":"7afed9fa-f8f1-4bde-adb9-f0eade2e1780"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BG9ZnT4jhHQJM7XBxW4cJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * TagRegistryEditor - Edit tag registry (tags with metadata)\n     3→ *\n     4→ * This is the authoritative place to define tags.\n     5→ * Tags can be referenced by templates, regions, and profiles.\n     6→ */\n     7→\n     8→import React, { useState, useMemo, useEffect, useCallback } from \"react\";\n     9→import PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\n    10→import {\n    11→  ExpandableCard,\n    12→  SectionHeader,\n    13→  EmptyState,\n    14→  NumberInput,\n    15→} from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\n    16→import { ToolUsageBadges as UsageBadges } from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\n    17→import \"./TagRegistryEditor.css\";\n    18→\n    19→// Category colors (dynamic - keep as objects)\n    20→const CATEGORY_COLORS = {\n    21→  status: { bg: \"rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.2)\", color: \"#22c55e\" },\n    22→  trait: { bg: \"rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2)\", color: \"#3b82f6\" },\n    23→  affiliation: { bg: \"rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.2)\", color: \"#a855f7\" },\n    24→  behavior: { bg: \"rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.2)\", color: \"#f97316\" },\n    25→  theme: { bg: \"rgba(236, 72, 153, 0.2)\", color: \"#ec4899\" },\n    26→  location: { bg: \"rgba(20, 184, 166, 0.2)\", color: \"#14b8a6\" },\n    27→  system: { bg: \"rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2)\", color: \"#94a3b8\" },\n    28→};\n    29→\n    30→// Rarity colors (dynamic - keep as objects)\n    31→const RARITY_COLORS = {\n    32→  common: { bg: \"rgba(156, 163, 175, 0.2)\", color: \"#9ca3af\" },\n    33→  uncommon: { bg: \"rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.2)\", color: \"#22c55e\" },\n    34→  rare: { bg: \"rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2)\", color: \"#3b82f6\" },\n    35→  legendary: { bg: \"rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.2)\", color: \"#fbbf24\" },\n    36→};\n    37→\n    38→const CATEGORIES = [\"status\", \"trait\", \"affiliation\", \"behavior\", \"theme\", \"location\", \"system\"];\n    39→const RARITIES = [\"common\", \"uncommon\", \"rare\", \"legendary\"];\n    40→\n    41→// Separate component for tag ID input to prevent cursor jumping\n    42→function TagIdInput({ value, onChange, allTagIds, disabled }) {\n    43→  const [localValue, setLocalValue] = useState(value);\n    44→\n    45→  useEffect(() => {\n    46→    setLocalValue(value);\n    47→  }, [value]);\n    48→\n    49→  const handleChange = (e) => {\n    50→    const newId = e.target.value.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9_]/g, \"\");\n    51→    setLocalValue(newId);\n    52→  };\n    53→\n    54→  const handleBlur = () => {\n    55→    if (localValue && localValue !== value && !allTagIds.includes(localValue)) {\n    56→      onChange(localValue);\n    57→    } else if (!localValue || allTagIds.includes(localValue)) {\n    58→      setLocalValue(value);\n    59→    }\n    60→  };\n    61→\n    62→  return (\n    63→    <input\n    64→      className=\"input tre-monospace\"\n    65→      value={localValue}\n    66→      disabled={disabled}\n    67→      onChange={handleChange}\n    68→      onBlur={handleBlur}\n    69→      placeholder=\"tag_id\"\n    70→    />\n    71→  );\n    72→}\n    73→\n    74→export default function TagRegistryEditor({\n    75→  tagRegistry = [],\n    76→  entityKinds = [],\n    77→  onChange,\n    78→  tagUsage = {},\n    79→}) {\n    80→  const [expandedTags, setExpandedTags] = useState({});\n    81→  const [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState(\"\");\n    82→  const [categoryFilter, setCategoryFilter] = useState(\"all\");\n    83→  const [rarityFilter, setRarityFilter] = useState(\"all\");\n    84→\n    85→  // Compute stats\n    86→  const stats = useMemo(() => {\n    87→    const byCategory = {};\n    88→    const byRarity = {};\n    89→    CATEGORIES.forEach((c) => (byCategory[c] = 0));\n    90→    RARITIES.forEach((r) => (byRarity[r] = 0));\n    91→    tagRegistry.forEach((tag) => {\n    92→      byCategory[tag.category] = (byCategory[tag.category] || 0) + 1;\n    93→      byRarity[tag.rarity] = (byRarity[tag.rarity] || 0) + 1;\n    94→    });\n    95→    return { total: tagRegistry.length, byCategory, byRarity };\n    96→  }, [tagRegistry]);\n    97→\n    98→  // Filter tags\n    99→  const filteredTags = useMemo(() => {\n   100→    return tagRegistry.filter((tag) => {\n   101→      const matchesSearch =\n   102→        !searchQuery ||\n   103→        tag.tag.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase()) ||\n   104→        tag.description?.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase());\n   105→      const matchesCategory = categoryFilter === \"all\" || tag.category === categoryFilter;\n   106→      const matchesRarity = rarityFilter === \"all\" || tag.rarity === rarityFilter;\n   107→      return matchesSearch && matchesCategory && matchesRarity;\n   108→    });\n   109→  }, [tagRegistry, searchQuery, categoryFilter, rarityFilter]);\n   110→\n   111→  const toggleTag = useCallback((tagId) => {\n   112→    setExpandedTags((prev) => ({ ...prev, [tagId]: !prev[tagId] }));\n   113→  }, []);\n   114→\n   115→  const addTag = () => {\n   116→    const newTag = {\n   117→      tag: `new_tag_${Date.now()}`,\n   118→      category: \"trait\",\n   119→      rarity: \"common\",\n   120→      description: \"New tag description\",\n   121→      usageCount: 0,\n   122→      templates: [],\n   123→      entityKinds: [],\n   124→      minUsage: 1,\n   125→      maxUsage: 50,\n   126→      relatedTags: [],\n   127→      conflictingTags: [],\n   128→    };\n   129→    onChange([newTag, ...tagRegistry]);\n   130→    setExpandedTags((prev) => ({ ...prev, [newTag.tag]: true }));\n   131→  };\n   132→\n   133→  const updateTag = (tagId, updates) => {\n   134→    const existing = tagRegistry.find((t) => t.tag === tagId);\n   135→    if (existing?.isFramework) return;\n   136→    onChange(tagRegistry.map((t) => (t.tag === tagId ? { ...t, ...updates } : t)));\n   137→  };\n   138→\n   139→  const renderTagTitle = (tag) => <span className=\"tre-monospace\">{tag.tag}</span>;\n   140→\n   141→  const renderTagActions = (tag, catColor, rarColor, isFramework) => (\n   142→    <>\n   143→      <span className=\"badge tre-badge-dynamic\" style={{ '--tre-badge-bg': catColor.bg, '--tre-badge-color': catColor.color }}>\n   144→        {tag.category}\n   145→      </span>\n   146→      <span className=\"badge tre-badge-dynamic\" style={{ '--tre-badge-bg': rarColor.bg, '--tre-badge-color': rarColor.color }}>\n   147→        {tag.rarity}\n   148→      </span>\n   149→      {tag.isAxis && (\n   150→        <span\n   151→          className=\"badge tre-badge-dynamic\"\n   152→          style={{ '--tre-badge-bg': 'rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.2)', '--tre-badge-color': '#22d3ee' }}\n   153→        >\n   154→          ↔ axis\n   155→        </span>\n   156→      )}\n   157→      {isFramework && <span className=\"badge badge-info\">framework</span>}\n   158→      {tagUsage[tag.tag] && <UsageBadges usage={tagUsage[tag.tag]} compact />}\n   159→      <span className=\"text-muted text-small\">\n   160→        {tag.minUsage || 0}-{tag.maxUsage || \"∞\"} | {(tag.entityKinds || []).length} kinds\n   161→      </span>\n   162→    </>\n   163→  );\n   164→\n   165→  const deleteTag = (tagId) => {\n   166→    const existing = tagRegistry.find((t) => t.tag === tagId);\n   167→    if (existing?.isFramework) return;\n   168→    if (confirm(\"Delete this tag? This cannot be undone.\")) {\n   169→      onChange(tagRegistry.filter((t) => t.tag !== tagId));\n   170→    }\n   171→  };\n   172→\n   173→  // Related tags management\n   174→  const removeRelatedTag = (tagId, relatedTag) => {\n   175→    const tag = tagRegistry.find((t) => t.tag === tagId);\n   176→    if (!tag) return;\n   177→    updateTag(tagId, { relatedTags: (tag.relatedTags || []).filter((r) => r !== relatedTag) });\n   178→  };\n   179→\n   180→  // Conflicting tags management\n   181→  const removeConflictingTag = (tagId, conflictingTag) => {\n   182→    const tag = tagRegistry.find((t) => t.tag === tagId);\n   183→    if (!tag) return;\n   184→    updateTag(tagId, {\n   185→      conflictingTags: (tag.conflictingTags || []).filter((c) => c !== conflictingTag),\n   186→    });\n   187→  };\n   188→\n   189→  const allTagNames = useMemo(() => tagRegistry.map((t) => t.tag), [tagRegistry]);\n   190→\n   191→  const handleTagIdChange = (oldId, newId) => {\n   192→    const updatedRegistry = tagRegistry.map((t) => {\n   193→      if (t.tag === oldId) return { ...t, tag: newId };\n   194→      const updated = { ...t };\n   195→      if (t.relatedTags?.includes(oldId)) {\n   196→        updated.relatedTags = t.relatedTags.map((r) =>\n   197→          r === oldId ? newId : r\n   198→        );\n   199→      }\n   200→      if (t.conflictingTags?.includes(oldId)) {\n   201→        updated.conflictingTags = t.conflictingTags.map((c) =>\n   202→          c === oldId ? newId : c\n   203→        );\n   204→      }\n   205→      return updated;\n   206→    });\n   207→    setExpandedTags((prev) => {\n   208→      const updated = { ...prev };\n   209→      if (updated[oldId]) {\n   210→        updated[newId] = updated[oldId];\n   211→        delete updated[oldId];\n   212→      }\n   213→      return updated;\n   214→    });\n   215→    onChange(updatedRegistry);\n   216→  };\n   217→\n   218→  const handleEntityKindToggle = (tag, ek, isFramework) => {\n   219→    if (isFramework) return;\n   220→    const isSelected = (tag.entityKinds || []).includes(ek.kind);\n   221→    const current = tag.entityKinds || [];\n   222→    const updated = isSelected\n   223→      ? current.filter((k) => k !== ek.kind)\n   224→      : [...current, ek.kind];\n   225→    updateTag(tag.tag, { entityKinds: updated });\n   226→  };\n   227→\n   228→  return (\n   229→    <div className=\"editor-container tre-container\">\n   230→      <SectionHeader\n   231→        title=\"Tag Registry\"\n   232→        description=\"Define tags that categorize entities. Tags provide governance through usage limits, relationships, and conflicts.\"\n   233→      />\n   234→\n   235→      {/* Stats Bar - Compact */}\n   236→      <div className=\"tre-stats-bar\">\n   237→        <span className=\"text-small tre-stat-total\">\n   238→          <strong>{stats.total}</strong> tags\n   239→        </span>\n   240→        {CATEGORIES.filter((cat) => stats.byCategory[cat] > 0).map((cat) => (\n   241→          <span\n   242→            key={cat}\n   243→            className=\"text-small tre-stat-category\"\n   244→            style={{\n   245→              '--tre-stat-bg': CATEGORY_COLORS[cat].bg,\n   246→              '--tre-stat-color': CATEGORY_COLORS[cat].color,\n   247→            }}\n   248→          >\n   249→            {stats.byCategory[cat]} {cat}\n   250→          </span>\n   251→        ))}\n   252→      </div>\n   253→\n   254→      {/* Toolbar */}\n   255→      <div className=\"tre-toolbar\">\n   256→        <input\n   257→          className=\"input tre-search\"\n   258→          type=\"text\"\n   259→          placeholder=\"Search tags...\"\n   260→          value={searchQuery}\n   261→          onChange={(e) => setSearchQuery(e.target.value)}\n   262→        />\n   263→        <select\n   264→          className=\"input\"\n   265→          value={categoryFilter}\n   266→          onChange={(e) => setCategoryFilter(e.target.value)}\n   267→        >\n   268→          <option value=\"all\">All Categories</option>\n   269→          {CATEGORIES.map((cat) => (\n   270→            <option key={cat} value={cat}>\n   271→              {cat}\n   272→            </option>\n   273→          ))}\n   274→        </select>\n   275→        <select\n   276→          className=\"input\"\n   277→          value={rarityFilter}\n   278→          onChange={(e) => setRarityFilter(e.target.value)}\n   279→        >\n   280→          <option value=\"all\">All Rarities</option>\n   281→          {RARITIES.map((r) => (\n   282→            <option key={r} value={r}>\n   283→              {r}\n   284→            </option>\n   285→          ))}\n   286→        </select>\n   287→        <span className=\"text-muted\">\n   288→          {filteredTags.length} of {tagRegistry.length} tags\n   289→        </span>\n   290→        <button className=\"btn btn-primary\" onClick={addTag}>\n   291→          + Add Tag\n   292→        </button>\n   293→      </div>\n   294→\n   295→      {tagRegistry.length === 0 && (\n   296→        <EmptyState icon=\"🏷️\" title=\"No tags defined\" description=\"Add one to get started.\" />\n   297→      )}\n   298→      {tagRegistry.length > 0 && filteredTags.length === 0 && (\n   299→        <EmptyState icon=\"🔍\" title=\"No matches\" description=\"No tags match your filters.\" />\n   300→      )}\n   301→      {filteredTags.length > 0 && (\n   302→        <div className=\"list-stack\">\n   303→          {filteredTags.map((tag) => {\n   304→            const isExpanded = expandedTags[tag.tag];\n   305→            const catColor = CATEGORY_COLORS[tag.category] || CATEGORY_COLORS.trait;\n   306→            const rarColor = RARITY_COLORS[tag.rarity] || RARITY_COLORS.common;\n   307→            const isFramework = Boolean(tag.isFramework);\n   308→\n   309→            return (\n   310→              <ExpandableCard\n   311→                key={tag.tag}\n   312→                expanded={isExpanded}\n   313→                onToggle={toggleTag}\n   314→                toggleId={tag.tag}\n   315→                title={renderTagTitle(tag)}\n   316→                actions={renderTagActions(tag, catColor, rarColor, isFramework)}\n   317→              >\n   318→                {/* Basic Info Row */}\n   319→                <div className=\"tre-basic-row\">\n   320→                  <div className=\"tre-field-id\">\n   321→                    <div className=\"label tre-label-gap\">\n   322→                      Tag ID\n   323→                    </div>\n   324→                    <TagIdInput\n   325→                      value={tag.tag}\n   326→                      allTagIds={allTagNames.filter((t) => t !== tag.tag)}\n   327→                      disabled={isFramework}\n   328→                      onChange={(newId) => handleTagIdChange(tag.tag, newId)}\n   329→                    />\n   330→                  </div>\n   331→                  <div>\n   332→                    <div className=\"label tre-label-gap\">\n   333→                      Category\n   334→                    </div>\n   335→                    <select\n   336→                      className=\"input tre-select-compact\"\n   337→                      value={tag.category}\n   338→                      onChange={(e) => updateTag(tag.tag, { category: e.target.value })}\n   339→                      disabled={isFramework}\n   340→                    >\n   341→                      {CATEGORIES.map((cat) => (\n   342→                        <option key={cat} value={cat}>\n   343→                          {cat}\n   344→                        </option>\n   345→                      ))}\n   346→                    </select>\n   347→                  </div>\n   348→                  <div>\n   349→                    <div className=\"label tre-label-gap\">\n   350→                      Rarity\n   351→                    </div>\n   352→                    <select\n   353→                      className=\"input tre-select-compact\"\n   354→                      value={tag.rarity}\n   355→                      onChange={(e) => updateTag(tag.tag, { rarity: e.target.value })}\n   356→                      disabled={isFramework}\n   357→                    >\n   358→                      {RARITIES.map((r) => (\n   359→                        <option key={r} value={r}>\n   360→                          {r}\n   361→                        </option>\n   362→                      ))}\n   363→                    </select>\n   364→                  </div>\n   365→                  <div className=\"tre-axis-group\">\n   366→                    <label className=\"tre-axis-label\">\n   367→                      <input\n   368→                        type=\"checkbox\"\n   369→                        checked={tag.isAxis || false}\n   370→                        disabled={isFramework}\n   371→                        onChange={(e) => updateTag(tag.tag, { isAxis: e.target.checked })}\n   372→                        className=\"tre-checkbox\"\n   373→                      />\n   374→                      <span className=\"text-small\">Axis</span>\n   375→                    </label>\n   376→                  </div>\n   377→                </div>\n   378→\n   379→                {/* Description */}\n   380→                <div className=\"tre-description-wrapper\">\n   381→                  <textarea\n   382→                    className=\"input tre-textarea\"\n   383→                    value={tag.description || \"\"}\n   384→                    disabled={isFramework}\n   385→                    onChange={(e) => updateTag(tag.tag, { description: e.target.value })}\n   386→                    placeholder=\"Description...\"\n   387→                  />\n   388→                </div>\n   389→\n   390→                {/* Usage Limits - Compact inline */}\n   391→                <div className=\"tre-usage-row\">\n   392→                  <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Usage:</span>\n   393→                  <div className=\"tre-usage-inputs\">\n   394→                    <NumberInput\n   395→                      className=\"input tre-usage-number\"\n   396→                      min={0}\n   397→                      value={tag.minUsage || 0}\n   398→                      disabled={isFramework}\n   399→                      onChange={(v) => updateTag(tag.tag, { minUsage: v ?? 0 })}\n   400→                      integer\n   401→                    />\n   402→                    <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">–</span>\n   403→                    <NumberInput\n   404→                      className=\"input tre-usage-number\"\n   405→                      min={0}\n   406→                      value={tag.maxUsage || 50}\n   407→                      disabled={isFramework}\n   408→                      onChange={(v) => updateTag(tag.tag, { maxUsage: v ?? 50 })}\n   409→                      integer\n   410→                    />\n   411→                  </div>\n   412→                  <span className=\"text-small text-muted tre-merge-label\">\n   413→                    Merge →\n   414→                  </span>\n   415→                  <select\n   416→                    className=\"input tre-merge-select\"\n   417→                    value={tag.consolidateInto || \"\"}\n   418→                    disabled={isFramework}\n   419→                    onChange={(e) =>\n   420→                      updateTag(tag.tag, { consolidateInto: e.target.value || undefined })\n   421→                    }\n   422→                  >\n   423→                    <option value=\"\">none</option>\n   424→                    {allTagNames\n   425→                      .filter((t) => t !== tag.tag)\n   426→                      .map((t) => (\n   427→                        <option key={t} value={t}>\n   428→                          {t}\n   429→                        </option>\n   430→                      ))}\n   431→                  </select>\n   432→                </div>\n   433→\n   434→                {/* Consolidated Tag Relationships - 3 columns */}\n   435→                <div className=\"nested-section-compact\">\n   436→                  <div className=\"tre-grid-3col\">\n   437→                    {/* Entity Kinds */}\n   438→                    <div>\n   439→                      <div className=\"label tre-section-label\">\n   440→                        Applies to\n   441→                      </div>\n   442→                      <div className=\"chip-list tre-chip-section\">\n   443→                        {entityKinds.map((ek) => {\n   444→                          const isSelected = (tag.entityKinds || []).includes(ek.kind);\n   445→                          return (\n   446→                            <div\n   447→                              key={ek.kind}\n   448→                              className={`chip chip-clickable ${isSelected ? \"chip-active\" : \"\"} ${isFramework ? \"tre-chip-framework\" : \"tre-chip-compact\"}`}\n   449→                              onClick={() => handleEntityKindToggle(tag, ek, isFramework)}\n   450→                              role=\"button\"\n   451→                              tabIndex={0}\n   452→                              onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }}\n   453→                            >\n   454→                              {ek.description || ek.kind}\n   455→                            </div>\n   456→                          );\n   457→                        })}\n   458→                      </div>\n   459→                      {(tag.entityKinds || []).length === 0 && (\n   460→                        <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">all kinds</span>\n   461→                      )}\n   462→                    </div>\n   463→\n   464→                    {/* Related Tags */}\n   465→                    <div>\n   466→                      <div className=\"label tre-section-label\">\n   467→                        Related\n   468→                      </div>\n   469→                      <div className=\"chip-list tre-chip-section\">\n   470→                        {(tag.relatedTags || []).map((relatedTag) => (\n   471→                          <div\n   472→                            key={relatedTag}\n   473→                            className=\"chip tre-chip-compact\"\n   474→                          >\n   475→                            <span>{relatedTag}</span>\n   476→                            <button\n   477→                              className=\"chip-remove tre-chip-remove-sm\"\n   478→                              onClick={() => removeRelatedTag(tag.tag, relatedTag)}\n   479→                              disabled={isFramework}\n   480→                            >\n   481→                              ×\n   482→                            </button>\n   483→                          </div>\n   484→                        ))}\n   485→                        {!isFramework && (\n   486→                          <select\n   487→                            className=\"input tre-add-select\"\n   488→                            value=\"\"\n   489→                            onChange={(e) => {\n   490→                              if (e.target.value) {\n   491→                                const current = tag.relatedTags || [];\n   492→                                if (!current.includes(e.target.value)) {\n   493→                                  updateTag(tag.tag, { relatedTags: [...current, e.target.value] });\n   494→                                }\n   495→                              }\n   496→                            }}\n   497→                          >\n   498→                            <option value=\"\">+ add</option>\n   499→                            {allTagNames\n   500→                              .filter((t) => t !== tag.tag && !(tag.relatedTags || []).includes(t))\n   501→                              .map((t) => (\n   502→                                <option key={t} value={t}>\n   503→                                  {t}\n   504→                                </option>\n   505→                              ))}\n   506→                          </select>\n   507→                        )}\n   508→                      </div>\n   509→                    </div>\n   510→\n   511→                    {/* Conflicting Tags */}\n   512→                    <div>\n   513→                      <div className=\"label tre-conflicts-label\">\n   514→                        Conflicts\n   515→                      </div>\n   516→                      <div className=\"chip-list tre-chip-section\">\n   517→                        {(tag.conflictingTags || []).map((conflictingTag) => (\n   518→                          <div\n   519→                            key={conflictingTag}\n   520→                            className=\"chip tre-chip-conflict\"\n   521→                          >\n   522→                            <span>{conflictingTag}</span>\n   523→                            <button\n   524→                              className=\"chip-remove tre-chip-remove-sm\"\n   525→                              onClick={() => removeConflictingTag(tag.tag, conflictingTag)}\n   526→                              disabled={isFramework}\n   527→                            >\n   528→                              ×\n   529→                            </button>\n   530→                          </div>\n   531→                        ))}\n   532→                        {!isFramework && (\n   533→                          <select\n   534→                            className=\"input tre-add-select\"\n   535→                            value=\"\"\n   536→                            onChange={(e) => {\n   537→                              if (e.target.value) {\n   538→                                const current = tag.conflictingTags || [];\n   539→                                if (!current.includes(e.target.value)) {\n   540→                                  updateTag(tag.tag, {\n   541→                                    conflictingTags: [...current, e.target.value],\n   542→                                  });\n   543→                                }\n   544→                              }\n   545→                            }}\n   546→                          >\n   547→                            <option value=\"\">+ add</option>\n   548→                            {allTagNames\n   549→                              .filter(\n   550→                                (t) => t !== tag.tag && !(tag.conflictingTags || []).includes(t)\n   551→                              )\n   552→                              .map((t) => (\n   553→                                <option key={t} value={t}>\n   554→                                  {t}\n   555→                                </option>\n   556→                              ))}\n   557→                          </select>\n   558→                        )}\n   559→                      </div>\n   560→                    </div>\n   561→                  </div>\n   562→                </div>\n   563→\n   564→                {/* Delete */}\n   565→                <div className=\"danger-zone\">\n   566→                  <button\n   567→                    className=\"btn btn-danger\"\n   568→                    onClick={() => deleteTag(tag.tag)}\n   569→                    disabled={isFramework}\n   570→                  >\n   571→                    Delete Tag\n   572→                  </button>\n   573→                </div>\n   574→              </ExpandableCard>\n   575→            );\n   576→          })}\n   577→        </div>\n   578→      )}\n   579→    </div>\n   580→  );\n   581→}\n   582→\n   583→TagIdInput.propTypes = {\n   584→  value: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\n   585→  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   586→  allTagIds: PropTypes.arrayOf(PropTypes.string).isRequired,\n   587→  disabled: PropTypes.bool,\n   588→};\n   589→\n   590→TagRegistryEditor.propTypes = {\n   591→  tagRegistry: PropTypes.array,\n   592→  entityKinds: PropTypes.array,\n   593→  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   594→  tagUsage: PropTypes.object,\n   595→};\n   596→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"283869e4-8656-46fb-b084-649222114059","uuid":"dd63e62f-014c-48a7-8e3b-899912fa5d18","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/apps/canonry/webui/src/components/SchemaEditor/TagRegistryEditor.jsx","content":"/**\n * TagRegistryEditor - Edit tag registry (tags with metadata)\n *\n * This is the authoritative place to define tags.\n * Tags can be referenced by templates, regions, and profiles.\n */\n\nimport React, { useState, useMemo, useEffect, useCallback } from \"react\";\nimport PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\nimport {\n  ExpandableCard,\n  SectionHeader,\n  EmptyState,\n  NumberInput,\n} from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\nimport { ToolUsageBadges as UsageBadges } from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\nimport \"./TagRegistryEditor.css\";\n\n// Category colors (dynamic - keep as objects)\nconst CATEGORY_COLORS = {\n  status: { bg: \"rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.2)\", color: \"#22c55e\" },\n  trait: { bg: \"rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2)\", color: \"#3b82f6\" },\n  affiliation: { bg: \"rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.2)\", color: \"#a855f7\" },\n  behavior: { bg: \"rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.2)\", color: \"#f97316\" },\n  theme: { bg: \"rgba(236, 72, 153, 0.2)\", color: \"#ec4899\" },\n  location: { bg: \"rgba(20, 184, 166, 0.2)\", color: \"#14b8a6\" },\n  system: { bg: \"rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2)\", color: \"#94a3b8\" },\n};\n\n// Rarity colors (dynamic - keep as objects)\nconst RARITY_COLORS = {\n  common: { bg: \"rgba(156, 163, 175, 0.2)\", color: \"#9ca3af\" },\n  uncommon: { bg: \"rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.2)\", color: \"#22c55e\" },\n  rare: { bg: \"rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2)\", color: \"#3b82f6\" },\n  legendary: { bg: \"rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.2)\", color: \"#fbbf24\" },\n};\n\nconst CATEGORIES = [\"status\", \"trait\", \"affiliation\", \"behavior\", \"theme\", \"location\", \"system\"];\nconst RARITIES = [\"common\", \"uncommon\", \"rare\", \"legendary\"];\n\n// Separate component for tag ID input to prevent cursor jumping\nfunction TagIdInput({ value, onChange, allTagIds, disabled }) {\n  const [localValue, setLocalValue] = useState(value);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    setLocalValue(value);\n  }, [value]);\n\n  const handleChange = (e) => {\n    const newId = e.target.value.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9_]/g, \"\");\n    setLocalValue(newId);\n  };\n\n  const handleBlur = () => {\n    if (localValue && localValue !== value && !allTagIds.includes(localValue)) {\n      onChange(localValue);\n    } else if (!localValue || allTagIds.includes(localValue)) {\n      setLocalValue(value);\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <input\n      className=\"input tre-monospace\"\n      value={localValue}\n      disabled={disabled}\n      onChange={handleChange}\n      onBlur={handleBlur}\n      placeholder=\"tag_id\"\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nexport default function TagRegistryEditor({\n  tagRegistry = [],\n  entityKinds = [],\n  onChange,\n  tagUsage = {},\n}) {\n  const [expandedTags, setExpandedTags] = useState({});\n  const [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState(\"\");\n  const [categoryFilter, setCategoryFilter] = useState(\"all\");\n  const [rarityFilter, setRarityFilter] = useState(\"all\");\n\n  // Compute stats\n  const stats = useMemo(() => {\n    const byCategory = {};\n    const byRarity = {};\n    CATEGORIES.forEach((c) => (byCategory[c] = 0));\n    RARITIES.forEach((r) => (byRarity[r] = 0));\n    tagRegistry.forEach((tag) => {\n      byCategory[tag.category] = (byCategory[tag.category] || 0) + 1;\n      byRarity[tag.rarity] = (byRarity[tag.rarity] || 0) + 1;\n    });\n    return { total: tagRegistry.length, byCategory, byRarity };\n  }, [tagRegistry]);\n\n  // Filter tags\n  const filteredTags = useMemo(() => {\n    return tagRegistry.filter((tag) => {\n      const matchesSearch =\n        !searchQuery ||\n        tag.tag.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase()) ||\n        tag.description?.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase());\n      const matchesCategory = categoryFilter === \"all\" || tag.category === categoryFilter;\n      const matchesRarity = rarityFilter === \"all\" || tag.rarity === rarityFilter;\n      return matchesSearch && matchesCategory && matchesRarity;\n    });\n  }, [tagRegistry, searchQuery, categoryFilter, rarityFilter]);\n\n  const toggleTag = useCallback((tagId) => {\n    setExpandedTags((prev) => ({ ...prev, [tagId]: !prev[tagId] }));\n  }, []);\n\n  const addTag = () => {\n    const newTag = {\n      tag: `new_tag_${Date.now()}`,\n      category: \"trait\",\n      rarity: \"common\",\n      description: \"New tag description\",\n      usageCount: 0,\n      templates: [],\n      entityKinds: [],\n      minUsage: 1,\n      maxUsage: 50,\n      relatedTags: [],\n      conflictingTags: [],\n    };\n    onChange([newTag, ...tagRegistry]);\n    setExpandedTags((prev) => ({ ...prev, [newTag.tag]: true }));\n  };\n\n  const updateTag = (tagId, updates) => {\n    const existing = tagRegistry.find((t) => t.tag === tagId);\n    if (existing?.isFramework) return;\n    onChange(tagRegistry.map((t) => (t.tag === tagId ? { ...t, ...updates } : t)));\n  };\n\n  const renderTagTitle = (tag) => <span className=\"tre-monospace\">{tag.tag}</span>;\n\n  const renderTagActions = (tag, catColor, rarColor, isFramework) => (\n    <>\n      <span className=\"badge tre-badge-dynamic\" style={{ '--tre-badge-bg': catColor.bg, '--tre-badge-color': catColor.color }}>\n        {tag.category}\n      </span>\n      <span className=\"badge tre-badge-dynamic\" style={{ '--tre-badge-bg': rarColor.bg, '--tre-badge-color': rarColor.color }}>\n        {tag.rarity}\n      </span>\n      {tag.isAxis && (\n        <span\n          className=\"badge tre-badge-dynamic\"\n          style={{ '--tre-badge-bg': 'rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.2)', '--tre-badge-color': '#22d3ee' }}\n        >\n          ↔ axis\n        </span>\n      )}\n      {isFramework && <span className=\"badge badge-info\">framework</span>}\n      {tagUsage[tag.tag] && <UsageBadges usage={tagUsage[tag.tag]} compact />}\n      <span className=\"text-muted text-small\">\n        {tag.minUsage || 0}-{tag.maxUsage || \"∞\"} | {(tag.entityKinds || []).length} kinds\n      </span>\n    </>\n  );\n\n  const deleteTag = (tagId) => {\n    const existing = tagRegistry.find((t) => t.tag === tagId);\n    if (existing?.isFramework) return;\n    if (confirm(\"Delete this tag? This cannot be undone.\")) {\n      onChange(tagRegistry.filter((t) => t.tag !== tagId));\n    }\n  };\n\n  // Related tags management\n  const removeRelatedTag = (tagId, relatedTag) => {\n    const tag = tagRegistry.find((t) => t.tag === tagId);\n    if (!tag) return;\n    updateTag(tagId, { relatedTags: (tag.relatedTags || []).filter((r) => r !== relatedTag) });\n  };\n\n  // Conflicting tags management\n  const removeConflictingTag = (tagId, conflictingTag) => {\n    const tag = tagRegistry.find((t) => t.tag === tagId);\n    if (!tag) return;\n    updateTag(tagId, {\n      conflictingTags: (tag.conflictingTags || []).filter((c) => c !== conflictingTag),\n    });\n  };\n\n  const allTagNames = useMemo(() => tagRegistry.map((t) => t.tag), [tagRegistry]);\n\n  const handleTagIdChange = (oldId, newId) => {\n    const updatedRegistry = tagRegistry.map((t) => {\n      if (t.tag === oldId) return { ...t, tag: newId };\n      const updated = { ...t };\n      if (t.relatedTags?.includes(oldId)) {\n        updated.relatedTags = t.relatedTags.map((r) =>\n          r === oldId ? newId : r\n        );\n      }\n      if (t.conflictingTags?.includes(oldId)) {\n        updated.conflictingTags = t.conflictingTags.map((c) =>\n          c === oldId ? newId : c\n        );\n      }\n      return updated;\n    });\n    setExpandedTags((prev) => {\n      const updated = { ...prev };\n      if (updated[oldId]) {\n        updated[newId] = updated[oldId];\n        delete updated[oldId];\n      }\n      return updated;\n    });\n    onChange(updatedRegistry);\n  };\n\n  const handleEntityKindToggle = (tag, ek, isFramework) => {\n    if (isFramework) return;\n    const isSelected = (tag.entityKinds || []).includes(ek.kind);\n    const current = tag.entityKinds || [];\n    const updated = isSelected\n      ? current.filter((k) => k !== ek.kind)\n      : [...current, ek.kind];\n    updateTag(tag.tag, { entityKinds: updated });\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"editor-container tre-container\">\n      <SectionHeader\n        title=\"Tag Registry\"\n        description=\"Define tags that categorize entities. Tags provide governance through usage limits, relationships, and conflicts.\"\n      />\n\n      {/* Stats Bar - Compact */}\n      <div className=\"tre-stats-bar\">\n        <span className=\"text-small tre-stat-total\">\n          <strong>{stats.total}</strong> tags\n        </span>\n        {CATEGORIES.filter((cat) => stats.byCategory[cat] > 0).map((cat) => (\n          <span\n            key={cat}\n            className=\"text-small tre-stat-category\"\n            style={{\n              '--tre-stat-bg': CATEGORY_COLORS[cat].bg,\n              '--tre-stat-color': CATEGORY_COLORS[cat].color,\n            }}\n          >\n            {stats.byCategory[cat]} {cat}\n          </span>\n        ))}\n      </div>\n\n      {/* Toolbar */}\n      <div className=\"tre-toolbar\">\n        <input\n          className=\"input tre-search\"\n          type=\"text\"\n          placeholder=\"Search tags...\"\n          value={searchQuery}\n          onChange={(e) => setSearchQuery(e.target.value)}\n        />\n        <select\n          className=\"input\"\n          value={categoryFilter}\n          onChange={(e) => setCategoryFilter(e.target.value)}\n        >\n          <option value=\"all\">All Categories</option>\n          {CATEGORIES.map((cat) => (\n            <option key={cat} value={cat}>\n              {cat}\n            </option>\n          ))}\n        </select>\n        <select\n          className=\"input\"\n          value={rarityFilter}\n          onChange={(e) => setRarityFilter(e.target.value)}\n        >\n          <option value=\"all\">All Rarities</option>\n          {RARITIES.map((r) => (\n            <option key={r} value={r}>\n              {r}\n            </option>\n          ))}\n        </select>\n        <span className=\"text-muted\">\n          {filteredTags.length} of {tagRegistry.length} tags\n        </span>\n        <button className=\"btn btn-primary\" onClick={addTag}>\n          + Add Tag\n        </button>\n      </div>\n\n      {tagRegistry.length === 0 && (\n        <EmptyState icon=\"🏷️\" title=\"No tags defined\" description=\"Add one to get started.\" />\n      )}\n      {tagRegistry.length > 0 && filteredTags.length === 0 && (\n        <EmptyState icon=\"🔍\" title=\"No matches\" description=\"No tags match your filters.\" />\n      )}\n      {filteredTags.length > 0 && (\n        <div className=\"list-stack\">\n          {filteredTags.map((tag) => {\n            const isExpanded = expandedTags[tag.tag];\n            const catColor = CATEGORY_COLORS[tag.category] || CATEGORY_COLORS.trait;\n            const rarColor = RARITY_COLORS[tag.rarity] || RARITY_COLORS.common;\n            const isFramework = Boolean(tag.isFramework);\n\n            return (\n              <ExpandableCard\n                key={tag.tag}\n                expanded={isExpanded}\n                onToggle={toggleTag}\n                toggleId={tag.tag}\n                title={renderTagTitle(tag)}\n                actions={renderTagActions(tag, catColor, rarColor, isFramework)}\n              >\n                {/* Basic Info Row */}\n                <div className=\"tre-basic-row\">\n                  <div className=\"tre-field-id\">\n                    <div className=\"label tre-label-gap\">\n                      Tag ID\n                    </div>\n                    <TagIdInput\n                      value={tag.tag}\n                      allTagIds={allTagNames.filter((t) => t !== tag.tag)}\n                      disabled={isFramework}\n                      onChange={(newId) => handleTagIdChange(tag.tag, newId)}\n                    />\n                  </div>\n                  <div>\n                    <div className=\"label tre-label-gap\">\n                      Category\n                    </div>\n                    <select\n                      className=\"input tre-select-compact\"\n                      value={tag.category}\n                      onChange={(e) => updateTag(tag.tag, { category: e.target.value })}\n                      disabled={isFramework}\n                    >\n                      {CATEGORIES.map((cat) => (\n                        <option key={cat} value={cat}>\n                          {cat}\n                        </option>\n                      ))}\n                    </select>\n                  </div>\n                  <div>\n                    <div className=\"label tre-label-gap\">\n                      Rarity\n                    </div>\n                    <select\n                      className=\"input tre-select-compact\"\n                      value={tag.rarity}\n                      onChange={(e) => updateTag(tag.tag, { rarity: e.target.value })}\n                      disabled={isFramework}\n                    >\n                      {RARITIES.map((r) => (\n                        <option key={r} value={r}>\n                          {r}\n                        </option>\n                      ))}\n                    </select>\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"tre-axis-group\">\n                    <label className=\"tre-axis-label\">\n                      <input\n                        type=\"checkbox\"\n                        checked={tag.isAxis || false}\n                        disabled={isFramework}\n                        onChange={(e) => updateTag(tag.tag, { isAxis: e.target.checked })}\n                        className=\"tre-checkbox\"\n                      />\n                      <span className=\"text-small\">Axis</span>\n                    </label>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Description */}\n                <div className=\"tre-description-wrapper\">\n                  <textarea\n                    className=\"input tre-textarea\"\n                    value={tag.description || \"\"}\n                    disabled={isFramework}\n                    onChange={(e) => updateTag(tag.tag, { description: e.target.value })}\n                    placeholder=\"Description...\"\n                  />\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Usage Limits - Compact inline */}\n                <div className=\"tre-usage-row\">\n                  <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">Usage:</span>\n                  <div className=\"tre-usage-inputs\">\n                    <NumberInput\n                      className=\"input tre-usage-number\"\n                      min={0}\n                      value={tag.minUsage || 0}\n                      disabled={isFramework}\n                      onChange={(v) => updateTag(tag.tag, { minUsage: v ?? 0 })}\n                      integer\n                    />\n                    <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">–</span>\n                    <NumberInput\n                      className=\"input tre-usage-number\"\n                      min={0}\n                      value={tag.maxUsage || 50}\n                      disabled={isFramework}\n                      onChange={(v) => updateTag(tag.tag, { maxUsage: v ?? 50 })}\n                      integer\n                    />\n                  </div>\n                  <span className=\"text-small text-muted tre-merge-label\">\n                    Merge →\n                  </span>\n                  <select\n                    className=\"input tre-merge-select\"\n                    value={tag.consolidateInto || \"\"}\n                    disabled={isFramework}\n                    onChange={(e) =>\n                      updateTag(tag.tag, { consolidateInto: e.target.value || undefined })\n                    }\n                  >\n                    <option value=\"\">none</option>\n                    {allTagNames\n                      .filter((t) => t !== tag.tag)\n                      .map((t) => (\n                        <option key={t} value={t}>\n                          {t}\n                        </option>\n                      ))}\n                  </select>\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Consolidated Tag Relationships - 3 columns */}\n                <div className=\"nested-section-compact\">\n                  <div className=\"tre-grid-3col\">\n                    {/* Entity Kinds */}\n                    <div>\n                      <div className=\"label tre-section-label\">\n                        Applies to\n                      </div>\n                      <div className=\"chip-list tre-chip-section\">\n                        {entityKinds.map((ek) => {\n                          const isSelected = (tag.entityKinds || []).includes(ek.kind);\n                          return (\n                            <div\n                              key={ek.kind}\n                              className={`chip chip-clickable ${isSelected ? \"chip-active\" : \"\"} ${isFramework ? \"tre-chip-framework\" : \"tre-chip-compact\"}`}\n                              onClick={() => handleEntityKindToggle(tag, ek, isFramework)}\n                              role=\"button\"\n                              tabIndex={0}\n                              onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }}\n                            >\n                              {ek.description || ek.kind}\n                            </div>\n                          );\n                        })}\n                      </div>\n                      {(tag.entityKinds || []).length === 0 && (\n                        <span className=\"text-small text-muted\">all kinds</span>\n                      )}\n                    </div>\n\n                    {/* Related Tags */}\n                    <div>\n                      <div className=\"label tre-section-label\">\n                        Related\n                      </div>\n                      <div className=\"chip-list tre-chip-section\">\n                        {(tag.relatedTags || []).map((relatedTag) => (\n                          <div\n                            key={relatedTag}\n                            className=\"chip tre-chip-compact\"\n                          >\n                            <span>{relatedTag}</span>\n                            <button\n                              className=\"chip-remove tre-chip-remove-sm\"\n                              onClick={() => removeRelatedTag(tag.tag, relatedTag)}\n                              disabled={isFramework}\n                            >\n                              ×\n                            </button>\n                          </div>\n                        ))}\n                        {!isFramework && (\n                          <select\n                            className=\"input tre-add-select\"\n                            value=\"\"\n                            onChange={(e) => {\n                              if (e.target.value) {\n                                const current = tag.relatedTags || [];\n                                if (!current.includes(e.target.value)) {\n                                  updateTag(tag.tag, { relatedTags: [...current, e.target.value] });\n                                }\n                              }\n                            }}\n                          >\n                            <option value=\"\">+ add</option>\n                            {allTagNames\n                              .filter((t) => t !== tag.tag && !(tag.relatedTags || []).includes(t))\n                              .map((t) => (\n                                <option key={t} value={t}>\n                                  {t}\n                                </option>\n                              ))}\n                          </select>\n                        )}\n                      </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    {/* Conflicting Tags */}\n                    <div>\n                      <div className=\"label tre-conflicts-label\">\n                        Conflicts\n                      </div>\n                      <div className=\"chip-list tre-chip-section\">\n                        {(tag.conflictingTags || []).map((conflictingTag) => (\n                          <div\n                            key={conflictingTag}\n                            className=\"chip tre-chip-conflict\"\n                          >\n                            <span>{conflictingTag}</span>\n                            <button\n                              className=\"chip-remove tre-chip-remove-sm\"\n                              onClick={() => removeConflictingTag(tag.tag, conflictingTag)}\n                              disabled={isFramework}\n                            >\n                              ×\n                            </button>\n                          </div>\n                        ))}\n                        {!isFramework && (\n                          <select\n                            className=\"input tre-add-select\"\n                            value=\"\"\n                            onChange={(e) => {\n                              if (e.target.value) {\n                                const current = tag.conflictingTags || [];\n                                if (!current.includes(e.target.value)) {\n                                  updateTag(tag.tag, {\n                                    conflictingTags: [...current, e.target.value],\n                                  });\n                                }\n                              }\n                            }}\n                          >\n                            <option value=\"\">+ add</option>\n                            {allTagNames\n                              .filter(\n                                (t) => t !== tag.tag && !(tag.conflictingTags || []).includes(t)\n                              )\n                              .map((t) => (\n                                <option key={t} value={t}>\n                                  {t}\n                                </option>\n                              ))}\n                          </select>\n                        )}\n                      </div>\n                    </div>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Delete */}\n                <div className=\"danger-zone\">\n                  <button\n                    className=\"btn btn-danger\"\n                    onClick={() => deleteTag(tag.tag)}\n                    disabled={isFramework}\n                  >\n                    Delete Tag\n                  </button>\n                </div>\n              </ExpandableCard>\n            );\n          })}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nTagIdInput.propTypes = {\n  value: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\n  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n  allTagIds: PropTypes.arrayOf(PropTypes.string).isRequired,\n  disabled: PropTypes.bool,\n};\n\nTagRegistryEditor.propTypes = {\n  tagRegistry: PropTypes.array,\n  entityKinds: PropTypes.array,\n  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n  tagUsage: PropTypes.object,\n};\n","numLines":596,"startLine":1,"totalLines":596}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CFLEjmWd97noZk7T52anxe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the situation. Let me analyze the CSS overlap between the two files:\n\n**RelationshipKindEditor.css** (canonical, prefix `rke-`):\n- `.rke-container` — max-width: 900px\n- `.rke-name-row` — flex row, gap 12px, mb 12px\n- `.rke-actions-flow` — flex, center, gap 4px\n- `.rke-constraint-label` — mb 8px\n- `.rke-constraint-row` — flex, center, gap 12px\n- `.rke-constraint-col` — flex: 1\n\n\n- `.rke-constraint-header` — flex with space-between alignment, mb 4px\n- `.rke-chip-list-flush` — removes bottom margin\n- `.rke-arrow` — 16px font size\n- `.rke-chip-framework` — disabled pointer events, semi-transparent at 0.6 opacity\n- `.rke-maintenance-label` — mb 8px\n- `.rke-maintenance-row` — flex with 16px gap, wrapping enabled, centered\n- `.rke-maintenance-field` — flex centered with 8px gap\n- `.rke-select-compact` — auto width with tight 6px/10px padding\n\nNow I'm defining more utility classes for the constraint editor. I'm setting up clickable labels with flex centering and a 6px gap, making checkboxes a fixed 14x14 size, and organizing verb-related sections with consistent 8px margins and a 12px gap between verb form rows. Then I'm moving into the TagRegistryEditor styles with a max-width container, a stats bar that displays category metrics with dynamic backgrounds and colors, and badge elements.\n\nStill writing styles... Continuing through the CSS classes, I'm noticing several patterns where styles are being duplicated across different component prefixes — like the select dropdowns all using the same width and padding values, and checkboxes maintaining consistent 14x14 dimensions. I'm also seeing conflict-related styling with danger colors and semi-transparent red backgrounds for chips that need special attention.\n\nThe clearest path forward is to consolidate these truly identical rules into a shared CSS file at the SchemaEditor level, then import it in both component files since they're in the same directory. Before committing to this approach though, I should check what the CSS architecture ADR recommends for handling shared styles across components.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13050,"cache_read_input_tokens":54756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13050},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"283869e4-8656-46fb-b084-649222114059","uuid":"0fdd4a82-6e0f-466b-9f69-b2709de0cb04"}
