{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KSNpZLuQz1Q72AU8H4tdu6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the ESLint config structure. The highest ADR is 034. I need to create ADR 035. Let me also look at one of the existing CSS drift guard rules to understand the pattern, like `no-archivist-section-drift.js`.\n\nFor this area, the guard rule should detect when SchemaEditor sub-components re-introduce CSS rules that duplicate the shared `schema-editor-shared.css` utilities — specifically `select-compact`, `checkbox` (with 14x14 sizing), and `chip-framework` patterns. \n\nSince the drift here is CSS-level and the duplicated classes are in co-located CSS files, the best ESLint approach would be a rule that checks CSS import patterns and class name usage in JSX files. \n\nESLint can't parse CSS directly, so the rule needs to check the JSX side instead. The most practical approach is to detect when SchemaEditor sub-components use class names with component-specific prefixes like `rke-`, `tre-`, or `eke-` for patterns that should use the shared `se-` prefix — this catches developers copying and redefining shared classes locally instead of reusing them. The simplest approach is to require that any JSX file in the SchemaEditor directory importing a CSS file must also import `schema-editor-shared.css`. Alternatively, I could ban className patterns that look like component-prefixed shared utilities—like `foo-chip-framework` or `foo-select-compact`—when they should be using the `se-` prefix instead. The practical constraint is catching when developers add classes matching those specific patterns.\n\nI'm leaning toward a custom ESLint rule that targets SchemaEditor files specifically and flags className strings containing restricted patterns like `-select-compact` or `-checkbox` when they're not prefixed with `se-`. This would catch the drift at the source in JSX rather than relying on CSS file imports alone.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5472,"cache_read_input_tokens":84233,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5472},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"283869e4-8656-46fb-b084-649222114059","uuid":"55005c61-c449-4718-8457-106e5d1a85c9"}
