{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Nfa6a2c66SRArkd3v4mFCs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So illuminator and name-forge do NOT import shared-components styles. That explains why they have their own full `:root` definitions — they don't use the shared theme.css at all.\n\nBut some other apps (coherence-engine, canonry, cosmographer, viewer) DO import `@the-canonry/shared-components/styles`.\n\nNow the plan is clear:\n1. Create `packages/shared-components/src/styles/arctic-theme-base.css` with the shared base (design tokens, reset, body)\n2. Import it from `packages/shared-components/src/styles/index.css`  \n3. Modify illuminator's App.css to import the shared base and keep only app-specific overrides + component styles\n\n\n4. Do the same for name-forge's App.css\n\nBut wait — if I add it to the shared-components index.css, that automatically affects all the apps already importing from there. They'd suddenly have access to `--bg-primary` and other variables, which could break things if they're not expecting them or if there are conflicts with their existing styles. I need to think about this more carefully. The safest approach is probably to keep the arctic-theme-base as a standalone file that only the apps that need it explicitly import, rather than bundling it into the shared index.\n\ncss. That way it's opt-in instead of forced on everything. Let me check how the package.json exports are set up to make sure that import path would actually work.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":527,"cache_read_input_tokens":66458,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":527},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f96e591f-9951-4599-91ca-4e5e08bd5234","uuid":"b9a58e2c-bb72-4b69-ad30-0f4