{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0182YJjvBNw85ytwhBB3Nyqr","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * Panel utility classes — shared structural patterns for dense information panels.\n     3→ *\n     4→ * These classes extract the most commonly duplicated CSS patterns across\n     5→ * Illuminator panel/tab components. Components should compose these alongside\n     6→ * their prefixed component-specific classes.\n     7→ *\n     8→ * Usage:  className=\"ilu-section htab-section\"\n     9→ *   The ilu-* class provides the base structural pattern.\n    10→ *   The component-prefixed class adds/overrides unique properties.\n    11→ *\n    12→ * Canonical reference: apps/illuminator/webui/src/components/ActivityPanel.css\n    13→ * ADR: docs/adr/029-panel-css-utilities.md\n    14→ */\n    15→\n    16→/* ── Section card container ──\n    17→ * Padded container with bg-secondary, border, radius.\n    18→ * Used by: htab-section, pt-checklist, vtab-section, itab-cover-section,\n    19→ *          itab-compat-panel, enrtab-container, crv-refinements, crv-panel, etc.\n    20→ */\n    21→.ilu-section {\n    22→  padding: 16px;\n    23→  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n    24→  border-radius: 8px;\n    25→  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    26→}\n    27→\n    28→.ilu-section-title {\n    29→  font-size: 14px;\n    30→  font-weight: 600;\n    31→}\n    32→\n    33→.ilu-section-mb {\n    34→  margin-bottom: 16px;\n    35→}\n    36→\n    37→/* ── Overflow container ──\n    38→ * Container without padding, with overflow hidden. For containers that have\n    39→ * a separate header bar and body section.\n    40→ * Used by: crv-checks-panel, crp-synth, crp-acv, ref-tab-synth, ref-tab-fcv,\n    41→ *          ctab-viewer, ctab-summary-section, ctab-tertiary-section, etc.\n    42→ */\n    43→.ilu-container {\n    44→  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n    45→  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    46→  border-radius: 8px;\n    47→  overflow: hidden;\n    48→}\n    49→\n    50→/* ── Collapsible header bar ──\n    51→ * Header bar inside a container, with bg-tertiary background.\n    52→ * Used by: crp-synth-header, crp-acv-header, ref-tab-synth-header,\n    53→ *          ref-tab-fcv-header, ctab-viewer-toolbar, ctab-summary-header,\n    54→ *          vtab-report-header, etc.\n    55→ */\n    56→.ilu-container-header {\n    57→  padding: 12px 16px;\n    58→  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n    59→  display: flex;\n    60→  align-items: center;\n    61→}\n    62→\n    63→.ilu-container-header-bordered {\n    64→  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    65→}\n    66→\n    67→/* ── Action button ──\n    68→ * Standard action button with bg-tertiary, border, rounded.\n    69→ * Used by: cic-action-btn, enrtab-button, htab-annotate-btn, htab-prep-btn,\n    70→ *          htab-backport-btn, pt-refrow-btn, vtab-action-btn, vtab-regen-btn,\n    71→ *          events-panel-export-btn, events-panel-clear-filters-btn, etc.\n    72→ */\n    73→.ilu-action-btn {\n    74→  padding: 8px 14px;\n    75→  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n    76→  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    77→  border-radius: 6px;\n    78→  color: var(--text-secondary);\n    79→  font-size: 12px;\n    80→}\n    81→\n    82→.ilu-action-btn:not(:disabled) {\n    83→  cursor: pointer;\n    84→}\n    85→\n    86→.ilu-action-btn:disabled {\n    87→  cursor: not-allowed;\n    88→  opacity: 0.6;\n    89→}\n    90→\n    91→/* Smaller variant */\n    92→.ilu-action-btn-sm {\n    93→  padding: 6px 12px;\n    94→  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n    95→  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n    96→  border-radius: 4px;\n    97→  color: var(--text-secondary);\n    98→  font-size: 12px;\n    99→}\n   100→\n   101→.ilu-action-btn-sm:not(:disabled) {\n   102→  cursor: pointer;\n   103→}\n   104→\n   105→.ilu-action-btn-sm:disabled {\n   106→  cursor: not-allowed;\n   107→  opacity: 0.6;\n   108→}\n   109→\n   110→/* ── Active version badge (green pill) ──\n   111→ * Pill-shaped badge indicating the active/current version.\n   112→ * Used by: hec-active-badge, cvs-active-badge.\n   113→ */\n   114→.ilu-active-badge {\n   115→  font-size: 11px;\n   116→  padding: 2px 8px;\n   117→  background: rgb(16 185 129 / 15%);\n   118→  color: #10b981;\n   119→  border-radius: 999px;\n   120→  font-weight: 500;\n   121→}\n   122→\n   123→/* ── Compact select ──\n   124→ * Smaller select input for version/comparison selectors in toolbars.\n   125→ * Compose with component class to set min-width.\n   126→ * Used by: hec-select, hec-compare-select, cvs-select-version, cvs-select-compare.\n   127→ */\n   128→.ilu-compact-select {\n   129→  width: auto;\n   130→  font-size: 12px;\n   131→  padding: 4px 6px;\n   132→}\n   133→\n   134→/* ── Empty state ──\n   135→ * Centered empty state text.\n   136→ * Used by: ap-empty-state, cip-empty-state, events-panel-empty,\n   137→ *          crv-empty, dmw-empty-state, htab-empty, itab-empty, etc.\n   138→ */\n   139→.ilu-empty {\n   140→  font-size: 13px;\n   141→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   142→  padding: 24px;\n   143→  text-align: center;\n   144→}\n   145→\n   146→/* ── Footer actions row ──\n   147→ * Row of actions at the bottom of a dialog or panel.\n   148→ * Used by: bcm-footer, dmw-footer, cfr-footer.\n   149→ */\n   150→.ilu-footer {\n   151→  padding: 12px 20px;\n   152→  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n   153→  display: flex;\n   154→  justify-content: flex-end;\n   155→  gap: 8px;\n   156→  flex-shrink: 0;\n   157→}\n   158→\n   159→/* ── Warning banner ──\n   160→ * Amber-tinted warning banner.\n   161→ * Used by: pp-key-warning, itab-version-warning, crv-stale-warning.\n   162→ */\n   163→.ilu-warning-banner {\n   164→  padding: 12px 16px;\n   165→  background: rgb(245 158 11 / 10%);\n   166→  border: 1px solid rgb(245 158 11 / 30%);\n   167→  border-radius: 4px;\n   168→}\n   169→\n   170→/* ── Error banner ──\n   171→ * Red-tinted error banner.\n   172→ * Used by: cfr-error-banner, dmw-review-error, cip-error-message.\n   173→ */\n   174→.ilu-error-banner {\n   175→  padding: 8px 14px;\n   176→  background: rgb(239 68 68 / 10%);\n   177→  border-radius: 6px;\n   178→  border: 1px solid rgb(239 68 68 / 30%);\n   179→  font-size: 11px;\n   180→  color: #ef4444;\n   181→}\n   182→\n   183→/* ── Status colors ──\n   184→ * Inline status color utilities. Used pervasively across all panel CSS.\n   185→ */\n   186→.ilu-status-success { color: #10b981; }\n   187→.ilu-status-warning { color: #f59e0b; }\n   188→.ilu-status-error { color: #ef4444; }\n   189→\n   190→/* ── Footer button sizing ──\n   191→ * Standard footer button sizing for dialog footers.\n   192→ * Used by: bcm-footer-btn, rfm-footer-btn, dmw-footer-btn.\n   193→ */\n   194→.ilu-footer-btn {\n   195→  padding: 6px 16px;\n   196→  font-size: 12px;\n   197→}\n   198→\n   199→/* ── Section heading (uppercase label) ──\n   200→ * Small uppercase label for section headings within panels.\n   201→ * Used by: bcm-section-label, cfr-context-heading, cfr-field-label, etc.\n   202→ */\n   203→.ilu-section-label {\n   204→  font-size: 11px;\n   205→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   206→  text-transform: uppercase;\n   207→  font-weight: 600;\n   208→  letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n   209→}\n   210→\n   211→/* ── Selection bar ──\n   212→ * Sticky bar showing selected-item count with bulk actions.\n   213→ * Used by: eq-selection-bar, eb-selection-bar, rp-selection-bar.\n   214→ */\n   215→.ilu-selection-bar {\n   216→  display: flex;\n   217→  align-items: center;\n   218→  justify-content: space-between;\n   219→  padding: 12px 16px;\n   220→  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n   221→  border: 1px solid var(--accent-color);\n   222→  border-radius: 6px;\n   223→}\n   224→\n   225→/* ── Stats grid ──\n   226→ * Grid of stat cards with large values and muted labels.\n   227→ * Used by: tps-stats-grid, storage-panel-stats-grid, rp-stats-bar.\n   228→ */\n   229→.ilu-stats-grid {\n   230→  display: grid;\n   231→  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(100px, 1fr));\n   232→  gap: 12px;\n   233→  margin-bottom: 16px;\n   234→}\n   235→\n   236→.ilu-stat-card {\n   237→  padding: 10px;\n   238→  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n   239→  border-radius: 6px;\n   240→  text-align: center;\n   241→}\n   242→\n   243→.ilu-stat-value {\n   244→  font-size: 20px;\n   245→  font-weight: 600;\n   246→}\n   247→\n   248→.ilu-stat-label {\n   249→  font-size: 11px;\n   250→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   251→}\n   252→\n   253→/* ── Thumbnail cover image ──\n   254→ * Absolute-positioned image filling its container with cover fit.\n   255→ * Used by: cip-thumb-img, ipm-thumbnail-img, storage-panel-thumbnail-img.\n   256→ */\n   257→.ilu-thumb-cover {\n   258→  position: absolute;\n   259→  top: 0;\n   260→  left: 0;\n   261→  width: 100%;\n   262→  height: 100%;\n   263→  object-fit: cover;\n   264→}\n   265→\n   266→/* ── Muted hint text (12px) ──\n   267→ * Base muted description / hint text at standard size.\n   268→ * Compose with component-prefixed classes for spacing overrides.\n   269→ * Used by: cfgp-section-desc, cfgp-about-text, cpanel-section-hint,\n   270→ *          cpanel-empty-hint, itc-sync-hint, stsel-compact-label, stsel-label, etc.\n   271→ */\n   272→.ilu-hint {\n   273→  font-size: 12px;\n   274→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   275→}\n   276→\n   277→/* ── Muted hint text (11px) ──\n   278→ * Smaller muted text for secondary annotations, sub-hints, descriptions.\n   279→ * Used by: cfgp-hint, cfgp-checkbox-hint, bcam-chronicle-tone,\n   280→ *          itc-sync-summary, stsel-description, cpanel-clear-button, etc.\n   281→ */\n   282→.ilu-hint-sm {\n   283→  font-size: 11px;\n   284→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   285→}\n   286→\n   287→/* ── Thumbnail placeholder ──\n   288→ * Absolute-positioned centered placeholder for loading/missing thumbnails.\n   289→ * Used by: cip-thumb-loading, ipm-thumbnail-placeholder, storage-panel-thumbnail-placeholder.\n   290→ */\n   291→.ilu-thumb-placeholder {\n   292→  position: absolute;\n   293→  top: 0;\n   294→  left: 0;\n   295→  width: 100%;\n   296→  height: 100%;\n   297→  display: flex;\n   298→  align-items: center;\n   299→  justify-content: center;\n   300→  color: var(--text-muted);\n   301→  font-size: 11px;\n   302→}\n   303→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e25f0ac-8e93-4dfd-8fc9-5da30702dc9f","uuid":"7dc655ef-0c37-4a94-8fc8-edf4d67dfcea","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/panel-utilities.css","content":"/**\n * Panel utility classes — shared structural patterns for dense information panels.\n *\n * These classes extract the most commonly duplicated CSS patterns across\n * Illuminator panel/tab components. Components should compose these alongside\n * their prefixed component-specific classes.\n *\n * Usage:  className=\"ilu-section htab-section\"\n *   The ilu-* class provides the base structural pattern.\n *   The component-prefixed class adds/overrides unique properties.\n *\n * Canonical reference: apps/illuminator/webui/src/components/ActivityPanel.css\n * ADR: docs/adr/029-panel-css-utilities.md\n */\n\n/* ── Section card container ──\n * Padded container with bg-secondary, border, radius.\n * Used by: htab-section, pt-checklist, vtab-section, itab-cover-section,\n *          itab-compat-panel, enrtab-container, crv-refinements, crv-panel, etc.\n */\n.ilu-section {\n  padding: 16px;\n  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n}\n\n.ilu-section-title {\n  font-size: 14px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.ilu-section-mb {\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n\n/* ── Overflow container ──\n * Container without padding, with overflow hidden. For containers that have\n * a separate header bar and body section.\n * Used by: crv-checks-panel, crp-synth, crp-acv, ref-tab-synth, ref-tab-fcv,\n *          ctab-viewer, ctab-summary-section, ctab-tertiary-section, etc.\n */\n.ilu-container {\n  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n/* ── Collapsible header bar ──\n * Header bar inside a container, with bg-tertiary background.\n * Used by: crp-synth-header, crp-acv-header, ref-tab-synth-header,\n *          ref-tab-fcv-header, ctab-viewer-toolbar, ctab-summary-header,\n *          vtab-report-header, etc.\n */\n.ilu-container-header {\n  padding: 12px 16px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n\n.ilu-container-header-bordered {\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n}\n\n/* ── Action button ──\n * Standard action button with bg-tertiary, border, rounded.\n * Used by: cic-action-btn, enrtab-button, htab-annotate-btn, htab-prep-btn,\n *          htab-backport-btn, pt-refrow-btn, vtab-action-btn, vtab-regen-btn,\n *          events-panel-export-btn, events-panel-clear-filters-btn, etc.\n */\n.ilu-action-btn {\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  color: var(--text-secondary);\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn:not(:disabled) {\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn:disabled {\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n}\n\n/* Smaller variant */\n.ilu-action-btn-sm {\n  padding: 6px 12px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  color: var(--text-secondary);\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn-sm:not(:disabled) {\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.ilu-action-btn-sm:disabled {\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n}\n\n/* ── Active version badge (green pill) ──\n * Pill-shaped badge indicating the active/current version.\n * Used by: hec-active-badge, cvs-active-badge.\n */\n.ilu-active-badge {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  padding: 2px 8px;\n  background: rgb(16 185 129 / 15%);\n  color: #10b981;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  font-weight: 500;\n}\n\n/* ── Compact select ──\n * Smaller select input for version/comparison selectors in toolbars.\n * Compose with component class to set min-width.\n * Used by: hec-select, hec-compare-select, cvs-select-version, cvs-select-compare.\n */\n.ilu-compact-select {\n  width: auto;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  padding: 4px 6px;\n}\n\n/* ── Empty state ──\n * Centered empty state text.\n * Used by: ap-empty-state, cip-empty-state, events-panel-empty,\n *          crv-empty, dmw-empty-state, htab-empty, itab-empty, etc.\n */\n.ilu-empty {\n  font-size: 13px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  padding: 24px;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n/* ── Footer actions row ──\n * Row of actions at the bottom of a dialog or panel.\n * Used by: bcm-footer, dmw-footer, cfr-footer.\n */\n.ilu-footer {\n  padding: 12px 20px;\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: flex-end;\n  gap: 8px;\n  flex-shrink: 0;\n}\n\n/* ── Warning banner ──\n * Amber-tinted warning banner.\n * Used by: pp-key-warning, itab-version-warning, crv-stale-warning.\n */\n.ilu-warning-banner {\n  padding: 12px 16px;\n  background: rgb(245 158 11 / 10%);\n  border: 1px solid rgb(245 158 11 / 30%);\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n/* ── Error banner ──\n * Red-tinted error banner.\n * Used by: cfr-error-banner, dmw-review-error, cip-error-message.\n */\n.ilu-error-banner {\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  background: rgb(239 68 68 / 10%);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  border: 1px solid rgb(239 68 68 / 30%);\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: #ef4444;\n}\n\n/* ── Status colors ──\n * Inline status color utilities. Used pervasively across all panel CSS.\n */\n.ilu-status-success { color: #10b981; }\n.ilu-status-warning { color: #f59e0b; }\n.ilu-status-error { color: #ef4444; }\n\n/* ── Footer button sizing ──\n * Standard footer button sizing for dialog footers.\n * Used by: bcm-footer-btn, rfm-footer-btn, dmw-footer-btn.\n */\n.ilu-footer-btn {\n  padding: 6px 16px;\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n/* ── Section heading (uppercase label) ──\n * Small uppercase label for section headings within panels.\n * Used by: bcm-section-label, cfr-context-heading, cfr-field-label, etc.\n */\n.ilu-section-label {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n}\n\n/* ── Selection bar ──\n * Sticky bar showing selected-item count with bulk actions.\n * Used by: eq-selection-bar, eb-selection-bar, rp-selection-bar.\n */\n.ilu-selection-bar {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  padding: 12px 16px;\n  background: var(--bg-secondary);\n  border: 1px solid var(--accent-color);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n}\n\n/* ── Stats grid ──\n * Grid of stat cards with large values and muted labels.\n * Used by: tps-stats-grid, storage-panel-stats-grid, rp-stats-bar.\n */\n.ilu-stats-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(100px, 1fr));\n  gap: 12px;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n\n.ilu-stat-card {\n  padding: 10px;\n  background: var(--bg-tertiary);\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.ilu-stat-value {\n  font-size: 20px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.ilu-stat-label {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n/* ── Thumbnail cover image ──\n * Absolute-positioned image filling its container with cover fit.\n * Used by: cip-thumb-img, ipm-thumbnail-img, storage-panel-thumbnail-img.\n */\n.ilu-thumb-cover {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 0;\n  left: 0;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  object-fit: cover;\n}\n\n/* ── Muted hint text (12px) ──\n * Base muted description / hint text at standard size.\n * Compose with component-prefixed classes for spacing overrides.\n * Used by: cfgp-section-desc, cfgp-about-text, cpanel-section-hint,\n *          cpanel-empty-hint, itc-sync-hint, stsel-compact-label, stsel-label, etc.\n */\n.ilu-hint {\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n/* ── Muted hint text (11px) ──\n * Smaller muted text for secondary annotations, sub-hints, descriptions.\n * Used by: cfgp-hint, cfgp-checkbox-hint, bcam-chronicle-tone,\n *          itc-sync-summary, stsel-description, cpanel-clear-button, etc.\n */\n.ilu-hint-sm {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n/* ── Thumbnail placeholder ──\n * Absolute-positioned centered placeholder for loading/missing thumbnails.\n * Used by: cip-thumb-loading, ipm-thumbnail-placeholder, storage-panel-thumbnail-placeholder.\n */\n.ilu-thumb-placeholder {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 0;\n  left: 0;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  font-size: 11px;\n}\n","numLines":303,"startLine":1,"totalLines":303}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AdZWPChEpsUL1dEFxnWHc1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me also check the shared-components styles index to see how shared CSS is wired up.\n\nLooking at the two files:\n\n**WeightMatrixEditor.css** - coherence-engine specific, uses hardcoded values, class names like `.matrix-*`, `.weight-*`\n**CoverageMatrix.css** - shared-components package, uses CSS vars with fallbacks, class names like `.cm-*`\n\nThe shared structural patterns I can extract:\n\n1. **Matrix container layout** - flex column container at 100% height\n2. **Matrix scrollable area** - flex 1, overflow auto, bg, border, radius\n\n\n3. **Matrix table** - width 100%, border-collapse, sticky headers, uppercase header text\n4. **Matrix row hover** - background transition\n5. **Matrix toolbar** - flex row with gap\n6. **Matrix search input** - styled input with focus state\n7. **Matrix legend** - flex row at bottom\n\nI'll create a shared base CSS file in `packages/shared-components/src/styles/components/matrix-base.css` with these structural patterns, then have both existing CSS files import it. The tricky part is handling the different class name conventions—I need to decide whether to create new base classes or use a mixin-like approach that both files can adapt to their own naming schemes.\n\nLooking at how panel-utilities.css works, it uses a dual-class pattern where shared structural classes (prefixed with `.ilu-`) are combined with component-specific classes on the same elements. I'll apply the same strategy here with a `.mat-` prefix for the shared matrix classes, defining the core layout and table structure that both components can layer their own styling on top of.\n\nBut wait—I need to reconsider the actual requirement. The goal is to consolidate duplicated styles into shared-components and update import paths, not just define a new pattern. Since CoverageMatrix.css is already in shared-components and WeightMatrixEditor.css is in the app, I should extract the truly shared structural patterns into a base CSS file in shared-components, then have WeightMatrixEditor import from there instead of maintaining its own copy.\n\nThe challenge is that both components use different class names, so I'd need to update the JSX to use a common `mat-` prefix for structural elements while keeping component-specific classes for unique styling. Looking at what's actually duplicated—the container flex layout, table structure, and toolbar styling—I can consolidate those into a shared base file and remove the redundant rules from both existing CSS files. I'm seeing that CoverageMatrix uses CSS custom properties with fallbacks while WeightMatrixEditor uses hardcoded values, so I'll standardize on the custom properties approach for better maintainability when building the shared base styles.\n\nRather than getting caught up in the abstraction details, let me focus on the concrete overlapping patterns: the matrix layout structure, scrollable container, table styling with sticky headers, row hover effects, toolbar with search input, and the legend bar at the bottom.\n\nNow I need to check how the shared components index is set up so I can properly wire in the import.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14749,"cache_read_input_tokens":72024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14749},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e25f0ac-8e93-4dfd-8fc9-5da30702dc9f","uuid":"d9c45376-7835-4546-bdb8-e8ad299339b6"}
