s from the component defaults. Still refactoring styles... need `.weight-matrix-editor` to exist on the element. The class name is still on the JSX element, it just won't have its own CSS rules anymore. The descendant selectors still work because the class is still on the element.\n\nSo I can remove the `.weight-matrix-editor { ... }` rule entirely from the CSS.\n\nFor `.matrix-container`, I can remove it entirely since all those styles are covered by `mat-scroll-area`.\n\nFor `.matrix-table`, I'm looking at the table styling rules — the base table properties, the cell padding and borders, and the sticky header styling. I can remove all of those since they're covered by `mat-table`, but I need to keep the checkbox input rule.\n\nStill reviewing table styles... Still writing CSS cleanup... Comparing the table header styles between the two components — they're nearly identical, except CoverageMatrix uses CSS variables while WME uses hardcoded values, and CoverageMatrix has an extra `white-space: nowrap` property I noted earlier. Writing CSS rules...\n\nNow I'm mapping out the JSX class name updates across the component — replacing the old class names with the new Material Design ones while keeping the original classes for specificity. Updating class names across the CoverageMatrix component to follow the new naming convention, adding the `mat-` prefix to all layout and structural classes while preserving the component-specific identifiers.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1064,"cache_read_input_tokens":88972,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1064},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e25f0ac-8e93-4dfd-8fc9-5da30702dc9f","uuid":"0f4ea700-f53f-43f0-a430-e7c1d1fd5a5c"}
