{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YGVz4LnyY9EVSjsVQNtKN7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand what's similar and what's different:\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Both have an SVG container class with `display: block` (`.ec-svg` and `.tb-svg`)\n- Both have a \"no pointer events\" class (`.ec-no-pointer` and `.tb-no-pointer`)\n\n**Unique to EnsembleConstellation:**\n- `.ec-svg` has `background: var(--bg-secondary)` and `border-radius: 8px`\n- `.ec-cursor-pointer` — `cursor: pointer`\n\n**Unique to TimelineBrush:**\n- `.tb-svg` has `cursor: var(--tb-cursor, crosshair)`\n\n\n- `.tb-grab` — `cursor: grab`\n- `.tb-ew-resize` — `cursor: ew-resize`\n\nThese components share about 43% similarity — both are SVG visualizations with overlapping base patterns like container styling, pointer event handling, and cursor utilities. I should extract the common SVG visualization foundations into a shared CSS file within the visualizations directory, then have both components import from it to eliminate duplication. Now I need to check which components are actually consuming these CSS files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":562,"cache_read_input_tokens":52079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":562},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee4ea11c-d389-40b8-aae4-dcc42ada4575","uuid":"5b30b749-cc00-441f-99fb-5c0372ff1577"}
