{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gz3c5qGYLK8ew78k3hmJDD","type":"tool_result","content":"034-dashboard-section-css-consolidation.md\n035-schema-editor-shared-css.md\n036-app-css-base-consolidation.md\n037-matrix-css-consolidation.md\n038-toggle-css-consolidation.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee4ea11c-d389-40b8-aae4-dcc42ada4575","uuid":"148d90a8-37eb-43e2-aac0-eef45d1c2c3f","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"034-dashboard-section-css-consolidation.md\n035-schema-editor-shared-css.md\n036-app-css-base-consolidation.md\n037-matrix-css-consolidation.md\n038-toggle-css-consolidation.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01F3fQhppa5bDk3Lty7DKeEz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LQfTKZRYxUWwhTcaqtCvWi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/adr/039-visualization-base-css.md","content":"<!-- drift-generated -->\n# ADR-039: Shared SVG Visualization Base CSS\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\nThe `ChronicleWizard/visualizations/` directory contains multiple SVG-based visualization\ncomponents (EnsembleConstellation, TimelineBrush, NarrativeTimeline, StoryPotentialRadar,\nIntensitySparkline, MiniConstellation). Each component independently defined the same\nutility CSS rules:\n\n- `display: block` on the SVG container (removes inline-element whitespace gap)\n- `pointer-events: none` for overlay text and decorations\n- Cursor utilities (`pointer`, `grab`, `ew-resize`)\n\nThese were prefixed per-component (`ec-no-pointer`, `tb-grab`, etc.), creating identical\nrules under different names.\n\n## Decision\nExtract shared SVG visualization utilities into a single `visualization-base.css` file\nin the `visualizations/` directory. All visualization components import this file and use\nthe shared `viz-*` class names:\n\n| Shared class | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `.viz-svg` | SVG container base (`display: block`) |\n| `.viz-no-pointer` | Suppress pointer events on overlays |\n| `.viz-cursor-pointer` | Pointer cursor for clickable elements |\n| `.viz-grab` | Grab cursor for draggable elements |\n| `.viz-ew-resize` | East-west resize cursor for handles |\n\nComponent-specific SVG styles (background, border-radius, CSS-variable cursors) remain\nin the component's own CSS file, which imports `visualization-base.css`.\n\n## Consequences\n- One place to update SVG visualization utilities across all components\n- Consistent class names make it easier to grep for usage patterns\n- New visualization components start by importing `visualization-base.css`\n- Component CSS files become smaller — only component-specific overrides\n\n## Enforcement\n- ESLint rule `local/no-viz-utility-drift` bans component-prefixed utility class names\n  (e.g. `ec-no-pointer`, `tb-grab`) in JSX within the `visualizations/` directory, requiring\n  the shared `viz-*` classes instead\n- Pattern guide: `docs/patterns/visualization-base-css.md`\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":184,"cache_read_input_tokens":77198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":184},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee4ea11c-d389-40b8-aae4-dcc42ada4575","uuid":"dfc8b6ea-7e72-4ad8-a251-51f0aca41760"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQfTKZRYxUWwhTcaqtCvWi","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/adr/039-visualization-base-css.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee4ea11c-d389-40b8-aae4-dcc42ada4575","uuid":"27a0bd03-224f-463e-9264-5aa9c675e6b1","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/docs/adr/039-visualization-base-css.md","content":"<!-- drift-generated -->\n# ADR-039: Shared SVG Visualization Base CSS\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\nThe `ChronicleWizard/visualizations/` directory contains multiple SVG-based visualization\ncomponents (EnsembleConstellation, TimelineBrush, NarrativeTimeline, StoryPotentialRadar,\nIntensitySparkline, MiniConstellation). Each component independently defined the same\nutility CSS rules:\n\n- `display: block` on the SVG container (removes inline-element whitespace gap)\n- `pointer-events: none` for overlay text and decorations\n- Cursor utilities (`pointer`, `grab`, `ew-resize`)\n\nThese were prefixed per-component (`ec-no-pointer`, `tb-grab`, etc.), creating identical\nrules under different names.\n\n## Decision\nExtract shared SVG visualization utilities into a single `visualization-base.css` file\nin the `visualizations/` directory. All visualization components import this file and use\nthe shared `viz-*` class names:\n\n| Shared class | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `.viz-svg` | SVG container base (`display: block`) |\n| `.viz-no-pointer` | Suppress pointer events on overlays |\n| `.viz-cursor-pointer` | Pointer cursor for clickable elements |\n| `.viz-grab` | Grab cursor for draggable elements |\n| `.viz-ew-resize` | East-west resize cursor for handles |\n\nComponent-specific SVG styles (background, border-radius, CSS-variable cursors) remain\nin the component's own CSS file, which imports `visualization-base.css`.\n\n## Consequences\n- One place to update SVG visualization utilities across all components\n- Consistent class names make it easier to grep for usage patterns\n- New visualization components start by importing `visualization-base.css`\n- Component CSS files become smaller — only component-specific overrides\n\n## Enforcement\n- ESLint rule `local/no-viz-utility-drift` bans component-prefixed utility class names\n  (e.g. `ec-no-pointer`, `tb-grab`) in JSX within the `visualizations/` directory, requiring\n  the shared `viz-*` classes instead\n- Pattern guide: `docs/patterns/visualization-base-css.md`\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
