{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AMcFMmQHnTo23uTLecwB48","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the two CSS files. Both are for components within the cosmographer app. They share similar structural patterns:\n\n1. Container with max-width\n2. Header section (title, subtitle)\n3. Toolbar with add button\n4. List/table of items with cards\n5. Action buttons (edit, delete)\n6. Empty state\n7. Modal overlay and content\n8. Form groups with labels, inputs\n9. Modal actions (cancel, save)\n\nThe similarity is around 46%, which is moderate. The shared patterns are:\n- Container (`max-width: 1000px`)\n- Header (title + subtitle)\n\n\n- Toolbar (flex, margin-bottom)\n- Add button (same styling: `#60a5fa` bg, `#0a1929` color, etc.)\n- Delete button (transparent bg, red border/color)\n- Empty state (centered text)\n- Modal (fixed position overlay, `z-index: 1000`, same backdrop color)\n- Modal content (same bg color, padding, border-radius, border)\n- Modal title (similar styling)\n- Form groups, labels, inputs\n- Modal actions (flex, flex-end, gap)\n- Hint text\n- Arrow\n\nThe main distinction is that AxisRegistry uses a card-based list layout, while the other component structures its items differently.\n\nNow I'm noticing the styling divergences between the two components—AxisRegistry has a card-based structure with specific class names, while RelationshipEditor uses a table layout with different class conventions. There are also subtle color and size variations across them. My approach would be to extract the common patterns into a shared CSS file within the cosmographer app, keeping component-specific overrides in their own files, then checking how the existing CSS infrastructure in the project is organized before implementing this.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4848,"cache_read_input_tokens":52212,"cac