{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F36okZXT5CGk8aQVrgr9JV","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * RelationshipEditor - Create and manage relationships between seed entities.\n     3→ */\n     4→\n     5→import React, { useState } from \"react\";\n     6→import PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\n     7→import { NumberInput } from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\n     8→import \"./RelationshipEditor.css\";\n     9→\n    10→export default function RelationshipEditor({ project, onSave }) {\n    11→  const [showModal, setShowModal] = useState(false);\n    12→  const [filterKind, setFilterKind] = useState(\"\");\n    13→  const [newRel, setNewRel] = useState({ kind: \"\", src: \"\", dst: \"\", strength: 1 });\n    14→\n    15→  const relationships = project?.seedRelationships || [];\n    16→  const entities = project?.seedEntities || [];\n    17→  // Schema v2: relationshipKinds at project root\n    18→  const relationshipKinds = project?.relationshipKinds || [];\n    19→\n    20→  const filteredRels = filterKind\n    21→    ? relationships.filter((r) => r.kind === filterKind)\n    22→    : relationships;\n    23→\n    24→  const updateRelationships = (newRels) => {\n    25→    onSave({ seedRelationships: newRels });\n    26→  };\n    27→\n    28→  const addRelationship = () => {\n    29→    if (!newRel.kind || !newRel.src || !newRel.dst) {\n    30→      alert(\"Please fill all required fields\");\n    31→      return;\n    32→    }\n    33→\n    34→    if (newRel.src === newRel.dst) {\n    35→      alert(\"Source and destination must be different\");\n    36→      return;\n    37→    }\n    38→\n    39→    const rel = {\n    40→      kind: newRel.kind,\n    41→      src: newRel.src,\n    42→      dst: newRel.dst,\n    43→      strength: parseFloat(newRel.strength) || 1,\n    44→    };\n    45→\n    46→    updateRelationships([...relationships, rel]);\n    47→    setShowModal(false);\n    48→    setNewRel({ kind: \"\", src: \"\", dst: \"\", strength: 1 });\n    49→  };\n    50→\n    51→  const deleteRelationship = (rel) => {\n    52→    if (!confirm(\"Delete this relationship?\")) return;\n    53→    updateRelationships(\n    54→      relationships.filter((r) => !(r.kind === rel.kind && r.src === rel.src && r.dst === rel.dst))\n    55→    );\n    56→  };\n    57→\n    58→  const getEntityName = (entityId) => {\n    59→    const entity = entities.find((e) => e.id === entityId);\n    60→    return entity?.name || entityId;\n    61→  };\n    62→\n    63→  const getRelKindName = (kindId) => {\n    64→    const kind = relationshipKinds.find((k) => k.kind === kindId);\n    65→    return kind?.description || kind?.kind || kindId;\n    66→  };\n    67→\n    68→  // Filter entities by allowed source/dest kinds for the selected relationship\n    69→  const selectedRelKind = relationshipKinds.find((k) => k.kind === newRel.kind);\n    70→  const allowedSrcEntities = selectedRelKind?.srcKinds?.length\n    71→    ? entities.filter((e) => selectedRelKind.srcKinds.includes(e.kind))\n    72→    : entities;\n    73→  const allowedDstEntities = selectedRelKind?.dstKinds?.length\n    74→    ? entities.filter((e) => selectedRelKind.dstKinds.includes(e.kind))\n    75→    : entities;\n    76→\n    77→  return (\n    78→    <div className=\"re-container\">\n    79→      <div className=\"re-header\">\n    80→        <div className=\"re-title\">Relationships</div>\n    81→        <div className=\"re-subtitle\">Define connections between seed entities.</div>\n    82→      </div>\n    83→\n    84→      <div className=\"re-toolbar\">\n    85→        <select\n    86→          className=\"re-filter-select\"\n    87→          value={filterKind}\n    88→          onChange={(e) => setFilterKind(e.target.value)}\n    89→        >\n    90→          <option value=\"\">All kinds ({relationships.length})</option>\n    91→          {relationshipKinds.map((k) => (\n    92→            <option key={k.kind} value={k.kind}>\n    93→              {k.description || k.kind} ({relationships.filter((r) => r.kind === k.kind).length})\n    94→            </option>\n    95→          ))}\n    96→        </select>\n    97→        <button\n    98→          className=\"re-add-button\"\n    99→          onClick={() => setShowModal(true)}\n   100→          disabled={entities.length < 2 || relationshipKinds.length === 0}\n   101→        >\n   102→          + Add Relationship\n   103→        </button>\n   104→        {entities.length < 2 && (\n   105→          <span className=\"re-hint\">Need at least 2 entities</span>\n   106→        )}\n   107→        {relationshipKinds.length === 0 && (\n   108→          <span className=\"re-hint\">\n   109→            Define relationship kinds in Schema first\n   110→          </span>\n   111→        )}\n   112→      </div>\n   113→\n   114→      {filteredRels.length === 0 ? (\n   115→        <div className=\"re-empty-state\">\n   116→          {relationships.length === 0\n   117→            ? \"No relationships yet. Create one to connect entities.\"\n   118→            : \"No relationships match the filter.\"}\n   119→        </div>\n   120→      ) : (\n   121→        <table className=\"re-table\">\n   122→          <thead>\n   123→            <tr>\n   124→              <th className=\"re-th\">Kind</th>\n   125→              <th className=\"re-th\">Source</th>\n   126→              <th className=\"re-th\"></th>\n   127→              <th className=\"re-th\">Destination</th>\n   128→              <th className=\"re-th\">Strength</th>\n   129→              <th className=\"re-th\"></th>\n   130→            </tr>\n   131→          </thead>\n   132→          <tbody>\n   133→            {filteredRels.map((rel, idx) => (\n   134→              <tr key={`${rel.kind}-${rel.src}-${rel.dst}-${idx}`}>\n   135→                <td className=\"re-td\">\n   136→                  <span className=\"re-kind-badge\">{getRelKindName(rel.kind)}</span>\n   137→                </td>\n   138→                <td className=\"re-td\">\n   139→                  <span className=\"re-entity-link\">{getEntityName(rel.src)}</span>\n   140→                </td>\n   141→                <td className=\"re-td-arrow\">\n   142→                  <span className=\"re-arrow\">→</span>\n   143→                </td>\n   144→                <td className=\"re-td\">\n   145→                  <span className=\"re-entity-link\">{getEntityName(rel.dst)}</span>\n   146→                </td>\n   147→                <td className=\"re-td\">{rel.strength}</td>\n   148→                <td className=\"re-td-actions\">\n   149→                  <button className=\"re-delete-button\" onClick={() => deleteRelationship(rel)}>\n   150→                    Delete\n   151→                  </button>\n   152→                </td>\n   153→              </tr>\n   154→            ))}\n   155→          </tbody>\n   156→        </table>\n   157→      )}\n   158→\n   159→      {/* Add Relationship Modal */}\n   160→      {showModal && (\n   161→        <div className=\"re-modal\" onClick={() => setShowModal(false)} role=\"button\" tabIndex={0} onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }} >\n   162→          <div className=\"re-modal-content\" onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()} role=\"button\" tabIndex={0} onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }} >\n   163→            <div className=\"re-modal-title\">Add Relationship</div>\n   164→\n   165→            <div className=\"re-form-group\">\n   166→              <label htmlFor=\"relationship-kind\" className=\"re-label\">Relationship Kind</label>\n   167→              <select id=\"relationship-kind\"\n   168→                className=\"re-select\"\n   169→                value={newRel.kind}\n   170→                onChange={(e) => setNewRel({ ...newRel, kind: e.target.value, src: \"\", dst: \"\" })}\n   171→              >\n   172→                <option value=\"\">Select kind...</option>\n   173→                {relationshipKinds.map((k) => (\n   174→                  <option key={k.kind} value={k.kind}>\n   175→                    {k.description || k.kind}\n   176→                  </option>\n   177→                ))}\n   178→              </select>\n   179→            </div>\n   180→\n   181→            <div className=\"re-form-group\">\n   182→              <label htmlFor=\"source-entity\" className=\"re-label\">Source Entity</label>\n   183→              <select id=\"source-entity\"\n   184→                className=\"re-select\"\n   185→                value={newRel.src}\n   186→                onChange={(e) => setNewRel({ ...newRel, src: e.target.value })}\n   187→                disabled={!newRel.kind}\n   188→              >\n   189→                <option value=\"\">Select source...</option>\n   190→                {allowedSrcEntities.map((e) => (\n   191→                  <option key={e.id} value={e.id}>\n   192→                    {e.name} ({e.kind})\n   193→                  </option>\n   194→                ))}\n   195→              </select>\n   196→            </div>\n   197→\n   198→            <div className=\"re-form-group\">\n   199→              <label htmlFor=\"destination-entity\" className=\"re-label\">Destination Entity</label>\n   200→              <select id=\"destination-entity\"\n   201→                className=\"re-select\"\n   202→                value={newRel.dst}\n   203→                onChange={(e) => setNewRel({ ...newRel, dst: e.target.value })}\n   204→                disabled={!newRel.kind}\n   205→              >\n   206→                <option value=\"\">Select destination...</option>\n   207→                {allowedDstEntities\n   208→                  .filter((e) => e.id !== newRel.src)\n   209→                  .map((e) => (\n   210→                    <option key={e.id} value={e.id}>\n   211→                      {e.name} ({e.kind})\n   212→                    </option>\n   213→                  ))}\n   214→              </select>\n   215→            </div>\n   216→\n   217→            <div className=\"re-form-group\">\n   218→              <label className=\"re-label\">Strength (0-1)\n   219→              <NumberInput\n   220→                className=\"re-input\"\n   221→                min={0}\n   222→                max={1}\n   223→                step={0.1}\n   224→                value={newRel.strength}\n   225→                onChange={(v) => setNewRel({ ...newRel, strength: v ?? 0.5 })}\n   226→              />\n   227→              </label>\n   228→            </div>\n   229→\n   230→            <div className=\"re-modal-actions\">\n   231→              <button className=\"re-button\" onClick={() => setShowModal(false)}>\n   232→                Cancel\n   233→              </button>\n   234→              <button className=\"re-add-button\" onClick={addRelationship}>\n   235→                Add Relationship\n   236→              </button>\n   237→            </div>\n   238→          </div>\n   239→        </div>\n   240→      )}\n   241→    </div>\n   242→  );\n   243→}\n   244→\n   245→RelationshipEditor.propTypes = {\n   246→  project: PropTypes.object,\n   247→  onSave: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n   248→};\n   249→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f18789e5-fb86-478f-adf1-eac13368c64f","uuid":"fa35bfe4-8b66-435f-afd1-4706d68b202b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/apps/cosmographer/webui/src/components/RelationshipEditor/index.jsx","content":"/**\n * RelationshipEditor - Create and manage relationships between seed entities.\n */\n\nimport React, { useState } from \"react\";\nimport PropTypes from \"prop-types\";\nimport { NumberInput } from \"@the-canonry/shared-components\";\nimport \"./RelationshipEditor.css\";\n\nexport default function RelationshipEditor({ project, onSave }) {\n  const [showModal, setShowModal] = useState(false);\n  const [filterKind, setFilterKind] = useState(\"\");\n  const [newRel, setNewRel] = useState({ kind: \"\", src: \"\", dst: \"\", strength: 1 });\n\n  const relationships = project?.seedRelationships || [];\n  const entities = project?.seedEntities || [];\n  // Schema v2: relationshipKinds at project root\n  const relationshipKinds = project?.relationshipKinds || [];\n\n  const filteredRels = filterKind\n    ? relationships.filter((r) => r.kind === filterKind)\n    : relationships;\n\n  const updateRelationships = (newRels) => {\n    onSave({ seedRelationships: newRels });\n  };\n\n  const addRelationship = () => {\n    if (!newRel.kind || !newRel.src || !newRel.dst) {\n      alert(\"Please fill all required fields\");\n      return;\n    }\n\n    if (newRel.src === newRel.dst) {\n      alert(\"Source and destination must be different\");\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const rel = {\n      kind: newRel.kind,\n      src: newRel.src,\n      dst: newRel.dst,\n      strength: parseFloat(newRel.strength) || 1,\n    };\n\n    updateRelationships([...relationships, rel]);\n    setShowModal(false);\n    setNewRel({ kind: \"\", src: \"\", dst: \"\", strength: 1 });\n  };\n\n  const deleteRelationship = (rel) => {\n    if (!confirm(\"Delete this relationship?\")) return;\n    updateRelationships(\n      relationships.filter((r) => !(r.kind === rel.kind && r.src === rel.src && r.dst === rel.dst))\n    );\n  };\n\n  const getEntityName = (entityId) => {\n    const entity = entities.find((e) => e.id === entityId);\n    return entity?.name || entityId;\n  };\n\n  const getRelKindName = (kindId) => {\n    const kind = relationshipKinds.find((k) => k.kind === kindId);\n    return kind?.description || kind?.kind || kindId;\n  };\n\n  // Filter entities by allowed source/dest kinds for the selected relationship\n  const selectedRelKind = relationshipKinds.find((k) => k.kind === newRel.kind);\n  const allowedSrcEntities = selectedRelKind?.srcKinds?.length\n    ? entities.filter((e) => selectedRelKind.srcKinds.includes(e.kind))\n    : entities;\n  const allowedDstEntities = selectedRelKind?.dstKinds?.length\n    ? entities.filter((e) => selectedRelKind.dstKinds.includes(e.kind))\n    : entities;\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"re-container\">\n      <div className=\"re-header\">\n        <div className=\"re-title\">Relationships</div>\n        <div className=\"re-subtitle\">Define connections between seed entities.</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"re-toolbar\">\n        <select\n          className=\"re-filter-select\"\n          value={filterKind}\n          onChange={(e) => setFilterKind(e.target.value)}\n        >\n          <option value=\"\">All kinds ({relationships.length})</option>\n          {relationshipKinds.map((k) => (\n            <option key={k.kind} value={k.kind}>\n              {k.description || k.kind} ({relationships.filter((r) => r.kind === k.kind).length})\n            </option>\n          ))}\n        </select>\n        <button\n          className=\"re-add-button\"\n          onClick={() => setShowModal(true)}\n          disabled={entities.length < 2 || relationshipKinds.length === 0}\n        >\n          + Add Relationship\n        </button>\n        {entities.length < 2 && (\n          <span className=\"re-hint\">Need at least 2 entities</span>\n        )}\n        {relationshipKinds.length === 0 && (\n          <span className=\"re-hint\">\n            Define relationship kinds in Schema first\n          </span>\n        )}\n      </div>\n\n      {filteredRels.length === 0 ? (\n        <div className=\"re-empty-state\">\n          {relationships.length === 0\n            ? \"No relationships yet. Create one to connect entities.\"\n            : \"No relationships match the filter.\"}\n        </div>\n      ) : (\n        <table className=\"re-table\">\n          <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th className=\"re-th\">Kind</th>\n              <th className=\"re-th\">Source</th>\n              <th className=\"re-th\"></th>\n              <th className=\"re-th\">Destination</th>\n              <th className=\"re-th\">Strength</th>\n              <th className=\"re-th\"></th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            {filteredRels.map((rel, idx) => (\n              <tr key={`${rel.kind}-${rel.src}-${rel.dst}-${idx}`}>\n                <td className=\"re-td\">\n                  <span className=\"re-kind-badge\">{getRelKindName(rel.kind)}</span>\n                </td>\n                <td className=\"re-td\">\n                  <span className=\"re-entity-link\">{getEntityName(rel.src)}</span>\n                </td>\n                <td className=\"re-td-arrow\">\n                  <span className=\"re-arrow\">→</span>\n                </td>\n                <td className=\"re-td\">\n                  <span className=\"re-entity-link\">{getEntityName(rel.dst)}</span>\n                </td>\n                <td className=\"re-td\">{rel.strength}</td>\n                <td className=\"re-td-actions\">\n                  <button className=\"re-delete-button\" onClick={() => deleteRelationship(rel)}>\n                    Delete\n                  </button>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            ))}\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Add Relationship Modal */}\n      {showModal && (\n        <div className=\"re-modal\" onClick={() => setShowModal(false)} role=\"button\" tabIndex={0} onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }} >\n          <div className=\"re-modal-content\" onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()} role=\"button\" tabIndex={0} onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" || e.key === \" \") e.currentTarget.click(); }} >\n            <div className=\"re-modal-title\">Add Relationship</div>\n\n            <div className=\"re-form-group\">\n              <label htmlFor=\"relationship-kind\" className=\"re-label\">Relationship Kind</label>\n              <select id=\"relationship-kind\"\n                className=\"re-select\"\n                value={newRel.kind}\n                onChange={(e) => setNewRel({ ...newRel, kind: e.target.value, src: \"\", dst: \"\" })}\n              >\n                <option value=\"\">Select kind...</option>\n                {relationshipKinds.map((k) => (\n                  <option key={k.kind} value={k.kind}>\n                    {k.description || k.kind}\n                  </option>\n                ))}\n              </select>\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"re-form-group\">\n              <label htmlFor=\"source-entity\" className=\"re-label\">Source Entity</label>\n              <select id=\"source-entity\"\n                className=\"re-select\"\n                value={newRel.src}\n                onChange={(e) => setNewRel({ ...newRel, src: e.target.value })}\n                disabled={!newRel.kind}\n              >\n                <option value=\"\">Select source...</option>\n                {allowedSrcEntities.map((e) => (\n                  <option key={e.id} value={e.id}>\n                    {e.name} ({e.kind})\n                  </option>\n                ))}\n              </select>\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"re-form-group\">\n              <label htmlFor=\"destination-entity\" className=\"re-label\">Destination Entity</label>\n              <select id=\"destination-entity\"\n                className=\"re-select\"\n                value={newRel.dst}\n                onChange={(e) => setNewRel({ ...newRel, dst: e.target.value })}\n                disabled={!newRel.kind}\n              >\n                <option value=\"\">Select destination...</option>\n                {allowedDstEntities\n                  .filter((e) => e.id !== newRel.src)\n                  .map((e) => (\n                    <option key={e.id} value={e.id}>\n                      {e.name} ({e.kind})\n                    </option>\n                  ))}\n              </select>\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"re-form-group\">\n              <label className=\"re-label\">Strength (0-1)\n              <NumberInput\n                className=\"re-input\"\n                min={0}\n                max={1}\n                step={0.1}\n                value={newRel.strength}\n                onChange={(v) => setNewRel({ ...newRel, strength: v ?? 0.5 })}\n              />\n              </label>\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"re-modal-actions\">\n              <button className=\"re-button\" onClick={() => setShowModal(false)}>\n                Cancel\n              </button>\n              <button className=\"re-add-button\" onClick={addRelationship}>\n                Add Relationship\n              </button>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nRelationshipEditor.propTypes = {\n  project: PropTypes.object,\n  onSave: PropTypes.func.isRequired,\n};\n","numLines":249,"startLine":1,"totalLines":249}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XA46KFuRU7ECmNkdFG5bNA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Both components are in the cosmographer app and share these identical/near-identical CSS patterns:\n\n**Identical patterns (shared):**\n1. Container: `max-width: 1000px`\n2. Header: `margin-bottom`\n3. Title: `font-size`, `font-weight: 600`\n4. Subtitle: `font-size`, `color`\n5. Toolbar: `display: flex`, `margin-bottom: 16px`\n6. Add button: identical styling (`#60a5fa` bg, `#0a1929` color, `8px 16px` padding, etc.)\n\n\n7. Delete button: transparent background with red border and slight rounding\n8. Empty state: centered text display\n9. Modal: fixed positioning with a dark semi-transparent overlay at z-index 1000, dark background color with padding and subtle border-radius\n10. Form elements: labels at 12px with block display, inputs spanning full width with 14px font and rounded borders, consistent spacing between groups\n11. Modal title: bold text with bottom margin\n12. Modal actions: flexbox layout aligned to the right with spacing between buttons, top margin for separation\n13. Hint text: smaller font size\n14. Arrow elements: blue color\n\nNow I'm looking at the component-specific styling patterns for AxisRegistry and RelationshipEditor, which use card-based and table layouts respectively with their own class naming conventions. I'm thinking about consolidating the shared CSS patterns into a single file within the cosmographer app rather than spreading them across components, so I should check what other shared styles already exist in the app.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8316,"cache_read_input_tokens":58669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8316},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f18789e5-fb86-478f-adf1-eac13368c64f","uuid":"e73ea0b4-7808-4525-87ac-7a0e3850e77b"}
