{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DMpi1RCaKAhrZjW1c1TFFN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the full picture. There are 4 editor components in cosmographer, and they all repeat these same CSS patterns. The audit scope is just AxisRegistry and RelationshipEditor, so I'll focus on those two.\n\nLet me identify the truly shared patterns between AxisRegistry.css and RelationshipEditor.css:\n\n**Identical or near-identical:**\n1. Container: `max-width: 1000px` (both use the same value)\n2. Header: `margin-bottom` (16px vs 24px - different)\n3. Title: both have title, but different sizes/colors\n\n\n4. Subtitle styling varies between the two\n5. Toolbar uses the same flex layout and 16px margin spacing in both\n6. The add button shares identical styling across padding, font size, blue background, dark text, and border radius\n7. Delete buttons are nearly identical with transparent backgrounds and red styling, though the exact red shade differs slightly between them\n8. Empty state messaging uses consistent font sizing and center alignment\n9. Modal overlay is identical with fixed positioning, dark semi-transparent background, and centered flex layout\n10. Modal content boxes are nearly the same with dark backgrounds and blue-tinted borders, but differ in width—one is 440px and the other 500px\n11. Modal titles follow the same font weight and spacing pattern\n12. Form groups have minor spacing variations between the two versions\n13. Labels maintain consistent small font sizes and block display\n14. Input fields are nearly identical in width and border styling, though background colors differ slightly\n15. Modal action buttons use the same flex layout with consistent spacing\n16. Hint text styling is nearly identical across both\n17. Arrow icons share the same blue color\n\nThe two CSS files are so similar that consolidating them into a single shared stylesheet would eliminate duplication while preserving the few differences through CSS variables or minor overrides. I'm realizing that changing class names across both components would require updating JSX too, which is a lot of work for minimal benefit. Instead, I should create a shared CSS file with generic cosmographer-editor class names for the common patterns, then have each component import it and override with their own prefixed classes where needed.\n\nDefining the shared class names... Now I'm organizing the implementation — I'll create a shared stylesheet with these class definitions, then update the CSS files for both components and sync the JSX files to use the standardized class names.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4922,"cache_read_input_tokens":67824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4922},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f18789e5-fb86-478f-adf1-eac13368c64f","uuid":"2d555799-b1de-47ee-aa85-a8431c946b08"}
