{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0153DRiQn5TPjs3znVtU89Yt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the ESLint config structure. The project uses a `localPlugin` object to bundle all custom rules, then references them as `local/rule-name`. Let me create the ESLint rule.\n\nThe enforceable pattern: detect inline switch statements that handle keyboard navigation (ArrowDown, ArrowUp, Enter, Escape) as case clauses. This is the pattern that should use `useKeyboardNavigation` instead.\n\nI'll write a custom rule that looks for SwitchStatement nodes where case clauses include string literals for at least 3 of the 4 keys (ArrowDown, ArrowUp, Enter, Escape) - this is a strong signal of duplicated keyboard navigation logic.\n\n\nI should exclude this rule from the shared-components directory since that's where the hook is defined.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3967,"cache_read_input_tokens":70788,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3967},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b581011f-7823-4110-9748-054ecf96699a","uuid":"713cf9ed-ef39-49c9-834c-b6f0d7cff0bd"}
