{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hqz2MXHLxDehqcTAQJSxxz","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've read the ESLint configuration. Here's a summary of the current setup:\n\n## Current ESLint Setup and Drift-Guard Rule Integration\n\n### Architecture Overview\n\nThe configuration uses a **plugin-based approach** with local custom rules:\n\n1. **Local Plugin Definition** (lines 37-65):\n   - All drift-guard rules are imported at the top (lines 11-35)\n   - They're registered in the `localPlugin` object with a `rules` property\n   - The plugin is namespaced as `local:` when referenced\n\n2. **Rule Configurations** (lines 67-252):\n   - Base JS rules with complexity limits (lines 87-99)\n   - TypeScript with type-checked rules (lines 101-112)\n   - **Three main rule scopes**:\n     - **Library code** (lines 121-143): Backend TypeScript, minimal rules\n     - **Frontend code** (lines 146-215): React + accessibility, **all drift-guard rules enabled as warnings**\n     - **Vite config** (lines 218-226): Only `no-cross-app-alias` rule\n\n### Drift-Guard Rules Currently Wired In\n\nAll 20 drift-guard rules are enabled in the **Frontend scope** (lines 196-213) as warnings:\n- `no-viz-overlay-drift`\n- `no-remote-shell-drift`\n- `no-bulk-shell-drift`\n- `no-panel-css-duplication`\n- `no-viewer-pattern-drift`\n- `no-hint-css-duplication`\n- `no-archivist-section-drift`\n- `no-version-toolbar-drift`\n- `no-dashboard-section-drift`\n- `no-schema-editor-css-drift`\n- `no-app-css-base-duplication`\n- `no-matrix-css-duplication`\n- `no-toggle-css-drift`\n- `no-viz-utility-drift`\n- `no-cosmo-editor-drift`\n- `no-inline-keyboard-nav`\n- `no-error-boundary-without-base`\n- `no-non-vitest-testing`\n\n### Key Integration Points\n\n- **Import location**: `/home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/eslint-rules/`\n- **Plugin namespace**: All rules referenced as `local/<rule-name>`\n- **Severity**: All warnings (won't block CI, show in e