{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111XdCxDjjpGkqNxAzkSQZg","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me provide you with a comprehensive summary:\n\n## TypeScript Config Status Across WebUI Directories\n\n### Apps WITH Complete tsconfig Setup (tsconfig.json + tsconfig.app.json + tsconfig.node.json)\n\n1. **apps/archivist/webui/** ✓\n2. **apps/chronicler/webui/** ✓\n3. **apps/illuminator/webui/** ✓\n4. **apps/lore-weave/webui/** ✓\n5. **apps/viewer/webui/** ✓\n\n### Apps WITHOUT TypeScript Config Files\n\n1. **apps/canonry/webui/** ✗\n2. **apps/coherence-engine/webui/** ✗\n3. **apps/name-forge/webui/** ✗\n4. **apps/cosmographer/webui/** ✗\n\n---\n\n## Canonical Pattern Reference\n\nThe established pattern (used in archivist, chronicler, illuminator, lore-weave, and viewer) consists of **three files**:\n\n### 1. **tsconfig.json** (Root/Base Config)\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"rootDir\": \".\"\n  },\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"references\": [\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.app.json\" },\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.node.json\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\nActs as a composite configuration that references the app and node configs.\n\n### 2. **tsconfig.app.json** (Application Code)\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"tsBuildInfoFile\": \"./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.app.tsbuildinfo\",\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": true,\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\"],\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"verbatimModuleSyntax\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noUnusedLocals\": true,\n    \"noUnusedParameters\": true,\n    \"erasableSyntaxOnly\": true,\n    \"noFallthroughCasesInSwitch\": true,\n    \"noUncheckedSideEffectImports\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src\"]\n}\n```\n\n### 3. **tsconfig.node.json** (Build Configuration)\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"tsBuildInfoFile\": \"./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.node.tsbuildinfo\",\n    \"target\": \"ES2023\",\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2023\"],\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"node\"],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"verbatimModuleSyntax\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noUnusedLocals\": true,\n    \"noUnusedParameters\": true,\n    \"erasableSyntaxOnly\": true,\n    \"noFallthroughCasesInSwitch\": true,\n    \"noUncheckedSideEffectImports\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"vite.config.ts\"]\n}\n```\n\n**Key Differences:**\n- `tsconfig.app.json`: ES2022 target, includes DOM libs, jsx: \"react-jsx\", includes `src/`\n- `tsconfig.node.json`: ES2023 target, only Node libs, no JSX, includes `vite.config.ts`\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**5 apps have the complete setup** (archivist, chronicler, illuminator, lore-weave, viewer)\n\n**4 apps are missing TypeScript configs entirely** (canonry, coherence-engine, name-forge, cosmographer)\n\nThe canonical pattern uses a three-file composite structure with separate configurations for application code (ES2022 + React/DOM) and build tooling (ES2023 + Node)."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acdd6410fe5656d7d (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 33806\ntool_uses: 9\nduration_ms: 12343</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e54c7e2e-0d44-4856-a582-afde6e85abbc","uuid":"6457501b-2f3e-4e50-88c6-5ea29fd8e5b1","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Check which webui directories have tsconfig.json files and which don't. Look in:\n- apps/canonry/webui/ \n- apps/coherence-engine/webui/\n- apps/name-forge/webui/\n- apps/cosmographer/webui/\n- apps/lore-