{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Convert these shared-components files from JavaScript with PropTypes to TypeScript with interfaces. For each file:\n1. Read the current file\n2. Remove `import PropTypes from 'prop-types'`\n3. Add a TypeScript interface for props based on the PropTypes definition\n4. Remove the `.propTypes = { ... }` block at the end\n5. Add `import type { ReactNode }` from React where needed (for `PropTypes.node`)\n6. Keep ALL existing logic, JSDoc comments, and behavior\n7. Write the converted file back\n\nFiles to convert (all in /home/tsonu/src/the-canonry/packages/shared-components/src/):\n- components/ModalShell.tsx\n- components/FormGroup.tsx\n- components/EmptyState.tsx\n- components/ErrorBoundary.tsx\n- components/ErrorMessage.tsx\n- components/EnableToggle.tsx\n- components/IconButton.tsx\n- components/InfoBox.tsx\n\nFor ErrorBoundary.tsx, note it's a class component — use generic class typing: `class ErrorBoundary extends React.Component<ErrorBoundaryProps, ErrorBoundaryState>`.\n\nIMPORTANT: Use the Edit tool, not Write. Remove PropTypes import AND the .propTypes block. Keep `import React` (not `import type React`). For `ReactNode`, use `React.ReactNode` — don't add a separate import. TypeScript interfaces go above the component function.\n\nExample conversion pattern:\nBEFORE:\n```jsx\nimport React from 'react';\nimport PropTypes from 'prop-types';\n\nexport function Foo({ title, children, className = '' }) {\n  return <div>{children}</div>;\n}\n\nFoo.propTypes = {\n  title: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\n  children: PropTypes.node,\n  className: PropTypes.string,\n};\n```\n\nAFTER:\n```tsx\nimport React from 'react';\n\ninterface FooProps {\n  title: string;\n  children?: React.ReactNode;\n  className?: string;\n}\n\nexport function Foo({ title, children, className = '' }: FooProps) {\n  return <div>{children}</div>;\n}\n```\n\nNote: Props with `.isRequired` become required (no `?`). Props without `.isRequired` become optional (`?`).\nNote: Keep `export default` statements if they exist, just remove the propTypes block.\nNote: For the ErrorBoundary, also add state interface."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MSjwERvzq8tWa6PqUQiEqU","session_id":"e54c7e2e-0d44-4856-a582-afde6e85abbc","uuid":"3f677e25-b7f0-4b92-931f-3d218946df05"}
